[8746]={"DISASTER has struck!  Metzen the Reindeer has been kidnapped!$B$BMetzen is one of Great-father Winter's eight reindeer - and property of Smokywood Pastures.  We've received not one but TWO ransom letters from groups claiming to have Metzen.  With the holiday season well under way, we're strapped to the coin box here!  Please - find Metzen and return him to us!$B$BCheck out the ransom letters for clues, and sprinkle this reindeer dust on him - it will free him from any of his bonds!$B$BPlease, hurry!","Find Metzen the Reindeer.  Use the notes provided to you for clues as to where he is being held.$B$BWhen you find Metzen, have the Pouch of Reindeer Dust in your possession so you can sprinkle some of the dust on him; this should free Metzen from his bonds of captivity.$B$BReturn the Pouch of Reindeer Dust to Kaymard Copperpinch in Orgrimmar once Metzen is freed.",4},
[8767]={nil,nil,0},
[8768]={nil,nil,0},
[8769]={nil,nil,0},
[8793]={"Hello, I'm glad that you've decided to hear me out. The Horde needs all of the help that it can get to prepare for the Ahn'Qiraj War, and that means that we need you! Even now as we speak, official collectors are gathering the necessary material needed for the upcoming war, but we won't be able to meet our goals without your assistance, $n!$B$BYou should go speak with the guy in charge, Warlord Gorchuk. What do you say, $c? Will you help out with the vital preparations?","Speak with Warlord Gorchuk in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits.",1},
[8794]={"Hello, I'm glad that you've decided to hear me out. The Horde needs all of the help that it can get to prepare for the Ahn'Qiraj War, and that means that we need you! Even now as we speak, official collectors are gathering the necessary material needed for the upcoming war, but we won't be able to meet our goals without your assistance, $n!$B$BYou should go speak with the guy in charge, Warlord Gorchuk. What do you say, $c? Will you help out with the vital preparations?","Speak with Warlord Gorchuk in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits.",1},
[8795]={"Hello, I'm glad that you've decided to hear me out. The Alliance needs all of the help that it can get to prepare for the Ahn'Qiraj War, and that means that we need you! Even now as we speak, official collectors are gathering the necessary material needed for the upcoming war, but we won't be able to meet our goals without your assistance, $n!$B$BYou should go speak with the guy in charge, Field Marshal Snowfall. What do you say, $c? Will you help out with the vital preparations?","Speak with Field Marshal Snowfall in Ironforge's Military Ward.",1},
[8796]={"Hello, I'm glad that you've decided to hear me out. The Alliance needs all of the help that it can get to prepare for the Ahn'Qiraj War, and that means that we need you! Even now as we speak, official collectors are gathering the necessary material needed for the upcoming war, but we won't be able to meet our goals without your assistance, $n!$B$BYou should go speak with the guy in charge, Field Marshal Snowfall. What do you say, $c? Will you help out with the vital preparations?","Speak with Field Marshal Snowfall in Ironforge's Military Ward.",1},
[8798]={nil,nil,0},
[8857]={"I'm looking for battle hardened adventurers willing and able to get a fresh husk sample from the fallen Colossus of Ashi to Oglethorpe in Booty Bay. No, no, I wouldn't want you to go anywhere near that thing's corpse. Just take one of my samples and make it snappy. These things are no good to him rotten!","Take the Colossus of Ashi's Husk to Oglethorpe Obnoticus in Booty Bay.",7},
[8858]={"There ain't nothin' I'd like more than to stuff this bug husk down Oilfist's fat face... Cept, I'm stuck here collectin' samples from that overgrown cockroach. I'll be here 'till the wee mornin' hours given the size o' that thing.$B$BTake this here sample to Oilfist fer me and do it fast, $c. He's payin' BIG!$B$BYar, Thorium Point - it be in the Searin' Gorge.","Take the Colossus of Regal's Husk to Overseer Oilfist in Searing Gorge.",7},
[8859]={"My servants were nearly killed in their efforts to recover this sample. You absolutely must hurry! Lord Maxwell Tyrosus eagerly awaits a fresh husk sample. He believes that the secrets of this Colossus could help us in the war against the Scourge!$B$BWhy are you still here!? To Light's Hope! Yes, you will be rewarded handsomely for your efforts...","Take the Colossus of Zora's Husk to Lord Maxwell Tyrosus at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.",7},
[8867]={"Every year the druids of Moonglade hold a celebration of our city's great triumph over an ancient evil.$B$BWe celebrate the wisdom of our elders, share in magnificent feasts and of course... shoot fireworks!$B$BFor a small donation you can purchase colorful rockets from our vendor.  Try using some of the launchers around here, $n.","Launch 8 Lunar Fireworks and 2 Cluster Fireworks and return to a Lunar Festival Harbinger at any capital city.",0},
[8868]={"The beast Omen was once a hero of this world.  A wolf of great strength and fortune, Omen fought beside the heroes of the War of the Ancients until he succumbed to demonic magics.  Turning against his allies, he raged across Azeroth and carried death and terror in his wake.$B$BFinally defeated here, in Moonglade, Omen now sleeps among the silt of Lake Elune'ara.  But each new year, during the festival, he stirs...$B$BGather cohorts, $n, and summon and defeat the beast Omen.  Earn the blessing of Elune!","Summon Omen, defeat him and gain Elune's Blessing.  Return to Valadar Starsong in Nighthaven",5},
[8871]={"It's that time of the year, $n!  The Cenarion Circle invites all denizens of Azeroth to partake in our celebration of the Lunar Festival.  You will find the Lunar Festival Harbinger in this very city at a location marked by a blessed circle of moonlight.  She can tell you more about the holiday.","Talk to the Lunar Festival Harbinger in the Park District in Stormwind.  You can also talk to Lunar Festival Harbingers in other capital cities.",0},
[8872]={"It's that time of the year, $n!  The Cenarion Circle invites all denizens of Azeroth to partake in our celebration of the Lunar Festival.  You will find the Lunar Festival Harbinger in this very city at a location marked by a blessed circle of moonlight.  She can tell you more about the holiday.","Talk to the Lunar Festival Harbinger at the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus.  You can also talk to Lunar Festival Harbingers in other capital cities.",0},
[8873]={"It's that time of the year, $n!  The Cenarion Circle invites all denizens of Azeroth to partake in our celebration of the Lunar Festival.  You will find the Lunar Festival Harbinger in this very city at a location marked by a blessed circle of moonlight.  She can tell you more about the holiday.","Talk to the Lunar Festival Harbinger in the Valley of Wisdom in Orgrimmar.  You can also talk to Lunar Festival Harbingers in other capital cities.",0},
[8874]={"It's that time of the year, $n!  The Cenarion Circle invites all denizens of Azeroth to partake in our celebration of the Lunar Festival.  You will find the Lunar Festival Harbinger in this very city at a location marked by a blessed circle of moonlight.  She can tell you more about the holiday.","Talk to the Lunar Festival Harbinger in the entrance to the Undercity.  You can also talk to Lunar Festival Harbingers in other capital cities.",0},
[8875]={"It's that time of the year, $n!  The Cenarion Circle invites all denizens of Azeroth to partake in our celebration of the Lunar Festival.  You will find the Lunar Festival Harbinger in this very city at a location marked by a blessed circle of moonlight.  She can tell you more about the holiday.","Talk to the Lunar Festival Harbinger at the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff.  You can also talk to Lunar Festival Harbingers in other capital cities.",0},
[8899]={"How to describe her beauty? Thousands of years of words and I am at a loss.$b$bThese mortals confound the mind and leave us babbling fools.$b$bI've stared at these words too long. No more eloquent meaning can I squeeze from them. No, she must have it now, or some other suitor will surely steal her eye.","Deliver the Immaculate Letter to Colara Dean outside the bank in Stormwind.",0},
[8902]={"A lifetime ago, I was betrothed to marry Elenia, my childhood sweetheart. It's been years since I thought about her last, but of late, she frequently occupies my thoughts.$b$bPerhaps, even with everything that has passed, there can be some room in each other's lives for our love.$b$bI'm sure she has changed, also. Can you deliver this letter to her for me? I am too nervous to give it in person.","Deliver the Lovingly Composed Letter to Elenia Haydon near the bank in the Undercity.",0},
[8910]={"Well met, $c.  I've something that might interest you.$B$BI have in my possession a set of armor much like the one worn by those of your profession, but of much higher quality.  I'd be willing to trade the bracers for ordinary ones in exchange for a small favor.$B$BThe blood of the frostsabers and bears that inhabit Winterspring has properties I'm in need of at the moment.  Bring me a sizeable sample of it along with the bracers and a small amount of gold.  You shall find the effort worth your while.","Acquire 15 Winterspring Blood Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Shadowcraft Bracers to Deliana in Ironforge.",5},
[8912]={"Well met, $c.  I've something that might interest you.$B$BI have in my possession a set of armor much like the one worn by those of your profession, but of much higher quality.  I'd be willing to trade the bracers for ordinary ones in exchange for a small favor.$B$BThe blood of the frostsabers and bears that inhabit Winterspring has properties I'm in need of at the moment.  Bring me a sizeable sample of it along with the bracers and a small amount of gold.  You shall find the effort worth your while.","Acquire 15 Winterspring Blood Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Bracers of Valor to Deliana in Ironforge.",5},
[8920]={"Hail, $c!  I can tell by your demeanor that you've seen and done much in this world.  Yet I'm willing to wager you haven't seen a piece of armor like this.$B$BPerform a small favor for me and I'll be willing to trade it to you for an ordinary set of bracers.$B$BI'm in need of a sizeable sample of venom drawn from the spiders and scorpions that inhabit Silithus.  Bring this to me along with a few gold coins and I'll perform the exchange.","Acquire 15 Silithus Venom Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Bracers of Valor to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.",5},
[8921]={"Ah, you're in need of my latest project... the extra-dimensional ghost revealer!  Unfortunately I've run out of funds and manpower.$B$BYou're willing to help?  Excellent!  Our first task is to build a device to harvest the very fabric of death!  Building an ectoplasmic distiller won't be an easy task, $n.$B$BI'll need you to bring me an arcanite converter, some greater eternal essences and stonescale oil. I'll also need some volcanic ash from the lava pools in the Burning Steppes to build a filter.","Return to Mux Manascrambler in Gadgetzan with 1 Delicate Arcanite Converter, 4 Greater Eternal Essence, 10 Stonescale Oil, 25 Volcanic Ash and 40 gold.",5},
[8922]={"I must find a way to speak with Anthion Harmon... or more specifically, his ghost!$B$BI know of an engineer with a queer interest in the supernatural.  He claims he can build a machine that allows him to speak with the dead!$B$BThe blood you collected was intended for him; travel to Gadgetzan and bring it to him as payment for his services!","Bring the Sealed Blood Container to Mux Manascrambler inside Gadgetzan in Tanaris.",5},
[8923]={"You must be quite brave to have stuck around after that.  That or I've piqued your interest with the piece of armor I gave you.  There is more from where that came from, if you're still interested in aiding me.$B$BThe venom samples you collected are for an acquaintance of mine, Mux Manascrambler, an engineer with an interest in the supernatural.  His latest project consists of a device that allows you to communicate with the dead!  My last hope is to contact Anthion and find out more about my situation.","Take the Sealed Venom Container to Mux Manascrambler in Gadgetzan.",5},
[8924]={"A fine piece of engineering, if I do say so myself!  You will need to travel a bit, I'm afraid, in order to find the incorporeal undead we require.$B$BYou see, different climates lend different consistencies to the spectral fabric of the dead.  The tortured night elves of Silithus, the spirits of the highborne from Winterspring and the ghosts and banshees of the Eastern Plaguelands should give us the different types of ectoplasm we need.  Be sure to place the distiller nearby before you harvest them!","Use the Ectoplasmic Distiller near incorporeal undead to collect 12 Scorched Ectoplasms in Silithus, 12 Frozen Ectoplasms in Winterspring and 12 Stable Ectoplasms in the Eastern Plaguelands.  Bring them along with the Ectoplasmic Distiller back to Mux Manascrambler in Gadgetzan.",5},
[8928]={"The core will provide us with enough juice to power our device; now we just have to build a rod that can channel that energy without melting.$B$BI met an imp in Winterspring that sold all manner of exotic goods.  He had an elemental rod that would do perfectly.  I'm kicking myself in the head right now for not having bought it.$B$BHe lives inside a cave in the entrance to Darkwhisper Gorge.  Sneak in there and try to find him.$B$BMake sure he only charges you forty gold; that's the price he quoted me!","Search for an imp inside a cave at the entrance of Darkwhisper Gorge in southern Winterspring, purchase a Fel Elemental Rod and return to Mux Manascrambler in Gadgetzan.",3},
[8929]={"Well, nothing left for us to do but try out the goblin's invention.  Word has it that Anthion was mowed down by the undead legions of Stratholme as he tried to enter its gates.$B$BTry using the device there and find out whatever Anthion knew.","Use the Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer at the entrance to Stratholme and speak with the ghost of Anthion Harmon.",5},
[8945]={"I'll provide you the information you ask for, $n.  But more pressing matters are at hand.$B$BMy beloved wife has been taken prisoner by Rivendare's undead scum.$B$BI strongly objected to her joining the Argent Dawn's foolish crusade, yet that's not of importance anymore.  You must finish what I attempted to do, you must rescue Ysida from the clutches of the Baron!","Go into Stratholme and rescue Ysida Harmon from Baron Rivendare.",6},
[8946]={"It is the cruelest of fates that my beloved has perished while trying to rescue me.  Yet, you claim to possess the ability to converse with him.$B$BBring him this locket as proof that I am well.  He must not linger in this world; my heart would not be able to bear it.$B$BFarewell, $n.  I shall be in your debt always.","Bring Ysida's Locket to Anthion Harmon in Eastern Plaguelands.",5},
[8948]={"Theldren is not one to willingly participate in a fair fight.  I've shaped this banner to display his family colors.$B$BWith some additional sorcery, this banner shall provoke him in a way he won't be able to resist.$B$BAn old acquaintance of mine named Falrin knows the exact procedure required.  He has a particular way of... aggravating people.  You shall find him at the library in Dire Maul.","Take the incomplete Banner of Provocation to Falrin Treeshaper at the library in Dire Maul.",5},
[8949]={"Yes, it is true that I am familiar with this enchantment you require, $c.  Yet I'm not one to give out favors freely, even if you were sent here by an old friend.$B$BI hold nothing but hatred and contempt for our brutish ogre neighbors.  And not only them, I hate the followers of Omokk just as much as I hate those that follow King Gordok.$B$BI want you to kill them.  Kill lots of them!  Bring me the beads they carry around their neck as proof of your work.  Do this and we shall talk about your request.","Collect 25 Ogre Warbeads from Ogres inside Dire Maul or Blackrock Spire and return to Falrin Treeshaper inside the Athenaeum in Dire Maul.",5},
[8961]={"In order to summon Lord Valthalak we're first going to need to gather the other two-thirds of the amulet. To do that we need to get a brazier and some special coals to burn in it.$B$BThere are three nobles of fire, Lord Incedius in Blackrock Depths, Pyroguard Emberseer in Blackrock Spire and Executor Asharell in the Steppes, with what we need. Collect from each a piece of their remains, and then return to me with a Hallowed Brazier, which can be purchased from the Argent Dawn if you are honored by them.","Gather the Incendicite of Incendius, the Ember of Emberseer and the Ash of Asharell, along with a Hallowed Brazier, and return them to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain.",5},
[8963]={"$C, listen closely. Now that we have the brazier, and the means to light it, we still need another component to suffuse it with; something that will provide a focus strong enough to entice the spirit of my deceased, former comrade.$B$BIsalien, our priestess, grew up in Winterspring at Starbreeze Village. I need you to gather a Starbreeze Village Relic from the Frostmaul giants of Frostwhisper Gorge in southern Winterspring, who are known for raiding to the north from time to time.","Acquire a Starbreeze Village Relic and return it to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain.",5},
[8970]={"As I was saying, $c, in my living years I flirted with becoming a diviner. But, there really wasn't as much profit in it as you might imagine, mostly because it's dangerous and the reagents are rare and expensive. However, I do know enough to be able to pinpoint the final piece of the amulet, and the spirit of my former comrade along with it.$B$BThis is where you come in, $n. I need you to go to Alcaz Island off the coast of Dustwallow Marsh and collect Bloodkelp from the Strashaz naga that live there.","Gather 20 Bloodkelp from the Strashaz naga and then return to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain.",5},
[8973]={nil,nil,0},
[8977]={"It's been great working with you, $n.  Here is the finished product.$B$BI hope it helps you in your current endeavors.  And hey, if you don't mind, help spread the word.  I wouldn't mind having more customers!","Bring the Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer  to Deliana in Ironforge.",5},
[8978]={"It's been great working with you, $n.  Here is the finished product.$B$BI hope it helps you in your current endeavors.  And hey, if you don't mind, help spread the word.  I wouldn't mind having more customers!","Return to Mokvar in Orgrimmar with the Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer.",5},
[8985]={"$C, listen closely. Now that we have the location of the last amulet piece, we still need another component to suffuse the brazier with; something that will provide a focus strong enough to entice the spirit of my deceased, former comrade.$B$BIsalien, our priestess, grew up in Winterspring at Starbreeze Village. I need you to gather a Starbreeze Village Relic from the Frostmaul giants of Frostwhisper Gorge in southern Winterspring, who are known for raiding to the north from time to time.","Acquire a Starbreeze Village Relic and return it to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain.",5},
[8995]={"All is now ready, $n.$B$BWhen alive, Lord Valthalak used to inhabit what is now The Beast's chamber. Go there and use the Brazier of Beckoning to summon forth Lord Valthalak. It will reincorporate him, so he'll have to be killed again. I'd take care of The Beast first, and be sure take enough friends along to survive the upper portion of Blackrock Spire.$B$BOnce you've dispatched Valthalak, use the amulet on his corpse. With his spirit reunified, he'll likely want his amulet back, as well.$B$BGood luck!","Use the Brazier of Beckoning to summon Lord Valthalak. Dispatch him, and use Lord Valthalak's Amulet on the corpse. Then, return Lord Valthalak's Amulet to the Spirit of Lord Valthalak.",7},
[8996]={"I will ignore your impertinence this time, $c, because you have done a noble thing today; returning the rest of my stolen spirit to me. Despite your obviously weak nature, $r, you have shown courage where those that stole from me did not, and probably never could!$B$BReturn to them, before I change my mind and slay you where you stand. Go back and tell them that they are safe... for now.","Return to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain and give him the Brazier of Beckoning.",1},
[8997]={"I suppose that this is goodbye then, my friend. But, I'll always be here if you want to come back and talk with me from time to time. Probably while you're loitering around waiting for your buddies to join you for a raid on Blackrock Spire.$B$BGo, before I start to cry. Go back to Deliana in Ironforge and tell her what's happened.","Speak with Deliana at The High Seat in Ironforge.",1},
[9052]={"I would ask you to help me create a toxin of sorts, to pacify a great creature living here in the crater.  It is not deadly, and only the keen eyes of a $c can hope to collect the ingredients.$b$bYou can find the bloodcap mushrooms growing within the bloodpetal sprouts all across the crater.  Gorishi stings are from the giant flying wasps inside and around the Slithering Scar, located in the southern part of the crater.","Collect 8 Bloodcap and 8 Gorishi Stings, and return to Torwa Pathfinder in Un'Goro Crater.",5},
[9053]={"It is as I feared -- the toxin is simply too weak for such a powerful creature.$b$bIf we are to create a toxin of high enough potency, you must venture to the bottom of the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, unlock the secrets of the altar and recover a putrid vine from the guardian there.  The temple is dangerous, and it would behoove you to bring friends.$b$bReturn to me when this is done.","Retrieve a Putrid Vine from the guardian at the bottom of the Sunken Temple and return to Torwa Pathfinder.",6},
[9065]={"$Tpunk;!  Kill Kobold Vermin, 2 of em.","Kill Kobold Vermin, 2 of em.",7},
[9085]={"After you bring down the defenses of the Scourge summoning circles that have appeared in the zones under attack, you will be able to confront the acolytes who protect them.$b$bIn truth, these are not men. They are shadows, some of the Lich King's most frightening creatures. They can be revealed using the necrotic runes they carry, and then destroyed with magic or strength of arms.","Go to a summoning circle and kill a Shadow of Doom, then return to Commander Thomas Helleran at Light's Hope Chapel in Eastern Plaguelands.",0},
[9121]={"In the thick of Plaguewood lies the entrance to the dread citadel of Naxxramas. Previously, all attempts to enter had been stymied by the magical wards placed upon the rune portal. That is, until now.$B$BWe have devised a way to gain entry via arcane cloaking - an old cantrip of the Kirin Tor with a few modifications of my own. Since your dedication to the cause of the Dawn is somewhat lacking, $n, the price will be high. You may decline and choose to return when you are revered or exalted for a discount.","Archmage Angela Dosantos at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 5 Arcane Crystals, 2 Nexus Crystals, 1 Righteous Orb and 60 gold pieces. You must also be Honored with the Argent Dawn.",0},
[9131]={"Have you ever seen Dreadnaught armor, $c? No, of course you haven't. You're still a $g boy:girl; - a tyke. Let me tell you, it is glorious.$B$BYou're probably asking yourself what any of this has to do with you, right? I'll tell you what, scrub; I need Dark Iron scraps and I'm willing to pay to get my hands on as many as possible.$B$BI need the scraps to put together sets of Dreadnaught for our champions. Bring me scraps and get paid.","Korfax at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 30 Dark Iron Scraps.",5},
[9247]={"$n,$B$BIn times past you have served the interests of the Argent Dawn, always to the best of your abilities. Now, once again, we sound the clarion call in our time of greatest need.$B$B$n, please report to the Keeper of the Rolls at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands if you are willing to aid us once more.","Take the Letter from the Keeper of the Rolls to him at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.",1},
[9260]={"The Scourge is camped upon our very doorstep; we cannot remain idle! Surely you will step up to defend Stormwind from these accursed invaders? $b $bThere are strange runic circles outside, glowing with the same energy that surrounds the undead and the Necropolis above. They have significance, I'm certain, and I want you to find out what. Thin the numbers of those aberrations while you're at it; bring me proof of their death along with your results, and I will reward you.  Go!","Collect three Dim Necrotic Stones from the Scourge outside Stormwind and investigate the glowing runic circles nearby their encampment.",4},
[9261]={"The Scourge is camped upon our very doorstep; we cannot remain idle! Surely you will step up to defend Ironforge from these accursed invaders? $b $bThere are strange runic circles outside, glowing with the same energy that surrounds the undead and the Necropolis above. They have significance, I'm certain, and I want you to find out what. Thin the numbers of those aberrations while you're at it; bring me proof of their death along with your results, and I will reward you.  Go!","Collect three Dim Necrotic Stones from the Scourge outside Ironforge and investigate the glowing runic circles nearby their encampment.",4},
[9262]={"The Scourge is camped upon our very doorstep; we cannot remain idle! Surely you will step up to defend Darnassus from these accursed invaders? $b $bThere are strange runic circles outside, glowing with the same energy that surrounds the undead and the Necropolis above. They have significance, I'm certain, and I want you to find out what. Thin the numbers of those aberrations while you're at it; bring me proof of their death along with your results, and I will reward you.  Go!","Collect three Dim Necrotic Stones from the Scourge outside Darnassus and investigate the glowing runic circles nearby their encampment.",4},
[9265]={"The Scourge is camped upon our very doorstep; we cannot remain idle! Surely you will step up to defend the Undercity from these accursed invaders? $b $bThere are strange runic circles outside, glowing with the same energy that surrounds the undead and the Necropolis above. They have significance, I'm certain, and I want you to find out what. Thin the numbers of those aberrations while you're at it; bring me proof of their death along with your results, and I will reward you.  Go!","Collect three Dim Necrotic Stones from the Scourge outside the Undercity and investigate the glowing runic circles nearby their encampment.",4},
[9292]={"On the corpse of the fallen abomination, you discover a cracked crystal, slowly pulsing with necrotic energy.","Bring the Cracked Necrotic Crystal to Lieutenant Orrin outside the gates of Stormwind.",0},
[9295]={"You found this letter on one of the many Scourge minions you've slain. From its appearance and smell, it has been with the undead for some time. Perhaps someone at Light's Hope Chapel would be interested in examining it further...","Take the Torn Letter to the Keeper of the Rolls at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.",3},
[9310]={"On the corpse of the fallen wight, you find a crystal that is faintly radiating necrotic energy.","Bring the Faint Necrotic Crystal to Lieutenant Rukag in the courtyard of the Undercity.",0},
[9322]={"The Midsummer Fire Festival is celebrated everywhere in Azeroth, and the diverse land of Kalimdor is no exception. You look fit to travel -- perhaps a journey is in order.$b$bMidsummer cannot be truly appreciated unless you've seen the blistering blue fires abroad. The celebrants have lit fires in chilly western Winterspring, northeastern Azshara, near Valor's Rest in the wastes of Silithus, and by the entrance to lush Un'Goro. Return once your journey is complete.","Visit the Midsummer camps located in Azshara, Silithus, Un'Goro Crater, and Winterspring, then return to the Festival Flamekeeper.",3},
[9388]={"There are many flames burning throughout the world today, $n. The trickiest fires to tend are those that burn green; they do not stay lit long without supervision. Make certain the emerald fires still burn on Kalimdor for our Flamekeeper, eh?$b$bYou will find them near Ratchet in the Barrens, close to the Master's Glaive in Darkshore, in the forest of Ashenvale by the bridge near Silverwing Outpost, and near the road to Windshear Crag along the main road in Stonetalon Mountains.","Visit the bonfires within Ashenvale, the Barrens, Darkshore, and Stonetalon Mountains, then speak with the Festival Flamekeeper.",4},
[9389]={"The Midsummer Fire Festival traditionally lights up the land with a myriad of flames. Some argue that the green fires are the finest, as they are the hardest to maintain and have such a distinctive hue.$b$bMake sure they still burn in the Eastern Kingdoms for our Flamekeeper. They sit near Dun Modr in the Wetlands, close to Pyrewood Village within Silverpine Forest, on the cliffs overlooking the lighthouse in Westfall, and by the ruined tower in Hillsbrad Foothills.","Visit the bonfires within Hillsbrad Foothills, Silverpine Forest, Westfall, and the Wetlands, then speak with the Festival Flamekeeper.",4},
[9411]={nil,nil,0},
[9422]={"For some time now, we have been tapping the crystal resources of the Silithus desert. The only dangers we faced were from the creatures that made this place their home and the oppressive sand and dust and heat.$b$bBut now the Alliance seems to have caught on to what we have found here. It is now a race between us to capture the natural resources, and keep them from the other.$b$bI need every set of hands that is available. I hope I have yours.","Find and deliver Silithyst to the Silithyst Extractor then speak with General Kirika at the Horde encampment near Hive'Regal.",5},
[60866]={nil,nil,0},
[65597]={"The time has come at last. Bring the hearts to the summoning circle below. Place them at its center and call forth the incubus.$b$bThe demon will not be pleased when it realizes that you have tempted it into a trap. Do not fall prey to its beguilement, $n. You must subdue it fully.$b$bOnly then can I teach you the spell to bind it to your will.","Using the Lovers' Hearts, summon and subdue an incubus, then return the Lovers' Hearts to Carendin Halgar in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.",5},
[76160]={"Maybe your skills lie with poisons, not disguises. The Harpies to the north nest in a tree which produces a resin of potent toxicity. Gather the fallen cones around the nests, then crush them into a salve. When applied to a blade this salve will sear your opponent's wounds into their flesh and turn their blood to salt.","Gather 8 Windfury Cones north of Thunder Bluff, use them with the Mortar and Pestle, then return to Boarton Shadetotem in Thunder Bluff with the result.",4},
[78088]={"<The mysterious orb you hold fills you with cold dread. You can almost hear a voice echo faintly in your mind. Low and guttural, you understand well that the language being spoken is demonic in nature. \n\nEven as a paladin, this magic is beyond you. Find a more senior paladin here in Kalimdor who might be able to help you discern the nature of this sinister object.>","Bring the Althalaxx Orb to Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post in Ashenvale.",5},
[78089]={"There's a powerful darkness about this orb. Its nature is clearly demonic, but past that it is beyond my ability to discern its purpose.\n\nTake the orb to the one known as Katherine the Pure in the Stormwind Cathedral. Consult with her for advice on the orb.","Bring the Althalaxx Orb to Katherine the Pure in Stormwind.",4},
[78090]={"I'm not sure what to make of this orb, $n. I think we will need the help of... a specialist.\n\nWe are aware of a warlock sect operating out of Stormwind. Officially we reject the presence of warlocks in the city. Unofficially, their knowledge can be of use when dealing with demonic forces.\n\nFind a representative of these warlocks, and seek their opinion on the orb.","Find the warlock sanctum within Stormwind and seek advice on the orb.",0},
[78091]={"I will study the orb and tell you what I learn, but you must first do something for me.\n\nThe warlocks of the Blackrock clan use specially prepared salts to enhance their summoning rituals. Collect some from the orcs in Redridge.\n\nWhen you return, I will share with you the results of my studies.","Collect 14 Summoner's Salt from Blackrock Summoners in Redridge Mountains, then return to Ursula Deline in Stormwind.",5},
[78093]={"<The shattered remains of the orb lay at your feet. Delgren will want to see you have succeeded.>","Return the Orb Shards to Delgren.",6},
[78134]={nil,nil,6},
[78142]={nil,nil,1},
[78143]={nil,nil,1},
[78145]={nil,nil,1},
[78146]={nil,nil,1},
[78148]={nil,nil,1},
[78261]={"<A note sits in the chest>\n\nHello, $n.\n\nI desire a treasure known as The Horn of Xelthos, which is somewhere within Shadowfang Keep.\n\nVenturing inside the keep usually calls for backup. However, for this job, a low profile is of utmost importance.\n\nYou must go alone.\n\nI have a contact, by the name of Veenix, in the Stonetalon Mountains. He should be able to help you get past the courtyard gate. The rest is up to you. \n\nReturn the horn here, and your payment will be sent soon after.\n\n- C","Find The Horn of Xelthos inside of Shadowfang Keep. Then, return it to C's dead drop near Pyrewood Village. You must complete the job alone.",5},
[78307]={"Description","Log",6},
[78676]={"<A note sits in the chest>\n\nGlad to have you back, $n.\n\nThe latest object of my desire is an artifact known as the Eye of Bhossca. My sources tell me the eye is somewhere within the Scarlet Monastery. As with Shadowfang Keep, you must infiltrate the monastery alone.\n\nIt may behoove you to find a disguise before going in. It will make getting around a touch easier. I'm sure you could find something on the monastery's grounds.\n\nReturn the eye here, and payment will be delivered as before.\n\n- C","Find The Eye of Bhossca inside of the Scarlet Monastery. Then, return it to C's dead drop near Pyrewood Village. You must complete the job alone.",6},
[79007]={"<The faint radiance of the embers darkening, you stumble across the remnants of a recent fire.\n\nAmidst the scattered provisions, you discover a blistered note.>\n\n\"Not all that burns is lost. Find the twin land, find the place.\"","Charred remains of the note serve as your only guide.",5},
[79008]={"<The faint radiance of the embers darkening, you stumble across the remnants of a recent fire.\n\nAmidst the scattered provisions, you discover a blistered note.>\n\n\"Not all that burns is lost. Find the twin land, find the place.\"","Charred remains of the note serve as your only guide.",5},
[79090]={"Some of the Warsong Outriders lie defeated, but the battle still rages...","Bring the Warsong Outrider Mark to Felore Moonray, Priestess of the Moon, at the Moonwell base in Ashenvale.",0},
[79091]={nil,nil,1},
[79096]={nil,nil,1},
[79097]={nil,nil,1},
[79098]={"This one is slain, but these infuriating alliance continue to fight... what is this charm?","Bring the Silverwing Sentinel Charm to Kazragore, Far Seer, at the Bonfire base in Ashenvale.",0},
[79192]={"The note begins, \"Mission said they were both making deliveries for New Plague. Looks like simple apothecary accidents to me. Find my cozy spot in the mountains between The Barrens and Desolace if you want a safe place to talk.\"","You tear the note from the plank and read the scrawled writing.",5},
[79235]={"I've found a couple of scenes like you describe, $n. Always camps of humans and dwarves. Rumor among the caravans is a group of Horde marauders did it. Seems likely given the victims, and how brutal the attacks were.\n\nApparently the bandits fled Desolace once an Alliance marshal got hot on their trail.\n\nIf you're looking to track one of 'em down, I'd check Booty Bay. Ports always have shady characters coming and going. You might catch one trying to get a boat to somewhere.","Find one of the Desolace marauders.",3},
[79358]={"Floodin' the Thousand Needles is no small feat, $n. If I hadn't felt the elements' outrage meself, I'd have never believed it. But here we are.\n\nThe quilboar aren't the first tae weaponize the elements irresponsibly, and they won't be the last. If we want to prepare our own counter-ritual, we'll need a better understanding of these twisted elements. Take this book. It details the many denizens of Azeroth and how they practice shamanism.\n\nIf you can learn from them, maybe we can find a solution.","Collect $1oa Twisted Fire Totems, $2oa Twisted Earth Totems, $3oa Twisted Air Totems, and $4oa Twisted Water Totems for Veyric Thunderhame in Arathi Highlands.",5},
[79360]={"Now that you have mastered the elements, you have an obligation to them, and thus to all of Azeroth herself. We call to them for aid, we do not demand their power. It is time you return the favors granted to you. And I think I know how.\n\nThe quilboar twist the elements for their own ends, and seem to be extending their reach within these borders. Go into their kraul and put an end to whatever they scheme. These lands must be protected.","Defeat Charlga Razorflank in Razorfen Kraul and collect information on the quilboar's plans.",6},
[79361]={"So the quilboar mean to flood the Thousand Needles with their twisted shamanism, do they? It seems almost unimaginable, but you yourself have seen that these creatures are not to be taken lightly.\n\nI had wished to continue your training in earnest, but there is no time for that now. These lands are home to many different creatures, friend and foe alike, and none of them deserve such a fate. We must act.\n\nTake this tome. It was meant for study, but may now hold the key to dispersing this coming storm.","Collect $1oa Twisted Fire Totems, $2oa Twisted Earth Totems, $3oa Twisted Air Totems, and $4oa Twisted Water Totems for Prate Cloudseer in Thousand Needles.",5},
[79365]={"Here mon, a Squall-breakers Potion be what you need. Drink this to protect yourself against the elements of the storm, but remember it only goin' to last for a short while.$B$BNow go, return to your friends in need. There's nothing more I can do for you.","Return to Rau Cliffrunner in Thousand Needles at Freewind Post.",0},
[79482]={"Listen... not to shatter the magic of the season here, but Smokywood Pastures could use some assistance - the kind you adventuring types are known to give.$B$BWe're missing an important shipment of treats that was restocking us for the season, and now we're missing the agent of Smokywood Pastures that we sent out to the field to find it!  Please - the shipment was last reported in the Alterac Mountains, and that's where our man went to look for it.$B$BSee if both are out there, safe and sound!","Locate the Smokywood Pastures investigator that has gone missing in the snowy regions of the Alterac Mountains.",2},
[79483]={"Listen... not to shatter the magic of the season here, but Smokywood Pastures could use some assistance - the kind you adventuring types are known to give.$B$BWe're missing an important shipment of treats that was restocking us for the season, and now we're missing the agent of Smokywood Pastures that we sent out to the field to find it!  Please - the shipment was last reported in the Alterac Mountains, and that's where our man went to look for it.$B$BSee if both are out there, safe and sound!","Locate the Smokywood Pastures investigator that has gone missing in the snowy regions of the Alterac Mountains.",2},
[79492]={"DISASTER has struck!  Metzen the Reindeer has been kidnapped!$B$BMetzen is one of Greatfather Winter's eight reindeer - and property of Smokywood Pastures.  We've received not one but TWO ransom letters from groups claiming to have Metzen.  With the holiday season well under way, we're strapped to the coin box here!  Please - find Metzen and return him to us!$B$BCheck out the ransom letters for clues, and sprinkle this reindeer dust on him - it will free him from any of his bonds!$B$BPlease, hurry!","Find Metzen the Reindeer.  Use the notes provided to you for clues as to where he is being held.$B$BWhen you find Metzen, have the Pouch of Reindeer Dust in your possession so you can sprinkle some of the dust on him; this should free Metzen from his bonds of captivity.$B$BReturn the Pouch of Reindeer Dust to Wulmort Jinglepocket in Ironforge once Metzen is freed.",4},
[79536]={nil,nil,1},
[79637]={nil,nil,0},
[79677]={"Other ogres laugh at Skonk because Skonk smaller than them. They say small ogre weak, so Skonk learn to cook instead of fight. This only cause more teasing, so Skonk run away to follow dream.\n\nSkonk can make dish, but need ingredients. You take note. Find ingredients. Skonk more focused on craft; not really logistics guy.","Gather the ingredients for Skonk's dish, then bring them to him in Arathi Highlands",5},
[79678]={"Ok $r buddy, it time for Skonk favorite part. Skonk have fire hot and ready, and want to share new dish with new friend. You do such big favors for Skonk; it only right you get some too!\n\nLet Skonk know when you ready for tasting.","Taste test the recipe with Skonk.",5},
[79940]={"<Katherine winces as she holds the shattered fragments of the broken hammer> \n\nI won't speak of this weapon's master in detail for the telling would fill me with shame, but I'll tell you what I can.","Speak with Katherine the Pure and learn more about the broken hammer.",4},
[79945]={"This appears to be orders from the Grand Crusader of the Scarlet Crusade himself, Dathrohan. It seems that Aeonas has run afoul of the Crusade. Judging by the scene before you, it appears that the Crusade was able to follow Aeonas here and apprehend him. It appears that he did not go down without a fight.\n\nThe charges levied against Aeonas are grave, but that would explain some of the scene you came upon in Desolace.","Bring the Orders from the Grand Crusader back to Katherine the Pure.",4},
[79948]={nil,nil,1},
[79949]={nil,nil,1},
[79963]={"<Aeonas needs immediate healing or he will die. Call upon the light and save him.>","Heal Aeonas.",4},
[79974]={"\"Always like to keep a reserve stash nearby in the off chance I've got to flee in a hurry.\n\nThe face of this mountainside is so beautiful you might say it was carved from the waterfalls of time. \nThat's the eagles nest, that's what you're looking for.\"","Dusting off a messenger bag emerging from the soil, you find a parchment nestled among the supplies.",5},
[79975]={"<You find a carefully folded letter inside of the toolbox.>\n\n\"From here, with the right tools, you call the shots. Great place to launch a parachute glider.\n\nMy loyalty to the Eagle and Fist requires distance in order to serve them best. This barricade has had better days, like the Old Kingdoms it once defended, but I'll never abandon it.\"","Water spray dampens the air, the view is incredible.",5},
[79976]={"\"So, I've decided to take my work back underground. To stop it falling into the wrong hands.\"\n\n<The paper is torn just large enough to fit the message. You aren't sure if these are the last words you'll read from the author, or if they're a clue to the next hideout. An inadequately secured sleeping bag is unrolling itself onto your feet...>","Whoever was here, you just missed them.",4},
[79980]={"\"Not so bad, eh? Since you're reading this, it means my stash is still there. Take a hundred paces due north and don't break your ankles going down the steep cliffside. There should be enough to keep you going.\"","Find what awaits you.",1},
[80001]={nil,nil,0},
[81570]={"I have cutting to do.  I can't tell you what I'm going to cut, but... I need myself a blade.  A certain blade...$B$BSome people call it a moonsteel broadsword.  I call it a swing blade.$B$BYou help me?  Maybe you find it in town, maybe you talk to a blacksmith and he'll make it special.$B$BBut don't sleep on this.  What I'm cutting won't keep forever...","Bring a Moonsteel Broadsword to Jarl in Dustwallow Marsh.",6},
[81730]={"While these demons distract us here, the Emerald Dream is being corrupted into nightmare. Quick, travel through the Emerald Dream Portal in the Twilight Grove, and journey to the Nightmare Incursion in the Rotting Orchard. Defeat worgen there and return to me.","Defeat 10 Nightmare Runners and 10 Nightmare Weavers in the Duskwood Nightmare Incursion in the Rotting Orchard and return to Field Captain Palandar.",5},
[81734]={"While these demons distract us here, the Emerald Dream is being corrupted into nightmare. Quick, travel through the Emerald Dream Portal in the Twilight Grove, and journey to the Nightmare Incursion at the Rotting Orchard. Retrieve an intelligence report from Dreamwarden Dorilar there and return to me.","Gather intelligence from Dreamwarden Dorilar in the Duskwood Nightmare Incursion in the barn at the Rotting Orchard and return to Field Captain Palandar.",4},
[81736]={"While these demons distract us here, the Emerald Dream is being corrupted into nightmare. Quick, travel through the Emerald Dream Portal in the Twilight Grove, and journey to the Nightmare Incursion at the Rotting Orchard. Retrieve a powerful artifact known as the Shadowscythe and deliver it to me.","Recover the Shadowscythe in the Duskwood Nightmare Incursion upstairs in the farmhouse at the Rotting Orchard and return to Field Captain Palandar.",4},
[81737]={"While these demons distract us here, the Emerald Dream is being corrupted into nightmare. Quick, travel through the Emerald Dream Portal in the Twilight Grove, and journey to the Nightmare Incursion at the Vul'gol Ogre Mound. Retrieve an Ogre Magi Text and deliver it to me.","Recover an Ogre Magi Text in the Duskwood Nightmare Incursion within the Vul'gol Ogre Mound and return to Field Captain Palandar.",4},
[81738]={"While these demons distract us here, the Emerald Dream is being corrupted into nightmare. Quick, travel through the Emerald Dream Portal in the Twilight Grove, and journey to the Nightmare Incursion at the Yorgen Farmstead. Retrieve an Unhatched Green Dragon Egg and deliver it to me.","Recover an Unhatched Green Dragon Egg in the Duskwood Nightmare Incursion from the Yorgen Farmstead near the large stump in the fields and return to Field Captain Palandar.",4},
[81739]={"While these demons distract us here, the Emerald Dream is being corrupted into nightmare. Quick, travel through the Emerald Dream Portal in the Twilight Grove and collect Nightmare Moss from within the Nightmare Incursions. We can harness its magic to reverse the damage. You will need the assistance of an herbalist.","Gather 10 Nightmare Moss in the Duskwood Nightmare Incursions and return to Field Captain Palandar.",5},
[81746]={"While these demons distract us here, the Emerald Dream is being corrupted into nightmare. Quick, travel through the Emerald Dream Portal in the Twilight Grove, and journey to the Nightmare Incursion at the Yorgen Darmstead. Find the sleeping Druid of the Claw Alara Grovemender there and escort her to safety. Then return to me.","Rescue Alara Grovemender in the Duskwood Nightmare Incursion in the stable at the Yorgen Farmstead and return to Field Captain Palandar.",4},
[81762]={"Greetings, $n. I have good news. I've made contact with my friend, and I am leaving soon to meet with him. What's more, another orb has surfaced in Kalimdor.  I cannot be in two places at once so if you are willing, I'd like for you to go in my stead to follow up on this new orb. Speak with Katherine for further instructions.","Speak with Katherine the Pure at the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind.",3},
[81765]={"<The Paladin standing before you is not known to you. Speak with him to determine what he knows of the merchant and the current situation.>","Speak with Elrick to learn more.",6},
[81790]={"Each of the Echoing Orbs is attuned to a different aspect of its master. The method you used in Ashenvale to destroy the Althalaxx Orb will not be effective on the orb we possess. I know of a ritual that may be able to destabilize the orb and allow us to destroy it, but it requires components with specific magical significance. We already possess some of the required materials, but you'll need to retrieve the rest. \n\nTake this, it should help you in your search.","Use the hints in Gregory's Note to determine where to find the magical components needed for the ritual. You will need help from allies for this.",6},
[81900]={"<The carving before you depicts a two-headed beast emerging from the Dark Portal. Fel-fire spews forth from its mouths. A plaque beneath the image reads: \"Calefactus the Unleashed\". \n\nIntuition tells you the Twilight cultists may have plans to harness this creature's destructive power for their own aims.\n\nYou reason that the next step in your hunt is towards the Blasted Lands. Someone there may know more of this hellish beast.>","Find an expert on the beasts of the Blasted Lands.",3},
[81917]={"I have seen this creature you call \"Calefactus\" many times in my field studies. By all accounts, it appears to be a nigh-invulnerable core hound made from Fel energies.\n\nHowever, if what you say is true, and the Twilight's Hammer were planning to enslave it, then there may be a way to subdue the beast.\n\nThe Shadowsworn, to the south-east, are known to perform dark rituals, including the enslavement of Fel creatures. Perhaps members of their order carry a clue to weakening Calefactus?","Bring 5 infernal chain links to Bloodmage Lynnore in the Blasted Lands",5},
[81944]={nil,nil,6},
[81947]={nil,nil,1},
[81949]={nil,nil,1},
[81952]={nil,nil,1},
[82208]={nil,nil,1},
[84135]={"Lying on the shore, half-lost in the afternoon spray, is a strange metal contraption. It looks like some kind of mech, but you have never seen anything like it before. You notice a label on its side that reads \"Property of D.E.L.T.A.: Deepsea Exploration and Liquefaction Technologies Alliance\". You also spot a small compartment that you might be able to open.","Use a rock or something to dislodge parts of the mech.",2},
[84137]={"You wonder why this mech was crashed here, and what this liquid is for. Maybe you can use it to reach the nearby islands and oil rig that seem to be connected to this mysterious organization. Opening the vial, a mildly intoxicating fruity aroma greets your nose.","Find a use for the Guided Buoyancy Accelerant",4},
[84138]={"I'm the chief engineer, founder and lead researcher of the Deepsea Exploration and Liquefaction Technologies Alliance. I've nearly finished my latest experiment, and I need your help! I am working on a special device to geolocate resource-rich dimensions.\n\nTo complete my construction, I need something back: a book of arcane formulas that I lent to an old colleague of mine, Nami, who continues her work in Winterspring.\n\nRetrieve the book for me and you'll be included as a published contributor!","Explain the book situation to Doctor Jurgens' colleague, Nami, in Winterspring.",4},
[84147]={"Well met, $c.  I've something that might interest you.$B$BI have in my possession a set of armor much like the one worn by those of your profession, but of much higher quality.  I'd be willing to trade the bracers for ordinary ones in exchange for a small favor.$B$BThe blood of the frostsabers and bears that inhabit Winterspring has properties I'm in need of at the moment.  Bring me a sizeable sample of it along with the bracers and a small amount of gold.  You shall find the effort worth your while.","Acquire 15 Winterspring Blood Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Wildheart Bracers to Deliana in Ironforge.",5},
[84149]={"Well met, $c.  I've something that might interest you.$B$BI have in my possession a set of armor much like the one worn by those of your profession, but of much higher quality.  I'd be willing to trade the bracers for ordinary ones in exchange for a small favor.$B$BThe blood of the frostsabers and bears that inhabit Winterspring has properties I'm in need of at the moment.  Bring me a sizeable sample of it along with the bracers and a small amount of gold.  You shall find the effort worth your while.","Acquire 15 Winterspring Blood Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Magister's Bindings to Deliana in Ironforge.",5},
[84151]={"Well met, $c.  I've something that might interest you.$B$BI have in my possession a set of armor much like the one worn by those of your profession, but of much higher quality.  I'd be willing to trade the bracers for ordinary ones in exchange for a small favor.$B$BThe blood of the frostsabers and bears that inhabit Winterspring has properties I'm in need of at the moment.  Bring me a sizeable sample of it along with the bracers and a small amount of gold.  You shall find the effort worth your while.","Acquire 15 Winterspring Blood Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with 1 set of Devout Bracers to Deliana in Ironforge.",5},
[84152]={"Well met, $c.  I've something that might interest you.$B$BI have in my possession a set of armor much like the one worn by those of your profession, but of much higher quality.  I'd be willing to trade the bracers for ordinary ones in exchange for a small favor.$B$BThe blood of the frostsabers and bears that inhabit Winterspring has properties I'm in need of at the moment.  Bring me a sizeable sample of it along with the bracers and a small amount of gold.  You shall find the effort worth your while.","Acquire 15 Winterspring Blood Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Shadowcraft Bracers to Deliana in Ironforge.",5},
[84153]={"Well met, $c.  I've something that might interest you.$B$BI have in my possession a set of armor much like the one worn by those of your profession, but of much higher quality.  I'd be willing to trade the bracers for ordinary ones in exchange for a small favor.$B$BThe blood of the frostsabers and bears that inhabit Winterspring has properties I'm in need of at the moment.  Bring me a sizeable sample of it along with the bracers and a small amount of gold.  You shall find the effort worth your while.","Acquire 15 Winterspring Blood Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Dreadmist Bracers to Deliana in Ironforge.",5},
[84154]={"Well met, $c.  I've something that might interest you.$B$BI have in my possession a set of armor much like the one worn by those of your profession, but of much higher quality.  I'd be willing to trade the bracers for ordinary ones in exchange for a small favor.$B$BThe blood of the frostsabers and bears that inhabit Winterspring has properties I'm in need of at the moment.  Bring me a sizeable sample of it along with the bracers and a small amount of gold.  You shall find the effort worth your while.","Acquire 15 Winterspring Blood Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Bracers of Valor to Deliana in Ironforge.",5},
[84156]={"Hail, $c!  I can tell by your demeanor that you've seen and done much in this world.  Yet I'm willing to wager you haven't seen a piece of armor like this.$B$BPerform a small favor for me and I'll be willing to trade it to you for an ordinary set of bracers.$B$BI'm in need of a sizeable sample of venom drawn from the spiders and scorpions that inhabit Silithus.  Bring this to me along with a few gold coins and I'll perform the exchange.","Acquire 15 Silithus Venom Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Beaststalker's Bindings to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.",5},
[84157]={"Hail, $c!  I can tell by your demeanor that you've seen and done much in this world.  Yet I'm willing to wager you haven't seen a piece of armor like this.$B$BPerform a small favor for me and I'll be willing to trade it to you for an ordinary set of bracers.$B$BI'm in need of a sizeable sample of venom drawn from the spiders and scorpions that inhabit Silithus.  Bring this to me along with a few gold coins and I'll perform the exchange.","Acquire 15 Silithus Venom Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Magister's Bindings to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.",5},
[84161]={"Hail, $c!  I can tell by your demeanor that you've seen and done much in this world.  Yet I'm willing to wager you haven't seen a piece of armor like this.$B$BPerform a small favor for me and I'll be willing to trade it to you for an ordinary set of bracers.$B$BI'm in need of a sizeable sample of venom drawn from the spiders and scorpions that inhabit Silithus.  Bring this to me along with a few gold coins and I'll perform the exchange.","Acquire 15 Silithus Venom Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Dreadmist Bracers to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.",5},
[84166]={"You kept your word and brought the device built by Mux.  I believe a reward is in order if I'm to keep you interested in saving my skin.  Bring me the belt and set of gauntlets that you wish to upgrade.  I promise the ones I give you in return will be far superior.","Bring a Lightforge Belt and a set of Lightforge Gauntlets to Deliana in Ironforge.",7},
[84170]={"You kept your word and brought the device built by Mux.  I believe a reward is in order if I'm to keep you interested in saving my skin.  Bring me the belt and set of gauntlets that you wish to upgrade.  I promise the ones I give you in return will be far superior.","Bring a Belt of Valor and a set of Gauntlets of Valor to Deliana in Ironforge.",7},
[84172]={"You've proven to be a very reliable individual, $n.  As much as I trust that you'll help me through this predicament, it would be wise of me to reward you according to your performance.$B$BFor now I will exchange your belt and gloves.  If we both see this through I shall make the rest of the pieces available to you.","Bring a Beaststalker's Belt and a set of Beaststalker's Gloves to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.",7},
[84173]={"You've proven to be a very reliable individual, $n.  As much as I trust that you'll help me through this predicament, it would be wise of me to reward you according to your performance.$B$BFor now I will exchange your belt and gloves.  If we both see this through I shall make the rest of the pieces available to you.","Bring a Magister's Belt and a set of Magister's Gloves to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.",7},
[84179]={"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet.  In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.$B$BThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the medallion back together.  Return to Deliana and tell her that Bodley is her only hope for finding the remaining pieces.  Speak to her about any rewards you've arranged for.$B$BI, for once, shall rest in peace.  I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","Return to Deliana in Ironforge with a set of Wildheart Boots, a Wildheart Kilt and Wildheart Spaulders.",7},
[84181]={"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet.  In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.$B$BThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the medallion back together.  Return to Deliana and tell her that Bodley is her only hope for finding the remaining pieces.  Speak to her about any rewards you've arranged for.$B$BI, for once, shall rest in peace.  I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","Return to Deliana in Ironforge with a set of Magister's Boots, Magister's Leggings and Magister's Mantle.",7},
[84184]={"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet.  In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.$B$BThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the medallion back together.  Return to Deliana and tell her that Bodley is her only hope for finding the remaining pieces.  Speak to her about any rewards you've arranged for.$B$BI, for once, shall rest in peace.  I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","Return to Deliana in Ironforge with a set of Shadowcraft Boots, Shadowcraft Pants and Shadowcraft Spaulders.",7},
[84186]={"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet.  In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.$B$BThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the medallion back together.  Return to Deliana and tell her that Bodley is her only hope for finding the remaining pieces.  Speak to her about any rewards you've arranged for.$B$BI, for once, shall rest in peace.  I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","Return to Deliana in Ironforge with a set of Boots of Valor, Legplates of Valor and Spaulders of Valor.",7},
[84187]={"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet.  In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.$B$BThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together.  Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces.  Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.$B$BI, for once, shall rest in peace.  I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of Wildheart Boots, a Wildheart Kilt and Wildheart Spaulders.",7},
[84191]={"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet.  In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.$B$BThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together.  Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces.  Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.$B$BI, for once, shall rest in peace.  I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of  Shadowcraft Boots, Shadowcraft Pants and Shadowcraft Spaulders.",7},
[84192]={"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet.  In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.$B$BThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together.  Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces.  Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.$B$BI, for once, shall rest in peace.  I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of Boots of Elements, Kilt of Elements and Pauldrons of Elements.",7},
[84202]={"That's an amazing story, $n! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved. Now maybe I'll be able to sleep at night with both eyes shut.$B$BAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you'll really enjoy.","Give Deliana your Helm of Valor and Breastplate of Valor.",2},
[84210]={"A truly amazing story, $n! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved, I can assure you. Through your efforts we are delivered from the mistakes of our past.$B$BAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you have definitely earned and will truly enjoy.","Give Mokvar your Helm of Valor and Breastplate of Valor.",2},
[84212]={"Nami hands over Jurgens' book. With it safely stowed, you begin the long journey back to the other side of the world.","Return to the D.E.L.T.A lab with the book Jurgens was looking for.",5},
[84213]={"Join me in this historic experiment and witness the wonders of my invention! I've calculated two locations with suitable geothermic bioflux energy. With manual-auto-locking phasers, I'm ready to send us to the coordinates within compatible regions.\n\nOnce you're at compatible coordinates, use this remote transponder to send the signal to me. I'll configure the warp transmitter to fold the space between here, and there.\n\nWhat I'm saying is, I'll meet you there when you say you're ready!","Use the Distant Communication Device to send the signal to Jurgens at either Tirisfal Glades or Westfall\nThen, assist him in demonstrating the capabilities of his elecro transmitter.",7},
[84397]={nil,nil,1},
[84401]={nil,nil,1},
[84402]={nil,nil,1},
[84414]={"<You hear the disembodied voice of Orthas in your mind>\n\n'Ere we are then. Let's get on with it, shall we?","Observe Orthas as he moves on from this world.",3},
[86585]={"The fallen mountaineer bears a standard of Ironforge. Perhaps she was scouting, or making a doomed charge. Either way, the standard has been cast down and trampled. The mountaineer was hit on the head so hard that her helm was knocked off and she was killed outright by a trogg, likely with a spiked club.\n\nThe trogg that killed her is probably still nearby, and likely remembers the banner. Raising the banner of Ironforge once more may call it out.","Raise the standard of Ironforge, call out the trogg Headsplitter and kill it, then report to Captain Rugelfuss.",5},
[86613]={"The excavation's tools, left behind when the dwarves fled from the troggs, seem mostly untouched. Returning them to the excavators will surely aid their work.","Return $1oa Excavation Tools to Magmar Fellhew.",5},
[86614]={"<Among the fishing knickknacks in the debris are some rusty hooks, broken spools of wire, and a slightly corroded but ornate silver hair clip with the monogram \"K.D.\">","Return the Monogrammed Silver Hair clip to its owner.",5},
[86615]={"Ach! Here I am serving as ambassador to the Wildhammers, and I left me satchel of the latest diplomatic missives somewhere in Wildhammer Keep. I must've left it in the tavern... or maybe I misplaced it by the steam tanks... or was it upstairs? I can never keep track!\n\nI need those papers! If you have a better eye for the keep than I do, see if you can spot my missing diplomatic satchel!","Find Ambassador Redstone's missing diplomatic satchel in Wildhammer Keep.",1},
[86667]={"My old mentor, Norric, sent a minor elemental with an odd request. He needs a jar of snow for some of his shamanic workings! I don't know what he's going to do with that, but I learned a long time ago not to question his ways with respect to magic.\n\nI'm busy learning about the local elementals, so I can't leave to help him. Go to the tunnel entrance at South Gate Pass where there's snow year-round. Scoop some up in this ceramic jar and bring it to him before it melts. The jar should keep it cold.","Deliver a Jar of Snow to Norric Lochthane at his house on the northwest coast of the Loch.",3},
[86746]={"My people are struggling, $n. \n\nThe Legashi satyr have invaded our den, corrupting many of the Blackmaw and separating us from our Timbermaw allies. Those of us who survive their attacks are huddled in makeshift camps. Worse still, the satyr's corruption is spreading across the land, and poses a threat to my already vulnerable tribe.\n\nThe Legashi lurk among the ruins northeast of here. I must ask you for help in defeating them.","Kill $1oa Legashi Satyr, $2oa Legashi Rogues, and $3oa Legashi Hellcallers for Ekkal at the Ruins of Eldarth.",5},
[86757]={"Orcs have taken over the eastern forest, and their scouts and grunts now lurk throughout the woods! It's not safe for our kind to move about Ashenvale any more.\n\nWe need to push back the orcs and secure the forest. We've been able to pick off some of the grunts and scouts by carefully sneaking around the edges of their camp.\n\nFight the orcs and bring me the jagged swords and curved knives that they use. I'll make sure their weapons are salvaged and repurposed, so nothing goes to waste.","Bring $1oa Jagged Orc Swords and $2oa Curved Orc Daggers to Shandrina.",5},
[86758]={"Did I ever tell you how I almost lost me hand to a crocolisk? Managed to jam me knife into its jaw, and scrambled out real quick. I thought I had the knife around here somewhere, but I can't seem to find it.\n\nAnyway, that croc is probably still out there hunting along the edge of the lake. That nasty brute probably needs to go, for the safety of the other hunters, if nothing else.\n\nI've taken to calling it Daggerfang. If you see it, give it a friendly hello from me! And by \"hello\" I mean \"stab.\"","Find and defeat the crocolisk Daggerfang and bring back Marek's knife.",5},
[86776]={"Thelsamar's a great place to live, but we don't have all of the amenities of Ironforge. I'm always running out of bronze! I need more bronze if I'm going to keep making tools and kettles and pots!\n\nI can tell you have a little experience at the forge. Think you could smelt me some bronze bars? I can pay you well for it!","Bring $1oa Bronze Bars to Morhan Coppertongue.",5},
[86784]={"My associate Eleanor Shackleton prides herself on traveling the wilds, surviving against weather and monsters. She is currently camped not far from here, in the hills to the west, and I remember a piece of advice that she once gave me: \"When you think you have enough firewood, gather five times more.\"\n\nIf you have some spare time, you could collect some wood in this basket and take it to her camp. I'm sure she could give you a few tips about the existence of a traveling adventurer.","Collect $1oa Dry Branches and bring them to Eleanor Shackleton.",5},
[86792]={"The satyr within the Legashi stronghold are even more fearsome than those of the outer camps. When our party was discovered, we found ourselves overwhelmed.\n\nOne of us was slain, and another captured. I was the only one able to successfully retreat. I cannot return to Rageroar with my head hung in shame, but I cannot fight the Legashi alone, either.\n\nI ask you, then, to assist me in weakening the satyr's forces. Go into their stronghold and slay them.","Kill $1oa Legashi Hellraisers, $2oa Legashi Soulstealers, and $3oa Legashi Blackguards for Korsa outside Legashi Stronghold.",5},
[86796]={"You there, $r!\n\nThese fiends ambushed my scouting party, and have taken me captive. I don't know what plans they have for me, but I don't intend to find out. I must escape and return to Ursolan; no doubt Korsa is worried about me.\n\nWhile I would love to break out of this cage and leave a trail of satyr corpses in my wake, I'm afraid I'm slightly outnumbered.\n\nPerhaps you share my hatred for the fiends, and would help me escape?","Help Graal break out of Legashi Stronghold, then inform Korsa outside Legashi Stronghold.",5},
[86799]={"<Furze lets loose an ugly, hacking, cough.>\n\nHear me, $r, I haven't much strength to speak. I am stricken by an illness unlike any I have ever known. It is as if my blood itself is aflame, and my very essence is coming undone. I can hardly move, much less fetch help.\n\nPlease, go find Elder Bramblesnap. Her tent is just northwest of here. She will know what to do.","Speak to Elder Bramblesnap about Furze's illness.",1},
[86804]={"Furze is not the first with his affliction. Since the Legashi's attacks against us began, many Blackmaw have presented with a similar illness. Each one eventually fell to corruption, becoming mindless and destructive.\n\nI have been working towards a cure. My studies indicate that one could possibly be made by transmuting the Legashi's own firewater, but I cannot acquire it myself.\n\nYou might find firewater, or a way to brew it, in the Legashi camps to the east. You would be a great help in doing so.","Find a way to get Legashi Firewater in the Legashi Encampment.",4},
[86927]={"As the satyrweed and fel mote splash into the boiling liquid, a plume of noxious gas emerges.\n\nBest to hold your nose, quickly grab a sample, and bring it back to Elder Bramblesnap.","Bring the Legashi Firewater to Elder Bramblesnap at Ursolan.",5},
[87295]={"You may have seen the Redstone basilisks wandering the wastes outside while you were on your way to Nethergarde Keep. They're tough creatures, well adapted to survival in the Blasted Lands. One of their key qualities is their sturdy scales, which reflect heat, protect against sand and wind, and even deflect weapon blows!\n\nThey're a perfect material for making shields, and if you can bring me a bundle, I'll compensate you well. Only bring ones in good condition!","Bring $1oa Redstone Basilisk Scales to Bernie Heisten.",5},
[87346]={"When the Legashi overran the Blackmaw, the rest of the Timbermaw sealed their passage to the hold to keep out the satyr. We had no idea they lived on as refugees.\n\nI would gladly aid my brethren, but we are fighting our own battles. Like the Legashi threaten the Blackmaw, the Deadwood do likewise to us. We haven't many warriors to spare.\n\nThe Deadwood chieftain, Bloodmaw, is in Felpaw Village to the south. Eliminating him would greatly ease our struggle. Bring me his mace, and you will have our aid.","Kill Chieftain Bloodmaw and bring his mace to Gorn One Eye in Timbermaw Hold.",5},
[87760]={"I have received word back from Darnassus, $n!\n\nFrom the animal samples, we learned that the naga dominated these sea creatures to use as unwilling mounts and beasts of burden. The ones that were too obstinate, or too old or badly injured, they drove out for sport. Monstrous!\n\nIt is our sacred duty to put a stop to this!\n\nThe naga have forces in the Ruins of Mathystra, and they must be seizing threshers from off the shore. Find their beastmistress, slay her, and bring back her tools of domination!","Find a Stormscale Beastmistress, slay her, and bring back her Rod of Deep Dominion.",5},
[88807]={"Azshara may appear beautiful, but it is a cursed place. There are horrors deep beneath its waters, waiting to emerge and tear the world asunder.\n\nAll we can do for now is fight the horrors that have already surfaced.\n\nThe Spitelash Naga occupy the Ruins of Eldarath to the north east. The ones within the ruins are well-fortified, so we must pick off the weaker ones along the outskirts first.\n\nAs you can see, we could always use another fighter here, if you are up to the task.","Kill 8 Spitelash Warriors and 8 Spitelash Screamers for Commander Truesong in Azshara.",5},
[88821]={"While scouting along the cliffs of the Shattered Strand, one of our sentinels noticed a kaldorei woman on the beach.\n\nClearly, she is not with our expedition, and she did not have the makings of a fighter. I wonder then, what she could be doing in such a hostile place as this.\n\nIf you can, try to make contact with her. I would like to know her purpose for being here, and if our interests are perhaps aligned.\n\nShe was last seen on the eastern coast, along the north side of the Bay of Storms.","Find the Kaldorei woman last seen on the Shattered Strand.",1},
[88884]={"Just south of here, along the beach, there are some tablets of highborne writing. They document the highborne's investigations into the laws and powers of the arcane. \n\nThe tablets are being kept in pagoda-like structures, guarded by naga, so I wouldn't dare attempt to procure them myself.\n\nFortunately, I've found myself a new assistant! \n\nSo, what do you say? Think you could be of further use in the pursuit of knowledge?","Find the three highborne tablets among the ruins of Southridge Beach, then bring them to Saria Fairmoon in Azshara.",5},
[88917]={"I came here in search of highborne artifacts. You could call me an archaeologist of sorts.\n\nThe ruins of Eldarath to the west hold many of them, although the naga are looting the ruins as we speak.\n\nA naga called Lady Sesspira leads the pillaging; no doubt keeping the best finds for herself. \n\nIf my research is correct, I believe she may be in possession of the staff of Archmage Selwyn, a fallen highborne mage.\n\nI need your help to get that staff, $r. Scholars like me are ill-suited for combat.","Find the Staff of Archmage Selwyn among the Ruins of Eldarath, and bring it to Saria Fairmoon in Azshara.",5},
[89015]={"If ye fancy yourself a real angler, there's bigger fish out here than ye can catch with a rod.\n\nMammoth Sharks lurk in the deepest waters of the northern an' southern coasts. They swim far out, right before the sea floor drops away into the great ocean.\n\nThey're mighty big; I'd advise ye take a group of anglers with ye. \n\nDwarf like me? I prefer dry land. Those sharks'd swallow me in one bite.\n\nIf ye do go hunting one, bring me a cut o' the meat. I'd be mighty thankful.","Bring a Mammoth Shark Steak to Berdun Cliffbrew at Talrendis Point in Azshara.",5},
[89037]={"On the beaches of the northern peninsula, east of here, I came upon the Tower of Eldara. While surveying the site, I noticed a large orange murloc wielding a spiked club, and carrying a peculiar glowing crystal. Given the location, it was likely the kind that the highborne used to store their history and memories.\n\nWe must recover that crystal, $r. Who knows what secrets it could contain?\n\nThe best route to the tower is along the cliffs, with the nearest way up being just west of here.","Take the Memory Crystal from Razorgill near the Tower of Eldara, and bring it to Saria Fairmoon in Azshara.",5},
[89038]={"It is said that Queen Azshara once bestowed a gift upon the kaldorei of House Ravencrest; an emblem of great beauty and magical power. This mark was given as recognition of the Ravencrests' unwavering loyalty to the queen. \n\nThe mark was last seen near the Ravencrest Monument, atop the cliffs of the southern peninsula. Securing such a relic would be the discovery of a lifetime.\n\nAs always, the ruins of the monument are crawling with Spitelash, but I trust you're rather adept at handling them by now.","Search for the Mark of the Queen among the ruins of the Ravencrest Monument, and bring it to Saria Fairmoon in Azshara.",5},
[89053]={"I know you were initially sent here on reconnaissance, $n, but you've done a great deal for the field of archaeology.\n\nSurely, after all of your toil, you'd like to know what fruits my studies will come to bear.\n\nTo that end, before you return to your camp, I'd like to show you something. Would you oblige me?","See what Saria has to show you.",5},
[90487]={"$n, I have little more to offer. If you mean to make the long trek up the mountain, you might do well to speak with some of its ancient caretakers.\n\nFollow the road to the west. Look north, toward the foot of the mountain. You will eventually see an outpost, a remnant of the guardians that once roamed the slopes. There is an ancient there named Fraxinus. He and his friends can assist you.","Travel west from the hermit's cave to find an outpost of ancients and dryads on the lower slopes of Mount Hyjal.",1},
[90789]={"There isn't much time, $n!  My scrying spells have revealed a powerful source of magic.  I cannot leave the tower, and would ask you to kill the vile creature in possession of this artifact.$b$bThe beast is known as Scalebeard, hiding in a cave among the Bay of Storms. Burn him to ashes and take the prismatic shell from his den.","Retrieve the Prismatic Shell for Archmage Xylem.  The Archmage resides in a tower atop the cliffs of Azshara.",5},
[90854]={"Livin' out in da wild for five years done take a toll on our supplies. We had to make dis place from scratch! We could use your skills as a leatherworker.\n\nI need to repair some of da tents and buildings, and patch up some armor. You bring me a pair of Rugged Armor Kits and a Cured Rugged Hide, I help you turn it into something special.","Bring $1oa Rugged Armor Kits and $2oa Cured Rugged Hide to Zet'gan in Elderwild on Mount Hyjal.",4},
[90902]={"I am proud to welcome another newly risen paladin to our ranks. As you begin to reconnect with the light you may notice that certain abilities that were once second nature to you may cause you considerable pain to use now, particularly those involving channeling the light to heal yourself or others. \n\nThe only way around this problem is--unfortunately--to go through it. Like any other muscle that has atrophied, you must push through the pain and exercise the flesh for it to return to full function.","Heal $1oa Injured Deathguard with your Holy Light ability.",3},
[91208]={"Not all of our fellow Paladins who rise again are quick to acclimate to our new reality. Some struggle to reconcile that they are now, in a way, the very thing they spent their lives fighting against.\n\nThese individuals often simply need a kind gesture and a sympathetic ear. Unfortunately, many others are quick to turn violent. Find the frightened paladin who fled into the hills directly west of this chapel. Extend a hand in friendship. Lead them back into the light if you can.","Find the Frightened Paladin in Deathknell.",3},
[91209]={"Lordaeron may not be what it used to be, but our home still needs protection from all manner of threats and it's time for you to go out and face the world. Your next stop should be the town of Brill in central Tirisfal Glades. Go and meet with Shari Stilwell there. She can see to your continued training. \n\nOne last bit of advice before you go--take extra care as a paladin traveling through Forsaken lands. There are many in the Dark Lady's service who distrust us and our proximity to the light.","Follow the road east out of Deathknell to find the town of Brill. Report to Shari Stilwell to continue your training.",2},
[91282]={"It is encouraging to see my newly risen brothers and sisters thrive as you have. It is only through community and shared faith that we can truly realize our full potential however, and to that end we've begun to form a new paladin order right here in Tirisfal. \n\nIf you wish to learn more, you should visit our monastery on the edge of the Whispering Woods. It is called Bandarion Keep. It's on the bluffs just northwest of the Solliden Farmstead, and should be hard to miss.","Find the fortress of Bandarion Keep and report to Breton Samuels there.",2},
[91285]={"Normally we'd show our newcomers a bit more hospitality, but we've got a bit of a murloc problem at the moment.\n\nA tribe of murlocs used to use the keep as their spawning grounds. They've been a problem since we moved in and kicked them out, but now it's starting to get out of hand. You look like you've seen some action. Do you think you could help us drive back some of these pests? You'll find them lurking in the bluffs along the road to the east, and in the camps around the lake to the west.","Slay $1oa Vile Fin Attackers and $2oa Vile Fin Seers and report back to Breton Samuels when it is done.",5},
[91294]={"Now that the immediate threat of the murloc attacks is under control, I'd encourage you to show yourself around our stronghold. It isn't much yet, but it's home.\n\nWhen you are done exploring, seek out Danitha Morr, our leader. She can help you get settled in.\n\nI'm very glad to have met you, $n. May the light be your guide.","Speak to the residents of Bandarion Keep.",3},
[91316]={"This far from the Undercity, logistics are challenging and we have a dire shortage of building materials needed to help restore this fortress. I'd like your help with that.\n\nThe ruined village of Shadowvale can be found in the Whispering Forest, just southwest of here. One of the buildings has an old root cellar used to store all sorts of things. There are likely to be usable materials down there. Scavenge what you can and return to us.","Collect 12 pieces of Sturdy Lumber from Shadowvale in Tirisfal Glades.",5},
[91317]={"Not all risen paladins have acclimated well to our new existence, as you may have seen yourself already. Some have carried forward their prejudices from life, and continue to visit violence upon their fellow Forsaken.\n\nAs it stands we are mistrusted by our people who remember well the persecution inflicted by the living in the name of the light, and these attacks do not help. A number of these tarnished have taken up residence at Shadowvale to the southwest. End them and bring me their leader's head.","Slay 8 Tarnished Drudges, 6 Tarnished Zealots, and collect the head of Commander Rudolph Gelhardt in Tirisfal Glades.",5},
[91488]={"During our last skirmish with the blood elves, my tent was badly damaged. For three nights, I have been at the mercy of the elements.\n\nIt can be repaired with a few mosshoof hides, but a lack of sleep has left me unable to hunt them myself.\n\nThe easiest mosshooves to hunt are west and south of here, but the hide of any mooshoof will do.","Bring 5 Mosshoof Hides to Kurll at Valormok in Azshara.",5},
[91500]={"<Seeing how the energies of the crystals are attuned to the seals, you reason that destroying a seal, thereby releasing its energy all at once, could cause its crystal to do the same.\n\nThe explosive results would certainly draw Rimtori's ire. It would also present the perfect opportunity to attack her while she's flustered.>","Break the Seals of the Sin'dorei, then bring Magus Rimtori's head to Ag'tor Bloodfist in Valormok.",4},
[91568]={"What the beaches here lack in looks, they make up for in value!\n\nMost of the ruins here have been picked clean, but there's some serious loot under that sand. Problem is, it's all scattered, and the naga make a long search a bit impractical. So, what's a girl to do?\n\nEnter the Treasure Trowel 3000! The all-in-one treasure detecting shovel! A personal invention of mine.\n\nTake this baby down to the eastern shore, and bring back whatever you find. Then, we can split the profits!","Dig up $1oa Highborne Treasure Fragments with the Treasure Trowel 3000 for Izvi Glidfizz in Valormok.",5},
[91569]={"Listen kid, everyone out here's scramblin' for the same thing. Belgrom, the elves, the naga, they all wanna piece 'a that ancient highborne magic.\n\nMe? Couldn't care less, but I know a seller's market when I see one.\n\nI've seen blood elf arcanists carrying special wands. They're used to extract magical energy from artifacts the elves find. The arcanists stay at a camp east of the elves' base camp, along the cliffs. Get me one of those wands and I'll put you on to the score of a lifetime!","Bring a Mana-Siphoning Wand to Izvi Gildfizz at Valormok.",4},
[91607]={"<The large hunk of crystal is even heavier than it looks. While it appears to be quite the prize, its true nature is unknown to you. Someone with an eye for valuables could say what you've really found.>","Find someone to appraise the Humongous Crystal.",6},
[91685]={"When we first got here, I did some surveying for any untapped resources. Y'know, typical prospector stuff.\n\nI didn't see nothin' special 'til I searched Lake Mennar, to the south. There, I saw a huge rift floating above the water's surface. I couldn't get close, but I think it was an open leyline.\n\nIf I'm right, we can use this wand to siphon magic straight from the source! Bottle that up, sell it to the highest bidder, and bam! I'm rich!\n\nIf you go and siphon that rift for me, I'll cut you in.","Use the Mana-Siphoning Wand on the Leyline Rift in Lake Mennar and bring the Tear of Mennar to Izvi Gildfizz.",6},
[91696]={"Deadwood set on my pup and his sire. He stood fast, fought to the death as our guard. We must go home, but the way is dark and full of jaws.\n\nStay near, guard us well. I will lead, you will fend, and we will see den safe.","Escort the Barkskin Matriarch out of Deadwood Den and return to Barkskin Burrow.",5},
[91697]={"Thank you for helping gather bear berries. Small steps build trust! With the aroma of berry resin on you, the Elders should be more welcoming of you. \n\nGo and speak with Elder Mistpaw and Elder Pinespeaker.","Find and speak with Elder Mistpaw and Elder Pinespeaker within Barkskin Burrow.",1},
[91698]={"<A matriarchal furbolg speaks to you from within the cage>\n\n\"Deadwood trap me and my cub in tough cage. Key hang on Deadwood Warden belt. You hunt them, take key, lift latch, set us free. Do this, and Barkskin know your heart true.\"","Recover a Deadwood Key from a Deadwood Warden and return to the Barkskin Cage.",4},
[91723]={"Blast it! Every time I try to calibrate these sensitive arcane instruments, they get thrown off again by a surge of energy.\nThe surges seem to be coming from the north, where those primitive Kobolds have been practicing their crude magic. Could you clear some of them out, so I can continue my work?","Kill 8 Kobold Geomancers in Jasperlode Mine, then return to Hamish Bergwort in the Tower of Azora.",4},
[91725]={"I was sent by Master Theocritus to pick up some enchanting supplies from the trading post, but on the way back I was ambushed by a pack of gnolls!\n\nI dropped the package and escaped, but if I return without it, I'll be cleaning up after the polymorph experiments for weeks as punishment! Do you think you could find the supplies for me?","Collect 5 Stolen Enchanting Supplies from gnoll camps around Stone Cairn Lake, then return to Blixie Fitzwink near the Tower of Azora.",4},
[91732]={"Good steel is in short supply after the war, and our tools have suffered for it. The Jasperlode miners used finely-crafted picks, and I imagine some of them are still there in the depths of the mine. Could you retrieve some for me, and I'll see if I can repurpose the steel?","Collect 4 Mining Tools from Jasperlode Mine, then return to Hagar Lowe in Eastvale Logging Camp.",3},
[91733]={"I was bringing back a supply shipment from the trading post, but my wagon tipped over and the supplies fell in the river! Before I could catch them, they had already washed downstream.\n\nBetween the murlocs and wolves down there, I don't stand a chance of retrieving the supplies on my own. You seem like the hardy sort. Do you think you could find them for me?","Collect the Waterlogged Axe, Waterlogged Saw, and Waterlogged Toolbox that have washed downstream from Eastvale Logging Camp, then return to Ormin Pelford.",4},
[91735]={"Listen, $c, you'd best not be hangin' round here for long. But since you are, perhaps you can do a little favor for me?\n\nI be expecting a certain something from a Jediga, in Azshara. She and some orcs be havin' a camp out there. Go and tell her Jes'rimon sent you, and I'll owe you one.","Speak to Jediga in Azshara.",1},
[91736]={nil,nil,0},
[91738]={nil,nil,4},
[91740]={"This murloc has no doubt been terrorizing the local roads for some time. You suspect the nearby watch guards will want to know of its demise.","Deliver Croaky's Head to Merell Ross at Ridgepoint Tower.",5},
[91741]={"<One of the kobolds dropped this book. It looks like the kobold might have tried to eat it.\n\nBrother Paxton inside the abbey has a small library he maintains. The book must have come from there.>","Return the book to Brother Paxton.",3},
[91745]={"Go talk to the new mining apprentice, Kelsey Fargo. She works right outside the mine and has probably seen what the kobolds are up to. Maybe she can teach you a thing or two about mining while you're at it.","Talk to Kelsey Fargo outside the Echo Ridge Mine in Northshire Valley.",1},
[91746]={"The trophy serves as an impressive reminder of your victory over Elmpaw. A local hunter or skinner might be interested to hear the story.","Deliver Elmpaw's Head to Helene Peltskinner near Goldshire.",5},
[91751]={"Are you looking for an opportunity to practice skinning? My husband usually helps with hunting wolves, but he's busy up by the abbey. I could use a hand collecting more pelts to finish the orders I'm working on.","Skin wolves around Elwynn Forest to obtain $1oa Rough Wolf Pelts, then deliver them to Helene Peltskinner near Goldshire.",5},
[91753]={"Academic rigor is of course essential to the enchanter's craft, but a practical foundation can pay dividends. Consider, as an example, the lowly Kobold. Lacking formal education, they nevertheless demonstrate a sort of innate aptitude for simple cantrips and enchantments.\n\nObtain some of their wax effigies and deconstruct the enchantments bound within them. You may find it elucidating.","Kitta Firewind in the Tower of Azora wants you to collect 3 Luminous Residue.\n\nLuminous Residue can be obtained by disenchanting Crude Wax Effigies dropped by Kobold Geomancers.",4},
[91755]={"Have you seen those nasty tainted shrubberies wandering around this valley?\n\nThose plants are mean, but some of them are not entirely toxic. Their leaves can have medicinal purposes.\n\nWould you be so kind as to fetch me some Verdant Leaves? You'll have to do a little pruning, of course.","Collect $1oa Verdant Leaves from Tainted Shrubbery in the foothills of Mount Hyjal.",5},
[91775]={"While you're investigating the Fargodeep Mine, see if you can find any of Brother Paxton's books to return. In particular, Paxton is very concerned about a book titled, \"Fun with Elementals\". He thinks even a kobold could use it to summon an elemental servant. Be warned, the depths of the mine are fairly dangerous. You should bring friends.\n\nTake this book bag to protect the books when you find them!","Find 6 Lost Books and \"Fun with Elementals\" and return them to Marshal Dughan.",6},
[91777]={"There are just two books left missing on Brother Paxton's list: \"Geomancy for Curious Young Wizards\" and \"Arcane Explainer: Magical Stuff in Simple Words\".\n\nThe kobolds must have taken them to the Jasperlode Mine. Please track down those two books and bring them back to Brother Paxton.\n\nBut I'm afraid it will be quite dangerous. If the \"apprentice\" kobold was summoning an elemental, who knows what the master can do. I'd bring some friends if I were you.","Recover \"Geomancy for Curious Young Wizards\" and \"Arcane Explainer: Magical Stuff in Simple Words\" and return them to Brother Paxton inside Northshire's Abbey.",6},
[91794]={"We been stuck up here for years, always fighting against de Scourge, but we never lose hope. We fight to survive. We fight for da Horde. Da Alliance shares dis fight, but we never forget dat we still got history. Still got blood.\n\nFar to da east, at Dae'gun, dere are Horde flags from da war. Da demons carry scraps and remains as trophies from da battle, especially da tough ones. Bring me a flag and some heraldry so I can put it up and show da Alliance dat da Horde is still strong!","Collect $1oa Horde Flag and $2oa Scraps of Horde Heraldry for Kal'tinzan at Elderwild.",6},
[91858]={"A most unfortunate turn of events in Silverpine has presented a unique opportunity for us to prove our worth in the eyes of the horde.\n\nA pair of dignitaries from the Earthen Ring went missing in Silverpine Forest en route to Tarren Mill. We don't know much else but rumors say that this is becoming quite the diplomatic incident. If we can recover these missing persons, it could help gain us the legitimacy we so dearly need.\n\nWe have a man at The Sepulcher, Trevan Rol. Travel there and speak with him.","Travel to The Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest and speak with Trevan Rol about the missing Earthen Ring travelers.",2},
[91859]={"Cutting straight to it, these \"dignitaries\" are no ordinary diplomats. One was a Tauren. Ordinary enough for the Earthen Ring, but the other--and you'll scarcely believe this--was an elf. A *high* elf. They were cloaked, but I've seen quel'dorei before and I'd bet my good pinky finger that's what I saw.\n\nWhy was an elf accompanying a Tauren through horde territory? Well, your guess is as good as mine. That's as much as I know, so I'd suggest speaking with Deathguard Baldren near the entrance to town.","Speak with Deathguard Baldren about the mysterious Earthen Ring travelers who recently passed through The Sepulcher.",2},
[91860]={"Out on patrol last night I spotted a group of gnolls dumping a very large body onto a pyre on the shores of Fenris Isle. I didn't see an elf or any smaller corpses, but I'd say this doesn't bode well for them.\n\nIf you are brave or stupid you are welcome to charge into Fenris Isle to learn more, but if you ask me, it's a lot of work to find some snooty elf that's probably long dead.\n\nI know you paladins love swearing oaths and taking on lost causes, but this one isn't worth it. Trust me.","Investigate Fenris Isle to the east and learn the fate of the Earthen Ring traveling party.",2},
[91861]={"<The fact that you found only one body is a hopeful sign. Perhaps the High Elf that Trevan and Hadrec described is still alive somewhere deeper inside the nearby fortress?>","Investigate Fenris Keep to the north and attempt to locate the missing member of the Earthen Ring party.",2},
[91862]={"Quel'dorei? No, I am no \"quel'dorei\". I am Lumina Windsinger and I am shen'dorei. One of the Windshaper Skyborne.\n\nI came to these lands as a guest of the Earthen Ring. My companion Banon and I were passing through Silverpine to reach the Arathi Highlands so that we could study the elemental convergences there. Clearly, we didn't make it.\n\nWe have no time for this now though. Kill the gnolls nearby. Retrieve the key to this cage and free me. I will tell you the rest once we are safely away.","Retrieve the Fenris Isle Key from the Rot Hide Gnolls and use it to free Lumina Windsinger.",5},
[91877]={"Not many demon hunters remain on Azeroth now, but a few of us continue to hunt the most dangerous or hidden threats.\n\nA colleague of mine, Maerion Thaelemaches, headed to Hyjal to investigate rumors of demons there. While there are many demons in the dangerous Darkwhisper Gorge, there is suspicion that the demons that assaulted the mountain during the last war might not be completely defeated.\n\nThis bears investigation.","Find Maerion Thaelemaches somewhere on Mount Hyjal.",1},
[91881]={"With the warlocks under control, I'd say this area's well in wing.\n\n<The crow nods sagely, looking pleased.>\n\nThough our work here is done, there are other areas that could use your help and as an underwing of mine I would like you to go see what all the fuss is about.\n\nFollow the path northwest up the road to the old tern outpost. An old friend awaits!","Meet Sefira Everbright at the outpost.",1},
[91882]={"Years ago, the Horde and the Alliance put aside their differences to fight a greater threat--the Legion. On Mount Hyjal, the Grand Alliance forces battled Archimonde and his minions to a halt.\n\nThe retreat from the mountain was perilous, however, and some brave fighters were left behind.\n\nNow that the way up the great mountain is again open, perhaps some of these heroes remain alive in the wilds? Go to Mount Hyjal and brave its dangers. Find what became of our forces there.","Search Mount Hyjal for remnants of the Grand Alliance.",1},
[91900]={nil,nil,0},
[91920]={"I wouldn't dare to question the effectiveness of Apothecary Renferrel's formulae, however I would be lying if I said that the potion made any noticeable difference.\n\nAlong the shore of Lake Lordamere are a swarm of murlocs, and of note, murlocs have eyes. I suspect the apothecary's willingness to try new things is suppressed by his recent obsession with hearts. Bring him a few.\n\nIf my choice is to inevitably die a second death or have Renferrel kill me for questioning his methods, I choose the latter.","Gather 3 murloc eyes and bring them to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher.",3},
[91921]={"Here is the new potion to aid in Quinn's recovery, made with love extracted from six whole hearts.\n\nNow, please excuse me before your presence necessitates more paperwork.","Bring Quinn's potion to Quinn Yorick at the Ivar Patch, north of the Sepulcher.",4},
[91923]={"The mountain is overrun with wild growth, inflamed by the fel energies that rained down so long ago. Now the weeds and plants are angry, corrupted, poisoned.\n\nThere is a great thorn-bush called Celastrus that lurks about the slopes to the east. It kills animals, lashes out at other plants, feeds on the bodies of the dead. It must be destroyed!\n\nThe weeds must be cleared so that the mountain may regrow.","Find and destroy Celastrus the Bitter, and return to Thylaen with its broken frond.",6},
[91952]={"So much corruption rains down into Felwood from above. When the waters run high from Hyjal, they are filled with fel taint. It soaks into the ground and diseases the trees and plants.\n\nThere was a druid who lived in the wild, a hermit named Ketharas, who had a deep knowledge of the mountain. If anyone knows what has happened on Hyjal, it is he.\n\nI think that Felwood cannot heal until the problem on Hyjal is resolved.","Find the hermit Ketharas on Mount Hyjal.",1},
[92008]={"Another new face? \n\nI shouldn't be surprised with the strength of our so-called wards these days. How's the fel down there? I haven't been away from this workshop in weeks. Say, while you're here, I do have some favors you may be able to help me with if you find yourself in the mood for errands.\n\nYou wouldn't believe how tricky it is to get proper parts all the way up here, let alone general building material for engineering. Nami in Everlook has a parts order waiting for me - care for a winter sprint?","Retrieve Kaylaena Springbolt's parts order from Nami in Everlook.",3},
[92009]={"There's something you should know about this order. There's a few inverted mana cells padded as well as I could at the bottom of the box. The cells have a tendency to discharge when they get bumped, and when not stabilized in time. It takes about two hours for the contents to fizzle.\n\nKaylaena will know what to do when she receives them, but I suggest going slow if you're going to ride saddled up Mount Hyjal.\n\nIf you need a refill, come back and I'll top off the canisters. Be careful, you know?","Gently transport the crate of parts and baubles to Kaylaena Springwhisper in Mount Hyjal.",5},
[92014]={"Every time I take my attention off the supplies I've lugged up here for more than a few minutes, one of nature's finest thieves is pilfering and rummaging through it.\n\nThe damned foxes seem to have made a burrow beneath the boulders nearby. Apparently, me digging out this hole gave them an idea of their own.\n\nI'm working on a solution. Tell you what, bring back some of their fox tails. That'll teach them a lesson, and I'll hang the tails around the perimeter to scare the others off!","Return $1oa Rustleaf Fox Tails to Johun \"Punchy\" Dillas in Hyjal.",5},
[92015]={"You say you want to help? Alright, I've got a task for ya.\n\nEver been skunked on a hot day? Nothing worse, I tell you. Bloody things cover everything within spittin' distance in the most vile lingering stench!\n\nA family of skunks have started making their home behind my equipment crates. Help me gently expel them from our perimeter and I'll think about sharing some of this gear, once we can get to it...\n\nI can't stress this enough: don't attack them - they WILL spray you!","Make skunks leave the area around Johun's equipment without killing them.",2},
[92016]={"The roots of Nordrassil stretch far and deep, thicker than riverbanks and older than memory. Such great size carries a great hunger. In healthy times, they drink of decay and renewal alike, drawing strength from the endless turning of the natural cycle.\n\nBut Hyjal has been wounded, its soil fouled by demonic venom.\n\nDescend into the deepest depths of the Well of Eternity. Study the roots there closely. We must know whether they have drawn in too much corruption... or if the World Tree may yet endure.","Enter the Well of Eternity and examine the roots of Nordrassil.",3},
[92020]={"I've been taking notes and making drawings in my sketchbooks of all of the creatures living in Un'Goro Crater, and I made a few copies so that I can send them to people who might be interested!\n\nI have a sketchbook copy here that I've been meaning to get into the hands of the druids on Mount Hyjal, since I know that they love to study the natural world.\n\nHyjal's a bit of a trip, though. Do you think you could take it along in case you go there?","Take Hol'anyee's Big Book of Big Lizards to a druid at the summit of Mount Hyjal.",1},
[92065]={"Will you aid us in our final battle, $r, and be a savior to the Blackmaw?\n\nVarrox Bleakhoof, bane of the Blackmaw: a demon whose appetite for destruction will never be satisfied. His corruption consumes all that it touches. Even now, he and his underlings continue to lay waste to our burrows.\n\nWe've come far in our fight against the Legashi, but for the Blackmaw to ever have a future, Varrox must fall.\n\nFind him in Blackmaw Hold, and strike him down. Only then can the Blackmaw finally be at peace.","Bring Varrox Bleakhoof's Head to Gatekeeper Rageroar at Ursolan.",5},
[92066]={"When the Legashi invaded, many precious things were left behind in the commotion. Of particular value to me are two totems. They depict legends of our twin gods, Ursoc and Ursol.\n\nI know our immediate survival is of greatest concern, but we must also think of saving our people's history.\n\nThose totems are likely still in our former hold. If they are, you would be doing a great kindness by returning them to me.","Find the Totem of Ursoc and the Totem of Ursol inside Blackmaw Hold. Then, return them to Lorekeeper Nok at Ursolan.",5},
[92069]={"Two behemoths patrol the place the Blackmaw once called home: Bonesnout, the Unbroken and Withermaw, the great bear. Generations of hunters have tried to fell them, and all have failed.\n\nI take no joy in asking you to slay these magnificent beasts, but my people need to be able to return home. The least I can do is ensure their deaths are not in vain. If you bring me their remains, I will fashion a weapon in memory of their strength.","Bring the Claws of the Great Bear and the Tusks of the Unbroken to Ogtinc, in Azshara.",5},
[92070]={"The necklace is adorned with miscellaneous charms: scraps of feathers, acorn shells, and colorful pebbles. Its leather strap is torn. The ornamentation suggests it belonged to a Furbolg, while its small size and rough quality indicate a child's handiwork.\n\nThere's a chance the necklace is of some sentimental value to one of the Blackmaw. It may be good to find the owner and return it.","Find the owner of the Feathered Charm Necklace.",5},
[92100]={"<A spirit materializes before you, recovering from a full-body yawn.>\n\nYou have no ranks with you... and you are not dressed as a soldier. We repelled Archimonde then?\n\nIt's been so long. I had almost forgotten what I once was, but you... you must be one of the first to walk these craters in years.\n\n<The veteran glances at his surroundings.>\n\nLet us continue our conversation at an overlook with a view I remember vividly, just west of here. Long ago, I left my scabbard to rest there.","Find the Veteran of the Third War's scabbard near Elderwild.",4},
[92109]={"Erm... 'Ello, $Gmister:miss;. I'm not supposed to talk to strangers, but... Hey, what are those shiny bottles sticking out of your backpack for? Are you an alchemist? That's so cool!\n\nWhen I grow up, I want to be an alchemist too. Daddy won't let me play with any of his herbs; too dangerous, he says.\n\nWell, I want to start learning now. Could you maybe get some supplies for me, pretty please?","Bring 5 Empty Vials, 5 Silverleaf, and 5 Peacebloom to the young, aspiring alchemist inside the barn of Moonbrook in Westfall.",3},
[92110]={"Wow, my very first potion! Did you know that mixing those two herbs together would change the potion to a bright red color when you first started?\n\nThat was fun, but mixing a few flowers doesn't seem like the kind of alchemy Daddy does. He uses other ingredients too.\n\nI don't know what else to use, so let's try the first thing that comes to mind! Let's see... maybe murloc eyes? That sounds so gross, but I bet something will happen.","Gather 3 Murloc Eyes for the young, aspiring alchemist inside the barn of Moonbrook in Westfall.",3},
[92111]={"I see you try, and try is more than most. We give you good will with time, if you do the same.\n\nEnter our den and talk to Osi. She has open paws, will give you more chance to help.","Enter Barkskin Burrow and find the furbolg they call Osi.",1},
[92171]={"To defeat Ve'han,  we require a touch of the sky. A bit of the divine, where one's upward-turned face yearns to fly.\n\nHead to the Shrine of Aviana and seek out Skylord Omnuron. As the leader of the Druids of the Talon, he can assist in adding a touch of Aviana's grace.","Travel to the Shrine of Aviana on Mount Hyjal and seek out Skylord Omnuron for aid.",1},
[92317]={"So, the hermit druid seeks a force to balance the 'life' in this magic of his? Then the answer is death, naturally. You have come to the right place for such a thing.\n\nNo doubt you've seen the undead crawling all over my domain. They are fueled by stolen power that animates them even in death.\n\nThat stolen power is exactly what is needed in this spell you speak of. Kill the undead and search through their skulls for a coalesced Drop of Stolen Life. Return it to Ketharas once you have it.","Acquire a Drop of Stolen Life from the Scourge in the ruins on Mount Hyjal, then return to Ketharas.",4},
[92329]={"There is a fel chimaera terrorizing beasts and travelers along hills. It is known to the Cenarion Circle as Ghansurok. I'll handle the aim and firing of the glaive thrower. Go to that drum by the cliff side. Let's see this blight driven from the mountain for good.\n\nI'll only have a chance of shooting it down if you can draw its attention. Once you have the beast by the ridge, find some place to hide!\n\nYes, I promise I have a full bag of maple seeds!","Walk to the ridge south of Kaylaena's workshop and find a way to make a loud distracting commotion to draw the chimaera Ghansurok in range to be attacked.",6},
[92344]={"The burrow you speak of is a tunnel to Blackmaw Hold. In the past, the furbolg have guarded it fiercely, making it inaccessible to outsiders. With this satyr situation, however, we can get inside.\n\nSo close to Nordrassil, there would be actively growing roots. Older roots can be seen on the world's surface, but newer ones can only be found deep underground. Little is known of their magical properties.\n\nIf you were to bring me some samples to study, the Cenarion Circle would be in your debt.","Gather 10 Nordrassil Root Caps inside Blackmaw Hold for Mathrengyl Bearwalker in Darnassus.",5},
[92401]={"It's my husband Edward...\n\nHe has not returned from his weekly journey to the graveyard in the Lordaeron ruins. Our son was lost when Arthas razed the city, and my dear Edward is still filled with guilt and sorrow that we never found his body. I've tried to warn him against searching those overrun ruins, but he refuses to give up. I try not to worry, but it's been days.\n\nThere are things there I cannot contend with but if you are willing, I need to know the fate of my husband.","Investigate the disappearance of Edward Heartweaver in the Ruins of Lordaeron.",6},
[92415]={"<A torn and stained bundle of parchment has barely survived the undead trodden grounds of the graveyard. It mentions a missing child of the Heartweaver family. Perhaps the orphan matron in Stormwind City will know more.>","Bring the Blood-Stained Letter to Orphan Matron Nightingale in Stormwind City.",7},
[92421]={"As a paladin of the Forsaken, it is my duty to exact the will of our Dark Lady while tending to our people's needs. We are fortunate with an opportunity to accomplish both.\n\nAbove the Undercity, the scourge still roam unchecked in great numbers. Our forces dwindle trying to reclaim our land, and decaying flesh cannot be reknit. Not without replacements.\n\nWould that our glorious captain Garek Bandarion still be with us, I know what he would wish. To finish what he started and heal our kin. For Lordaeron!","Collect $1oa Intact Limbs within The Ruins of Lordaeron for Morbin Lightbane in the Undercity.",6},
[92422]={"Reports have come in from the Lordamere Overlook deep within the Ruins of Lordaeron. An unholy fog has taken over the streets and graveyard, affording the scourge up there some measure of stealth. \n\nOur scouts indicate they're being conjured by a new power within their ranks, a necromancer known as Rath'mael. We do not have the luxury of waiting this one out, $n.\n\nIf you have allies, summon them and their aid to the Forsaken. Drive this creature out of our lands.","Kill Rath'mael in the Ruins of Lordaeron for Deathguard Kristof in Brill.",6},
[92432]={"I bring ill tidings from Dalaran. Something has disrupted our leylines, causing erratic and destructive behavior from our constructs in the city.\n\nWe know not yet what is causing this mayhem. The high council has ordered us to keep this matter private so as to not bring shame to our order. But we cannot keep up this charade forever. The city is being overrun as we speak!\n\nArchmage Modera has dispatched me to solicit outside aid. Seek her image out near Dalaran beside Lordamere Lake.","Report to the Image of Archmage Modera near the City of Dalaran.",2},
[92433]={"Hey! I'm pretty busy trying to turn these scraps into something edible. You wanna help out? I could really use some more variety for this meal! It sure would be nice to have something different on the menu.\n\nThere's a goblin in Everlook who has this recipe for Savory Stag Sliders... perfect for tiny hands like mine. If you could cook up some of those, that would be great! You can get stag meat from the stags here on the mountain.","Bring $1oa Savory Stag Sliders to Hnaz Blunderflame in Elderwild.",3},
[92446]={"South of here, among da forests where I sometimes hunt, dere is a great and cunning bear. We call him Head Scratcher, as his paws have caught more dan one unsuspecting villager. He ambushes hunters who are returning with prey, striking da heads by surprise and knocking dem unconscious, then stealing da catch and running back into da forest.\n\nHe is wise to me, he knows dat I track him. But he may not know your scent yet.\n\nTake dis carcass and lure him out. Finish him and bring back his claws.","Take the rabbit carcass into the woods to the south, lure out Head Scratcher, defeat him, and bring his claws back to Zet'gan.",6},
[92456]={"If you're going to bother me you can at least make yourself useful. I have an errand I need run.\n\nFor a city of mages, Dalaran has a surprising interest in botany. The Kirin Tor keep to themselves, but I would love a sample of their mana-infused vegetation.\n\nYou're clearly someone who is comfortable being where people don't want you, maybe you could find a way into the city. If you do, bring me back whatever is growing in their central garden.","Collect a Fel Infused Blossom from the City of Dalaran for Shylamiir in Stormwind City.",7},
[92457]={"The breach has affected many of our factotums and enchantments throughout the city, including many that are seeing to our defenses. This fragmented arcane energy has spoken to rogue elementals who seek to saturate themselves in this free flowing magic.\n\nWhile we are busy tending to the wards and other major incidents, it would be a favor to the Kirin Tor if you could cull this elemental throng.","Defeat $1oa Seeking Remnants, $2oa Saturated Remnants, and $3oa Mana Echoes inside the City of Dalaran for Archmage Modera outside of Dalaran.",7},
[92458]={"Whatever disturbed the leylines, it started at the top of the Violet Citadel. A thunderous crash rang out from the parlors above, and now we are overrun with rampant arcane power. It's taking all we have just to keep the wards in place.\n\nWe cannot afford to stall any longer. We need help.\n\nThe Kirin Tor are busy inside, but you will still need a less public approach to gain entry. Take this key and meet me in the citadel once you've made your way into the city. We must put an end to this disruption.","Collect the Arcane Mote for the Image of Archmage Modera near the City of Dalaran.",7},
[92460]={"Look at you, bright eyed and ready for adventure! We need all the help we can get here in Thendal Village and your arrival is most welcome. I imagine you are brimming with nerves for what is to come. After all, you only get to come of age once in a lifetime.\n\nGo, seek out our village leader Rorian the Dayseeker at the entrance to the greatfather tree just west of here. He will get you started on your journey.","Speak with Rorian the Dayseeker in Thendal Grove.",3},
[92461]={"We live in times of great uncertainty for our people. We face unprecedented challenges that may require bold solutions, but we also must contend with the ordinary and mundane here in Thendal Grove. Take, for example, the recent unsustainable rise in the vuldren population.\n\nThe vuldren are a vital part of our ecosystem. However, imbalances must be corrected to maintain the delicate harmony that all creatures in Thendal Grove share.\n\nHead east and cull some of the vuldren there.","Slay 8 Vuldren Juveniles in Thendal Grove.",5},
[92463]={"If the forest is as thick with these insects as it sounds, simply killing the workers won't be enough.\n\nGo deeper into the forest and find the queen. She'll be close to the hive and surrounded by bigger and more aggressive soldiers, so be careful.\n\nPut her down and return here when it's done. That'll be one less problem to think about around here.","Destroy the Cirrusfly Queen in Thendal Grove.",6},
[92464]={"Ever since our elemental benefactors left us, it seems that we are simply moving from one unrest to another. The problem we face now is that the manifestations of the winds near the standing stones to the northeast are agitated.\n\nNot truly self-aware like the sentient wind spirits that once lived here, these simple sprites respond in kind to forces, emotions, and intentions of the creatures around them. \n\nMy apprentice Yala Windwatcher went to observe them. Seek her out and discover what she's learned.","Speak to Yala Windwatcher in Thendal Grove.",1},
[92466]={"While we owe much of our prosperity to the elements of wind, the path we walk requires that we obey the call of all four of the primary elements and undertake a trial for each. Before you begin your first trial in earnest however, you must prove the strength of your resolve.\n\nTravel to the standing stones to the east. A force of Al'Aketh converts has been spotted there and they must be driven off. Confront the cultists there and bring me one of their signets as proof of your deeds.","Bring a Signet of Akir to Windshaper Boro.",4},
[92467]={"A sapta is a drink created to bind our spirits to the elements. Fused with magic, the potion will allow the strong willed to see the elements as no one else can. Your spirit will be connected to the element the sapta was created for, and only a select few shaman know the recipe.$B$BThe sapta is always drunk in a sacred place, and never anywhere else--remember that.$B$BSeek out the Rise of Spirits up the pass east of here. Drink your sapta there, and... well, you will see what you need to see.","Find the Rise of Spirits and drink the Earth Sapta.",3},
[92469]={"You've done enough here, $c. I'll stay and clean up any stragglers down there.\n\nHead back to the Village and tell Rorian about the cult's presence. He will not be pleased.","Bring word of the Al'Aketh to Rorian the Dayseeker in Thendal Grove.",1},
[92471]={"You may not realize this but everything you've done has been a trial of sorts. A test for what is to come for you. It's a big island out there, and Zephras needs spirited young adventurers such as yourself if we are to survive the trials our people face.\n\nThe one called Aetheen of the Gales is one of the leaders of our people here on Zephras Isle, and she has been watching you. She has a task that you must complete. Speak with her to learn more.","Speak with Aetheen of the Gales in Thendal Grove.",1},
[92472]={"One of the most pervasive threats on Zephras Isle is the Al'Aketh Cult. They are religious zealots devoted to the worship of the supposed elemental ruler of Skywall, Al'Akir the Windlord. They are brutal, single-minded, and their power and ambitions are growing more deadly by the day.\n\nYour path will soon take you to Shen'dar Village to the south. Present yourself to Constable Aonda when you arrive. The cult threatens Shen'dar and they are in need of aid. Tell Aonda that I sent you.","Report to Constable Aonda in Shen'dar Village.",3},
[92473]={"The ursera den to the southwest is rapidly becoming a problem. Just last week the rangers had to kill an adolescent ursera who wandered too close to the village and attempted to attack a boy playing near the base of the elder tree in the center of the village.\n\nWe were fortunate that the boy escaped with his life. Hunger and desperation makes these beasts too dangerous to be left unchecked. Go south and put the scrawniest among the ursera down. Bring me their claws as proof when it is done.","Collect 6 Scrawny Ursera Claws from Scrawny Ursera in Thendal Grove.",5},
[92479]={"I was asked to bring this to your attention as soon as you returned from the kobold camps, $n. It appears to be a letter sealed with the mark of Tordrin Stemblade, our local hunter trainer. Take a moment to read it before you go about any other business here in the Abbey.","Read the Scribbled Letter and speak to Tordrin Stemblade in Northshire Abbey.",3},
[92480]={"The cultist you just killed dropped what appears to be orders from a high priestess of the Cult of Al'Akir. It makes mention of a spy in Shen'dar Village and cult operations in a place called Falaath Village. The authorities at Shen'dar Village will want to learn of this.","Bring the Orders from the High Priestess to Shen'Dar Village and present it to whomever is in charge there.",3},
[92484]={"While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident Shaman trainer--Windshaper Boro--left this recall crystal for you. Please examine it, then speak with Boro just over yonder near the center of the village.","Examine the Humming Recall Crystal then speak with Windshaper Boro in Thendal Grove.",3},
[92485]={"While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident druid trainer--Xyton Silverwind--left this note for you. Read it as soon as you can, and then seek out Silverwind on the ground floor of this great tree just behind me.\n\nHeed his words and his counsel, he can teach you much.","Read the Folded Parchment then speak with Xyton Silverwind in Thendal Grove.",3},
[92489]={"The Kirin Tor have long been allies of the Alliance. With the destruction of their city at the hands of the arch demon Archimonde, the once proud city of mages has now become reclusive and distrusting of outsiders.\n\nIn recent years they have begun reconstruction efforts to bring the city of Dalaran back to its former glory. However, reports show they are struggling to contain an outbreak of wayward arcane energies.\n\nWe must help them disperse these attacks lest we lose one of our most powerful allies.","Slay the Mana Elemental in the City of Dalaran for High Sorcerer Andromath in Stormwind City.",7},
[92514]={"You've got that \"Windshaper\" air about you. Something about how I can feel a tiny bit of static on my skin when near someone spirit-touched that gives it away. Before I properly put you to work around here, you should check in with our resident Windshaper elder, Illaya Amberwind. She's just outside, near the center of town.\n\nOh, and check in with Coriella Calmbreeze as well, she runs the local inn and can provide lodging and supplies, should you need them.","Speak with Illaya Amberwind and Coriella Calmbreeze in Shen'dar Village.",2},
[92519]={"Apothecary Jorell was supposed to bring us a case of antidotes and elixirs days ago, but we're still empty handed. That fool has probably poisoned himself again by brewing in that poorly-ventilated shack he calls his lab.\n\nIf you want to further help our ward, you would be a far more reliable individual for this job.\n\nFollow the road to Go'shek farm, south and a bit west of here. You'll likely find it packed and ready to go, with Jorell either missing or unconcerned with his obligations.","Pick up a case of Packaged Tonics at Jorell's lab in Go'shek Farm and return to Doctor Gregory Victor in Hammerfall.",5},
[92521]={"You know I'm a warlock, right? Now reduced to squalor and meat-cutting, but once a mighty magician!\n\nMy imp keeps wandering off and while I could just call him back, I'm kinda curious about what he's doing. He's been sneaking off to talk to a bound satyr at a tower to the southeast of here. If you wouldn't mind, I'd like to know what they're talking about.\n\nI'm sure it's nothing to worry about, but you can never tell with demons, right?","Spy on Hnaz's imp at the tower with the captive satyr.",0},
[92528]={"The faithful of Al'Akir grow ever stronger with each eager new recruit like yourself. As you can see, our strength gives form to the storm itself!\n\nNormally I'd send you straight to Skypriest Aanders for assessment, but he is occupied at present receiving a guest at the inn on the north side of town. Please avoid that place for now. An unshaven recruit like yourself in the presence of such a guest would be inappropriate.\n\nFor now, just don't get in anyone's way.","Look around Falaath Village to learn about the cult's intentions in the Shen'dar Highlands.",3},
[92550]={"Our best defense here might just be a strong offense. The advantage we now have is that we expect an attack is coming. What they won't expect is for us to hit them first.\n\nI've already asked a lot of you, but please head back over to Falaath Village. Kill as many cultists as you can and if you can get close enough, kill the commander and bring me his head. I'll stay here and organize the citizens and our few peacekeepers to prepare a defense... just in case you don't return.","Travel to the ruins of Falaath Village and slay 6 Al'Aketh Stormcallers, 4 Living Lightning and take the head of Commander Cyclas.",5},
[92551]={"I overheard you might be going to Falaath Village? While you are there, please keep an eye out for our stolen supply caches.\n\nThe Al'Aketh have been raiding our supply caravans carrying various goods such as food and windstones to and from the lowlands for months. They've been blaming the bandits, of course, but we all know that it all ends up in the same place. If there's any of that stuff left in Falaath, it would be a huge help if you could recover it.","Collect 10 packs of Stolen Shen'dar Supplies from Falaath Village in the Shen'dar Highlands.",4},
[92579]={"For now it seems the pylon and the village are safe, so I'd like you to deliver this report to Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar, at the southeastern edge of the island. Valennia is the leader of the peacekeepers on the island and she needs to know what happened here.\n\nThe cult is expanding rapidly and the peacekeepers have avoided direct conflict until now, but those days are over. Valanaar will need to be ready for a fight.\n\nAt any rate, thank you. You'll always have friends in Shen'dar, $n.","Deliver Aonda's Written Report to Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar.",2},
[92592]={"We've tried to get off da mountain, but da Scourge always stop us. A powerful lich reanimates da remains of da ones we destroy and sends dem against us again. Dat lich is da reason we can't win!\n\nDa lich has a pile of bones dat it uses to rebuild skeletons. Take dis torch, go to da ruins, and burn da bone pile. Da lich be sure to respond.\n\nBring me its amulet, and we destroy it and get rid of it for good!","Use the Survivor's Torch on the Bone Pile, then collect the Reanimator's Amulet.",5},
[92594]={"While you're traveling around the mountain, I can't resist asking for another small favor...\n\nDid you see all those fel shrubberies and plants littering the hills down below? It turns out they burn rather well, which is both good, and bad. Handy for feeding into a small furnace, but also a risk when it twists together and binds up gears...or bootstraps!\n\nThin their numbers on your way down, and I'll pick up the weeds myself once they've dried out.","Destroy $1oa Tainted Shrubbery for Kaylaena Springwhisper at the workshop in the Tainted Foothills.",4},
[92596]={"The aura of arcane energy that surrounds you is strong, even though you are not initiated as a mage. I am quite sure that you are going to be a capable adventurer, and your connection with our ancient magic will only ever be a boon to you even if you were to never utter a single word of power in spellcasting.\n\nCome, let us sit and speak some on my order, the nature of the arcane here on Zephras, and the plight of our people.","Have a seat and speak with Rathiril Sunlance.",2},
[92609]={"We been tryin' ta leave many a time, but keep gettin' pulled back ta defend our brothas an' sistas. Wit our defenses dwindlin', it's time we get ta restockin'.\n\nToday we be needin' arrows. Lots an' lots o' dem.\n\nFind dem big, beautiful birds and bring us back dem long feathers for da straight shootin' arrows.","Gather $1oa Hyjal Owl Feathers for Zet'gan.",5},
[92643]={"There is a turncoat amongst the Al'Aketh. They claim to know the cult's true intentions for the island and want to come in, but will only do so with assurances of protection.\n\nThis defector is hiding at a secluded residence just northwest of Valanaar inside the highlands. I need someone who can discreetly go there, find the traitor, and escort him back to us. This might be a trap, but if this information is as important as this traitor claims, it's worth some risk.","Find the cultist turncoat at the house just inside the highlands northwest of Valanaar.",4},
[92645]={"This attack is going to be hard to repel unless we can take out the cult commander. Belguilos \"the Breaker\" they call her, and she's a veritable terror. She used to be a peacekeeper before the cult got out of control, and even then she was... off. As a cultist I can only imagine how much worse she could be now.\n\nI might just be sending you to your death, but someone needs to take Belguilos out if we are going to survive here. You can find her at the villa at the hill's base. Good luck, $c.","Slay Commander Belguilos in the Gustberry Lowlands.",4},
[92646]={"Lorthuna fled up to the spires above using some sort of portal. Ayessa and Elaadrin went in after her. That was just a few moments ago.\n\nI'm afraid I took one too many hits and this is where I stay. Go through the portal, find Ayessa and help them stop Lorthuna.\n\nUnless that help that Elaadrin and Ayessa said they sent for arrives soon, you are on your own from here. Good luck, $c.","Take the portal to the Rohashi Spires overhead and join Elaadrin Evengale and Ayessa Dawnsinger in their confrontation with the High Priestess Lorthuna.",3},
[92679]={"H--Hello, stranger. You have the look of a capable adventurer about you. I...\n\n<The Skyborne man winces, clearly suffering terrible pain>\n\n...I was wondering if you were seeking employment? I came here to Valanaar to recruit fighters to help save my farm. If you are interested, please go find my wife Aamelia Windfield at our orchard to the west of Valanaar, in the lowlands.","Listen to what Alvarion Windfield has to say and find Aamelia Windfield at the Windfield Orchard.",3},
[92682]={"Oh, so you've got more courage than sense, then? Fine, I won't argue.\n\nFerauu and his goons aren't due to pick up their take of the harvest just yet, so I'm going to put you to work for your meals until they arrive.\n\nHead outside and gather today's batch of stormapples for me. Oh, and the bandits lurking around the stormapple trees... They think they are sneaky. They aren't. Kill them for me. \n\nLet's see what you've got in a fight.","Gather 10 Ripe Stormapples and slay 5 Hungry Bandits at the Windfield Orchard.",5},
[92684]={"As if the harvest wasn't light enough this year already, the galestriders in the area have been getting into the orchard and stealing my stormapples. Think you can head out to the fields and cull them for me?\n\nTake care though stranger, these lowlands galestriders are bigger and angrier than the highlands variety. Watch yourself. A well-timed kick is all it takes to put you down for good if you aren't paying attention.\n\nBring me some of their meat and I can make us a hot meal with it as well.","Gather 7 Lowlands Galestrider Tenderloins from the Ornery Galestriders found throughout the Gustberry Lowlands.",4},
[92685]={"The bandits have camps all over and there's a small one in the hills just north of here. Head up there and start cracking skulls. If we can catch them off guard and take them out before they come for us, we might just even the odds enough to stand a chance.\n\nBring me their masks. The bloodier the better.","Loot 7 Blood-Stained Bandit Masks from Highwayman Bandits in the Gustberry Lowlands.",5},
[92700]={"Now that you've arrived in Valanaar, you'll likely want to check in with the other members of the Windshapers here. The current Grand Skyseer and her people operate out of the lodge near the center of Valanaar.\n\nYou should also be aware, the Windshapers and High Order don't get along very well in these parts. Be careful and give the High Order a good, wide berth. We've got enough to worry about with the cult, I won't tolerate faction violence in the streets of Valanaar.","Find Ayessa Dawnsinger in Valanaar.",1},
[92706]={"Calling all anglers!\n\nA giant shark has been circling the waters near the shipping dock, attacking sailors and small boats. Dockworkers have given it the nickname \"Bruuz\". A hefty reward will be given to whoever brings me its fin!\n\n-- Gazlowe","Bring Bruuz's Dorsal Fin to Gazlowe in Ratchet.",6},
[92707]={"Wrenched from its hulking corpse, the goliath's bracers are massive. Your whole arm, up to the shoulder, can fit through one without touching the sides.\n\nYou should bring these back to Hammerfall, as a warning. Drum Fel ought to know what he's up against.","Bring the Goliath's Wristguards to Drum Fel in Hammerfall.",6},
[92708]={"The Windshapers have been hard at work trying to respond to the current crisis on Zephras Isle. We have made several surprising discoveries in our search for the missing wind spirits, and we are developing a plan of action that could help us gain the means to save the island.\n\nWe'll need strong young adventurers like yourself for this to work however. Please, if you have a moment, let us speak on this further.","Listen to what Ayessa Dawnsinger has to say.",1},
[92709]={"Your highborne lineage shines as clearly in your eyes as the sky above. You are one of us, and it's youths like yourself that will help us save our home. But first, let me tell you more of our mission and plans here on Zephras... and beyond.","Listen to what Elaadrin Evengale in Valanaar has to say.",1},
[92742]={"We must determine the source and nature of the poison corrupting this land. Let us begin with the groundwater under the farms in the area.\n\nGo to the Jansen Stead in the north and the Molsen Farm northwest of here, and collect samples from the wells there.","Use the Well Water Sample Kit to collect samples from the wells at the Jansen Stead and the Molsen Farm.",3},
[92748]={"The supplies you found point to a massive industrial operation somewhere in the Deadmines. There's no question that this is the source of the toxins plaguing the farmland of Westfall. We need to stop it, quickly.\n\nWhatever's down there will be difficult to destroy. Go to the Dwarven District of Stormwind, and find an engineer who can supply us with some explosives.","Travel to the Dwarven District in Stormwind and find an engineer who can help.",3},
[92750]={"I assume you want a \"controlled\" explosion? Not as much fun, but a good choice if you want to keep all your limbs.\nI'm afraid I don't have a remote detonator--why don't you go check with the sneaky folks down at Stormwind Intelligence? They should be able to find us something.","Talk to someone in Stormwind Intelligence about acquiring a remote detonator.",1},
[92752]={"That's it--the bomb's ready to go! Careful with that detonator, now.","Return to Alba Fairmoon in Westfall.",3},
[92753]={"The source of the poison is likely a large metallurgical forge of some kind. Find a way into the Deadmines and locate the forge, then place the explosives.\nI will wait for you in the hills behind Moonbrook. Once you return, we can detonate the explosives. Hopefully, with the forge gone, the land can begin to heal.","Find the forge hidden in the Deadmines, and plant the Extra-Destructive Explosives nearby. Then, meet up with Alba Fairmoon at the Deadmines exit.",5},
[92814]={"My mate, Halea, is tasked with ensuring our armaments are empowered with appropriate magical energy.\n\nThe whole concept of enchanting is far beyond my understanding, but as the centaur whose job is to keep our village well supplied and equipped, I know that Halea is often behind on her duties--to no fault of her own.\n\nI would like to gift her some simple clothes to practice her craft on. I see some adventurers wandering through sandstorms with simple facemasks. Could you get me a few of those?","Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring a White Bandit Mask to Molkar in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.",4},
[92817]={"Convincing my Gelkis clanmates to put on armor is nigh impossible, despite the numerous losses we have suffered with blades or bolts through the chest.\n\nI have been tasked with designing a vest that offers some reasonable protection, without the supposed 'itchiness' that they complain about. Supplies are scarce, so I dare not waste precious leather on junk.\n\nOutsider, would you bring me a harness fit to a brutish centaur? I would like to learn from your technique.","Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring a Barbaric Harness to Talra in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.",4},
[92819]={"We are almost finished. Use the detonator, and end this.","Use the detonator.",1},
[92834]={"When the cult began their campaign of violence, the Peacekeepers and Windshapers responded with posturing. I saw this as foolish escalation so I advocated for peaceful dialogue. Yesterday I dispatched my friend Belathaan Brightwish to the Shrine of Akir, hoping to establish that dialogue.\n\nA box just arrived containing Belathaan's tongue, dipped in silver pigment. \n\nIt's clear to me now that there is no reasoning with the cult. Kill any cultists you see, and bring me the prayer charms that they carry.","Collect 10 Al'Aketh Windstone Charms from Al'Aketh cultists found north of Valanaar at the Gustberry Fields or Shrine of Akir.",5},
[92840]={"Fillion was sent to the Overlook Standing Stones with a special device used to measure and study the elemental energy there.\n\nTake this--an Index Esoteria--and use it to extract data from the massive windstone formations that form there. Be on your guard however, as the Windshapers are likely to be jealously guarding this site now.\n\nShould any attempt to obstruct you, well... do what you need to do. I have no more patience for their interference.","Take the Index Esoteria to the Overlook Standing Stones in Shen'dar Highlands and use it on the Windstone Formations in the area to gather data.",5},
[92859]={"Folks have been trying to get onto Mount Hyjal since the end of the war, but there's one big problem... all the demons in Darkwhisper Gorge!\n\nI think I have the solution. A concoction made from locally-sourced ingredients might be able to make the drinker blend in with the Winterspring surroundings so that creatures here can't see you as easily.\n\nI'd love to test this theory, if you're game for bringing me a few small things!","Bring $1oa Winterspring Chimaera Fur and $2oa Winterspring Owl Feathers to Evie Whirlbrew.",3},
[92860]={"The High Order have done our best to avoid direct conflict with the cult, but that is clearly no longer an option. Their hostility has been clearly demonstrated, and now there are rumors of larger-scale cult movements around the island. They are clearly gearing up for something and whatever it is can't be good for the people of Zephras.\n\nReport to Valennia Stormfist and inform her that the High Order offers our full support in Valanaar's efforts against the Al'Aketh, should the need arise.","Report to Valennia Stormfist and let her know that the High Order is with them in their fight against the Al'Aketh.",2},
[92881]={"The attacks on both the western and eastern watchtowers are not a coincidence. Based on what you told us about what occurred at the western watchtower with that skypriest, our best guess is that the cult is trying to do something to the anchor pylons.\n\nPlease speak with High Elder Shadowsong. He will tell you about a lead that could prove to be promising.","Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",1},
[92893]={"As you tread further into the Valley of Bones, you will find Gelkis wanderers that dared to enter our territory. I instructed they be kept alive so they could feed the bone worms burrowing about, but they seem uninterested in their prey being alive.\n\nThis task is simple. Find the prisoners, then snuff out their life. Don't give them a brief glimmer of hope for freedom.","Maintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and slay $1oa Gelkis Captives scattered around the Valley of Bones. Return to Orgrul after the task is complete.",4},
[92894]={"I can see the excitement in your eyes, outsider. Do you grasp the potential of necromancy yet?\n\nOf course you do. And that is why I am ordering you to hone your skills further.\n\nAs you venture deeper into the Valley of Bones, you will see the remains of failed attempts at raising the dead. Gelkis attempts, no doubt. Hardly able to claw out from the dirt. Funny, were it not so pathetic.\n\nI have imbued your staff with greater power. Use this to grow our army, and crush the ones that fight back!","Maintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and use the Enhanced Necromancy Staff to fully raise undead that are struggling to emerge throughout the Valley of Bones. Return to Orgrul once the Magram army has grown.",4},
[92910]={"The part you managed to salvage from the harvester appears mostly intact. Someone interested in harvest golems may want to see it.","Bring the Precessive Autocognition Assembly to Ozwin Ironsprocket at Saldean's Farm.",4},
[92911]={"I see... this gives me some insight into what makes those monsters tick. I have an idea how we could override their systems, at least momentarily.\n\nI'll continue tinkering with the assembly you brought me. In the meantime, could you scrounge up some parts for the device?","Ozwin Ironsprocket at Saldean's Farm wants you to bring him 8 Golem Isosprings, 4 Copper Modulators, and a Crude Scope.",5},
[93016]={"You will have to forgive me for sending you on such a series of tasks without providing any context. I hadn't considered how suspicious this may have seemed, more so now that the skies have taken on such a dramatic appearance.\n\nI will gladly answer your questions.","Speak with Mordent Evenshade in Shen'dralas for information about the crystals you repaired.",1},
[93030]={"I once was a knight like you--bound to the service of the light. Then, I died. It seems that we both have that much in common.\n\nUnlike you, however, I am bound to this place by a purpose unfinished, an oath unfulfilled. If you would listen, I would tell you of my quest... and my failure.","Speak with the Knight of Mourning to learn more about his unfinished quest.",1},
[93041]={"This discovery is devastating for our clan, but it is in our best interest to keep this only to those who need to know. Uthek is one such person who needs to be aware of what is going on here. I suspect she will know how to proceed.\n\nTake this to show her. For good measure, we should also bring evidence of the necromancy itself to her. Find a skull that looks recently cursed. I suspect they may be hoarding them in the maws of one of the goliath's skeletons.","Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis Clan, and bring an Accursed Skull and Gelkis Necromantic Garb to Uthek the Wise in Gelkis Village.",2},
[93044]={"When you return to Nerlokh in the Valley of Bones, it will not be empty-handed.\n\nGo inside the cave at the heart of our village and seek out Mulara. Ask for Tears of Theradras on my behalf. Our supply is low, but it is our best hope against the Magram's foul necromancy!\n\nI will prepare a ritual. We will create a weapon to disrupt their spells.","Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring Tears of Theradras back to Uthek the Wise in Gelkis Village.",4},
[93066]={"On the other side of the valley, we have established a small foothold to prepare to march into the forest nearby. Before you head straight there, I want you to deal with a recent Bristleback intrusion along the way. They seem to have arrived right around the same time we did, but managed to secure an artifact from the nearby temple that has kept us at bay.\n\nThis task is simple. Look for the thorns and the pigs. Kill a bunch, indiscriminately. Then report to Hagiak at the camp I mentioned.","Maintain your reputation with the Magram, and slay quilboar at Bristleback Retreat. Then report to Hagiak at the Magram Front on the other side of Valley of Bones in Desolace.",5},
[93089]={"Please extend my thanks to Elaadrin for all that the High Order and your new friends from this \"Kirin Tor\" have done for Zephras Isle. I'm aware of the High Order's plans to leave the island, and your order has my blessing and well-wishes in this expedition.\n\nI can only hope that whatever arcane solution the High Order finds can truly provide us with the stability we've lacked these past years. If you plan to go with them... well, this mission will be all the stronger for it.\n\nWinds be with you, $n.","Speak with Elaadrin Evengale when you are prepared to leave Zephras Isle.",1},
[93128]={"As much as I would like Uthek or Khan Shaka to give the order, I fear our window of opportunity is short. Too short to consult those at Gelkis Village.\n\nI believe with the situation unfolding here at the Valley of Bones that the Magram have left Khan Jehn with minimal defenses. If there was ever a time to attack another clan's Khan, it is now.\n\nBut $n, a Khan is not to be trifled with, least of all Jehn. If you are brave enough to make your move, you must be swift but do not underestimate him.","Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and slay Khan Jhen at Magram Village. Once you have succeeded, report to Uthek the Wise in Gelkis Village in Desolace.",5},
[93159]={"Uh, um... h-hello, I mean to say, hi! Greetings, even! I'm sorry... it's um, been so long since I've actually spoken to another person. I'm afraid I'm a bit rusty at this.\n\n<The strange hooded figure shifts uncomfortably before you.>\n\nSo er, um... how is your day going?","Speak with the Strange Hermit in the Shadowgale Forest and learn more about him.",2},
[93160]={"I do appreciate you stopping by to talk with me! I-If you do want to help out, I could use a bit of help gathering up acorns from the forest floor. I've gathered most of the ones close by but there sure are a lot of raptor-bird things in the forest. It's dangerous out there and I'd rather not become a giant bird's lunch!\n\nSo if you want, you could maybe gather them for me? I'll make us something tasty if you do!","Gather $1oa Shadowgale Acorns in Shadowgale Forest.",4},
[93161]={"In the faint illumination of your torchlight, you can make out a small glint of metal. Upon further inspection, it's clear that this is the broken hilt of an ancient sword.\n\nDespite missing a blade, you can clearly see that this hilt is a product of masterful workmanship. This is a precious heirloom, and there may be those who are interested to learn more about this.","Find someone who would be interested in the Ancient Hilt you found in the ruins of Ban'aethal.",0},
[93165]={"The Al'Aketh have visited great tragedy upon our enclave, and blood must be repaid with blood.\n\nI have an offer for you, stranger. Should you find conflict with these accursed cultists, bring me the ears of those you kill. I will reward you for each that you return with in both coin and, in time, access to the Nightclaw's secrets should you prove yourself to be a true friend.","Collect $1oa Al'Aketh Cultist's Ears from the Al'Aketh cultists in Shadowgale Forest, the Shrine of Akir, or Gustberry Lowlands.",5},
[93176]={"Admiring my little menagerie, are you? They are my un-life's work. I've spent countless hours studying them: their anatomy, their diets, even their social rituals.\n\nDo you wish to join me in the hobby? Here, take this package. The notes and materials contained within should get you started. If you lose it, you'll have to purchase another one from me for a small fee.","Use the items contained in the Entomology Starter Kit to find and catch an Arbor Tarantula, Hay Weevil Specimen, and a Flesh Picker.",5},
[93196]={"The leader of our clan, Khan Jehn, was slain by a band of outsiders much like you. They were acting on behalf of the Gelkis Clan.\n\nYou can stop feigning your surprise. An assault on Magram Village while our attention was elsewhere is a predictable war strategy, especially for the Gelkis.\n\nDo you know why I am showing no rage or remorse, outsider?\n\n<Orgrul hands you a familiar weapon, imbued with even greater power than the last time you held it.>\n\nThis is why.","Maintain your reputation with the Magram and perform a necromancy ritual to resurrect Khan Jehn. The ritual site can be found in a tent at the central lake of Magram Village.",5},
[93224]={"It likely comes as no surprise to you that both of the centaur clans are hesitant to accept aid from anyone outside of their clan. This is especially true for folks like you and me - you know, non-centaurs.\n\nOne thing we all have in common is an understanding that money is power, and we have learned that the local centaur barter with carved wood. If you bring me a few samples of their designs, I can put in a rush order for similar etchings. Perhaps we can buy ourselves an advantage.","Acquire $1oa Carved Centaur Totems by slaying centaur of any clan throughout Desolace, then return them to Captain Pentigast at Nijel's Point.",4},
[93226]={"Siding with the Magram would be my choice. There is no question that they are the dominant clan in the present day, regardless of their previous struggles. I have heard reports that they are brutally hostile against the Gelkis.\n\nI sympathize with both warring clans and especially the Gelkis, but this is their war; not ours. We ought to side with the faction that poses the least risk to our cause. I believe that to be the Magram.\n\nBring this to their quartermaster in Magram Village to the southeast.","Bring the Totem Tote to the Magram Quartermaster at Magram Village in the Desolace to significantly increase your reputation with that clan. You must be of at least Neutral standing with the Magram Clan Centaur.",1},
[93227]={"At first glance, I would wager that the Gelkis are struggling. Their numbers are far fewer than the Magram, and I rarely hear of them stomping around from our scouts.\n\nNonetheless, they are one of the dominant clans in the Desolace and survive to this day. They must be doing something right.\n\nIf you want to make peace with the Gelkis, take this tote of totems with you to Gelkis Village far to the southwest. Primitive as they may be, they are likely to have a treasurer of some kind.","Bring the Totem Tote to the Gelkis Quartermaster at Gelkis Village in the Desolace to significantly increase your reputation with that clan. You must be of at least Neutral standing with the Gelkis Clan Centaur.",1},
[93269]={"Now that you've recovered all the mail, you can take it all back with you to Mount Hyjal!\n\nShould be no problem, right?","Take mail from Everlook up to Innkeeper Sebelia on the summit of Mount Hyjal.",1},
[93317]={"Are you familiar with Windsong Crawlers? You see, these crabs are native only to Windsong Lake here on Zephras, and they are only able to be harvested a few weeks of the year.\n\nWith all of the cult activity of late, I've not been able to get out to the lake to harvest them, and our window is rapidly closing. I'd be appreciative if you could go and gather some for me. They can generally be found along the shorelines around the lake and in rivers.\n\nDo be careful though, they are meaner than they look!","Collect 6 pieces of Windsong Crawler Meat.",4},
[93318]={"By order of Constable Aonda of the Peacekeepers, a bounty is hereby placed upon the scourge of the highlands, Vulgara the Insatiable. Last spotted on a hilltop rise just southwest of Shen'dar Village, the winged vuldren terror is highly dangerous and should be approached with caution.\n\nDeliver the beast's head to Danarii Bellowveil to receive your reward.","Kill Vulgara the Insatiable in the Shen'dar Highlands and bring her head to Danarii Bellowveil.",5},
[93320]={"I've just received word that the cult is attacking the pylon watchtower just outside of town! I've sent the few extra peacekeepers we have here to try and break through the enemy back line to relieve the defenders, but any additional help could mean the difference between our people there living or dying.\n\nPlease leave immediately for the east watchtower and provide whatever aid you can.\n\nMy lieutenant Yorana Windyreed led the relief force. If she still lives she can tell you how best to help.","Report to Yorana Windyreed at the eastern watchtower in the Gustberry Lowlands.",3},
[93362]={"Please spare the details of how the life may have been twisted there. My heart is broken enough with the loss of my necklace.\n\nBut while I weep, the plants suffer.\n\n$n, I would like you to go back to the garden and cull some of the angered flora. Please be swift and merciful; they can feel pain, and they have been hurt enough. If you intend to go hunting for my necklace as well, I would ask you to prioritize that before visiting the gardens again... in the unlikely chance you find it.","Cull plants in the Forlorn Garden and then return to Mithera at Shen'dralas.",5},
[93394]={"I suspect your curiosity is luring you toward the grand structure now, yes? Good!\n\nThe Shen'dralar there are unlikely to welcome you with open arms, but so long as you tread respectfully, I do not think you will run into any trouble.\n\nWith any luck, my old friend Kirandis might be easy to find. Of everyone, he is the most likely to be amicable to your presence.","Locate Magister Kirandis inside the temple of Shen'dralas.",1},
[93404]={"I am the ancient. Towering above us. That which still burns despite many rains. I feel its flames in death. Forever burdened by my last mistake.\n\nI do not know why I am cursed to haunt this place. I do not understand why death was not the end.\n\nPlease put out the flame. Seek pristine water from a sacred ravine. Such a place exists across Mashan'she. I have heard murmurs of the place in the wind.\n\nMaraudon.","Venture to Maraudon and recover a Vial of Earth Song Water and return it to Woodwyrd at the Forlorn Gardens in Desolace.",6},
[93407]={"We need to improve our defenses here, and we lack the resources to construct fortifications. We do, however, have all of the bounty of nature.\n\nSearch the forest for thorn bushes and bring their seeds back to me. With the power of nature, we will grow our own defenses.","Find thorn seeds in the forests at the summit of Mount Hyjal and bring them back to Tiala Whitemane.",5},
[93429]={"Although they are our kin, the Lost Ones of Fallow Sanctuary have become beings of pure violence and hatred.\n\nThere can be no redemption or salvation for them. They are doomed to wander this swamp as mindless, hateful creatures for all their lives.\n\nTheir suffering must end. Someone must put them out of their misery. A grisly task, I know, but would you do it to protect those of us who remain?","Slay 10 Lost Ones in the Fallow Sanctuary.",5},
[93430]={"Now they've really done it! As if those wretches weren't already enough to deal with, one of them has stolen my lucky lure!\n\nI was just out fishing this morning, when one came up out of the muck, cut my line, and ran off with it. The thief is almost certainly one of the Lost Ones' own fishermen, hoping to use the lure themselves.\n\nWell, our supply of fish depends on that lure, so I need it back. The Lost Ones fish along the banks east of here. Find that thief, $r!","Find the Lost One Fisherman who stole Pelluk's lure, and take it back.",4},
[93444]={"The most vicious fel chimaera of Hyjal is known as Ghansurok. It likes to swoop in and prey on wildlife caught out of their burrows. Not only that, it's making hippogryph travel in and out of Hyjal more stressful than usual!\n\nFirst, hunt down one of the Nightsabers hiding in the Summit's shadows. Next, place meat from the fallen cat somewhere on the northern ridge where chimaeras feed.\n\nLure Ghansurok towards it. Slay the beast and return with its heart. Marn will study it to help heal Hyjal.","Kill a Nightsaber Guardian, then bait out and kill Ghansurok using the Nightsaber Guardian haunch on the northern ridge of the summit.\n\nReturn with the heart of the chimaera.",6},
[93464]={"Allow me to admit something, $n. While draenethyst is sacred to us, and keeps us sane, none here fully understand it.\n\nI recall a mage who once came to the Harborage, from Desolace. A human by the name of Azore. He feared the power of the draenethyst; said it shouldn't fall into the wrong hands. \n\nAt the time, we drove him away to protect what was ours. Lately, however, I find myself wondering what exactly he knew.\n\nI ask that you find this mage, $r. His knowledge could be of immense value to us.","Find the mage in Desolace who knows about the power of draenethyst.",3},
[93546]={"Finally, FINALLY I can use this anvil for something other than a monumentally heavy table. I am delighted to finally hone my craft again after centuries of missed practice.\n\nNow, you are probably thinking, \"Vindael, this sounds like you are setting the stage for another request.\" And you would be correct!\n\nI need to replenish my supply of iron, but your iron has a similar predicament to my blade. Fortunately, the solution is MUCH simpler.\n\n<He hands you a ghostly pickaxe, without a chance to refuse.>","Search for Spectral Iron Deposits around Shen'dralas and collect $1oa Spectral Iron Ore. Return to Vindael in Shen'dralas once you have found enough.",4},
[93547]={"We are constantly under threat here, both by the Blackthorne Pact and by the hostile creatures of Hyjal. But we can use the thorns to our advantage! With a little help from the power of nature, we can grow new thorn bushes to help protect our enclosure.\n\nPlant thorn seeds near the road to help create barricades by the inn, the storage tower, and the grouping of trees near the road.","Plant thorn seeds near the inn, the storage tower, and the grouping of trees at the loyalist druid camp.",2},
[93572]={"You may have brought Kum'isha a draenethyst sphere, but that only shows Kum'isha you are lucky, not skilled. If you wish to earn your reward, you will aid Kum'isha's brethren in returning home.\n\nKum'isha will use this sphere to open a rift, while other draenei will go through. Whatever dangers come out, you will fight. If any of Kum'isha's brothers and sisters are harmed, you can forget about that reward.\n\nAre you ready, $r?","Protect the draenei refugees as they pass through Kum'isha's rift to Outland. None of the refugees may die.",5},
[93584]={"The lands surrounding the Well of Eternity are overrun with followers of the Wild King. Many once stood beside us, bound by the same oaths, but their devotion has curdled into reckless zeal. They actively hinder our efforts to tend Nordrassil and protect the Well.\n\nI will not pretend this is easy, nor that my hands will be clean. Still, we cannot allow them to harm our land or strike our flank when the greater incursion begins.\n\nThin their ranks swiftly, and may Elune forgive what necessity demands.","Kill $1oa Blackthorne Adepts and $2oa Wild-branded Cultists.",5},
[93594]={"Among the treants borne of the necklace, one in particular stood above all the others to have received the gift of life and sentience. I suspect if they have fallen, he may be the only one that remains.\n\nHe spent his days tending to each and every bloom and bud, and his evenings rooted in the ground to serve as a nest for the smaller critters.\n\nIf he is alive, and I pray that to be true, then he may know what happened.\n\nI am holding out hope for my good friend, Woodwyrd.","Find Woodwyrd in the Forlorn Gardens at Shen'dralas in the Desolace.",1},
[93604]={"Big $R heard of Razorfen Downs? <Snort.> Of course not! Big place in Barrens. Lots of thorns. Can't miss it.\n\nAgamaggan died there. Important place for all quilboar. Now bristleback not allowed. Belong to sniffle-snorting Razorfen. Razorfen disrespect quilboar history!\n\nAgamaggan's blood feeds the valley. Grow thorns. BIG ones. Bigger than puny elf necklace ever could!\n\nGo to the Downs. Fetch Kog'thug blood. Stale blood from the kraul won't work. Need GOOD blood!\n\nGive blood, get necklace, win.","Venture to Razorfen Downs and acquire Virulent Blood of Agamaggan, then return it to Kog'thug the Brave at Bristleback Retreat in the Desolace. Kog'thug felt it worth reminding that the Blood of Agamaggan inside Razorfen Kraul would not be sufficient.",5},
[93609]={"<The necklace you have been seeking is at last in your possession, but unfortunately the magic contained within has been entirely depleted. While not ideal for your current situation, at least it made its acquisition from the quilboar relatively easy.\n\nIt is probably best to bring this back to Mithera.>","Bring the Forlorn Necklace to Mithera at the temple of Shen'dralas in the Desolace.",6},
[93615]={"Oh, a tasty morsel...\n\nFear not, I jest. Though I could snap your spine like a dry branch. I am a demigod of the wilds, after all.\n\nIf you would gain my favor and avoid my appetite, perhaps I could burden you with a task?\n\nMy litter of young have wandered off to entertain themselves. Little on this mountain could threaten them directly, but there are dark things afoot near the summit, and I'd leave nothing to chance.\n\nWould you check on them? In return for my not eating you, of course.","Find Shalla'kal's kittens in the wilds of Mount Hyjal.",4},
[93644]={"<Found near Shen'dralas, this dirty old tome no longer holds most of its knowledge.\n\nOf the text that remains, individual letters are difficult to distinguish from words. It may prove challenging to read at first, but one of them appears to be a surname.\n\nPerhaps its author, \"Evenshade\", may be found nearby.>","The text suggests the author of this journal may be somewhere in Shen'dralas.",5},
[93679]={"It is good to see you again, $n. I have been reading the notes you brought to us, and speaking with Onku, our eldest seer, about the matter.\n\nHe has recently been granted a vision that may lead us to the draenethyst sphere. We would like to share the revelations of that vision with you, if you'd join us for a moment?","Watch Onku's vision with Magtoor.",1},
[93680]={"The Alliance had an army of mages known as the Kirin Tor. While they were powerful, the demonic Burning Legion proved to be even more so. In one fell swoop, the arch demon Archimonde flattened their city like it was a child's plaything. Those who remained were reduced to merely dispossessed vagabonds.\n\nThat is, until they rebuilt Dalaran. And on the Dark Lady's very doorstep, no less!\n\nWhile in their camps, search for something that can get us into the city unnoticed. I must know more.","Acquire the Dalaran Sewer Key for Magus Wordeen Voidglare in Tarren Mill.",0},
[93684]={"While I know of no other settlement like ours, I have seen lost ones south of here in the Blasted Lands. They are much like the ones of Fallow Sanctuary--hostile and mindless. I assumed that was the fate which befell all of our kind there.\n\nHowever, if Onku's vision points to a lone draenei wandering a wasteland, then perhaps I was wrong.\n\nI am calling on you once again, $n. Find this draenei and aid them however you can.","Find the draenei searching for draenethyst in the Blasted Lands.",3},
[93685]={"Can your miniscule brain comprehend the rarity of a flawless sphere of draenethyst, $r? Draenei have spent lifetimes in search of just one of these crystals, only to meet horrible fates, their purpose unfulfilled.\n\nSo you stand before Kum'isha, knowing what Kum'isha has requested and still wish to assist? Very well, $r... At any time during your travels across these lands, should you find a flawless sphere of draenethyst, return it to me and I shall reward you with riches beyond your wildest dreams.","Find a Flawless Draenethyst Sphere in the Blasted Lands, and bring it to Kum'isha the Collector.\n\nBe warned, this gem is one of the rarest crystals in all of Azeroth. Any creature in these lands could be holding a Flawless Draenethyst Sphere.",7},
[93689]={"This is excellent news! With Dalaran returned to peace, I can see no reason the Kirin Tor would not welcome you with open arms!\n\nPlease, report to the council with great haste. I'm sure they will be looking forward to meeting the city's savior.","Speak with Archmage Celindra in the City of Dalaran.",1},
[93735]={"Historically, the Windshapers have seen to the tending of the magical instruments and devices that were gifted to us by the spirits of the wind. This includes the myriad of magical constructs around the island. Since the spirits left us, only a scant few of these are still functional.\n\nOne of the few remaining working constructs in Valanaar has become damaged. One of our artisans was dispatched to help, but he may be in need of aid. Travel to the west end of the city and offer any assistance you can.","Find Riaani Nightwind on the west side of Valanaar.",4},
[93736]={"The paramount concern of the Windshapers is to better understand why the spirits left us, and what we may be able to do to bring them back. One curious fixture of Shadowgale Forest to the north is the presence of a curious form of wind sprite that some call \"hollows\". We know little of them and why they are there, but we do know that they first started to appear after the spirits of the wind left us.\n\nI need you to go there and disperse them. Gather the remains and bring them back here.","Gather 10 Wind Hollow Essences from Wind Hollows in the Shadowgale Forest.",5},
[93737]={"Oh, hello. Ayessa sent you to assist me? Very well then. \n\nNot sure what an obvious novice like yourself can do, but if you give me a moment to pull my head out of this construct's innards I might have a few ideas of things you can do to help.","Speak with Riaani Nightwind and listen to what he has to say.",5},
[93738]={"Brightwish, eh? So the High Order wanted to remove these components for some reason. But why though?\n\nThe High Order has always been meddlesome, constantly wanting to experiment with the wind spirits' magic. They are too bold by a mile, and we've strictly forbidden them from meddling with knowledge under Windshaper purview, but lately they've been testing our patience.\n\nI think you should report what you've learned back to Ayessa Dawnsinger. She can instruct you further on what to do.","Report back to Ayessa Dawnsinger in Valanaar.",4},
[93773]={"It seems that Ve'han has successfully stolen at least a portion of the power of a Wild God. Such a thing seems beyond belief to me, but here we are.\n\nAnd what is this \"Pact\" Ve'han spoke of? $n, you must return to Ketharas. Tell him what you've learned.\n\nI'm sorry to say but it is likely well beyond your abilities to put a foe such as Ve'han down. Only the power of--well, the Wild Gods themselves may be able to counteract this magic.","Report back Ketharas on Mount Hyjal.",3},
[93787]={"Humans within these lands have long enjoyed the warmth, comfort and sustenance these lands provide. It's time we start denying these humans such pleasantries.\n\nSeek out the supplies of our enemies at the farm to the southwest. Take whatever you find.\n\nIt won't bring pleasure like bloodying a blade, but slowing them buys us time to plan our next move.","Steal $1oa Feed Satchels from the Alliance farm in Meadowsbrook then return to Krom'rosh.",5},
[93797]={"It is a time-honored tradition for young mages to create their own spell focus when they have shown a certain degree of magical proficiency. This is typically done by gathering a fallen branch from our oldest trees, as they have some lingering traces of elemental wind.\n\nI have found the most ideal ones to be near the wind shrine, just south of Falaath Village. Go and bring me back a large branch and I will teach you about the traditions as we create your spell focus.","Bring a Wind-Infused Bough to Belann Windwood in Valanaar.",5},
[93825]={"You wish to learn from us? The trees of Hyjal speak to us. Their bark holds life, and on it grows the moss we call Moonveil. It is soft, green, and strong with the mountain's soul. We need this moss to heal our hurt and bless roots.\n\nGo, gentle one. Seek the old trees where the mist clings and the sun hides. Take Moonveil moss from their bark and bring it back to me. With it, we will mend what pains us.","Gather $1oa clumps of Moonveil Moss and return to Suma Mossmane.",5},
[93830]={"The Deadwood dwell by a pond born of Mount Hyjal's snow melt. That water is pure, strong with the mountain's breath. We use it for our draughts and to save roots from death.\n\nHere, the springs run slow. Our source must be saved, and used with care. But their pond flows with life, it could fill our den twice over. Bring me a skin filled with that water, friend. Spirits will bless your steps, and our den will drink deep of the mountain's gift.","Fill a waterskin provided by Fennar Mossmane at the pond outside of the Deadwood Furbolg den.",3},
[93833]={"The owls of Hyjal are more than feathers and flight. Their talons, their plumes, even the bones whisper of the wild. We use these gifts to craft talismans, charms that bind the spirits and shield our kin.\n\nBut the owls do not give freely. You must take what the mountain offers. Kill $1oa owls and bring their carcasses to me.\n\nYes, we ask you to return the whole body to us, as we waste nothing provided by such graceful creatures.","Bring $1oa owl bodies to Elder Pinespeaker in Barkskin Burrow in Hyjal.",4},
[93834]={"Burrow beetles! They're a bane... and now they dig in our den more than their own. We beat them back and swing clubs when we see them skulk by, but they are quick, and to hide in the dark is their shield.\n\nIf you spot them as you climb our den, squash them! We will take their crushed shells and make a meal, so it is not all bad.","Gather $1oa Burrow Beetle Bits for Dala Fairmaw.",3},
[93835]={"Lorthuna fled up to the spires above using some sort of portal. Ayessa and Elaadrin went in after her. That was just a few moments ago.\n\nI'm afraid I took one too many hits and this is where I stay. Go through the portal, find Elaadrin and help them stop Lorthuna.\n\nUnless that help that Elaadrin and Ayessa said they sent for arrives soon, you are on your own from here. Good luck, $c.","Take the portal to the Rohashi Spires overhead and join Elaadrin Evengale and Ayessa Dawnsinger in their confrontation with High Priestess Lorthuna.",3},
[93848]={"The magic that Ketharas was able to craft to counteract this threat was vital to this victory. Our druids should be able to replicate the magic and use it to dispel the wards empowering the Blackthorne Pact at scale.\n\nYou should go back to Ketharas and let him know what transpired here. Tell him that he has the thanks of the Guardians of Hyjal and the Cenarion Circle. He should know that he is always welcome amongst us should he desire a place alongside his fellow druids once again.","Return to Ketharas and inform him of what occurred at the Summit of Eternity.",5},
[93926]={"Whatever reason the cult has for attacking the tower, it's not worth losing our people over.\n\nI'd like for you to head to the southwest and check in on that watchtower for us. Find the peacekeepers there and tell them to head back to the village. Holding that tower is not worth the lives it would cost and I'd rather concentrate the defenders we do have here to protect our citizens.\n\nPeacekeeper Vaaniel is in charge; let him know to head back here as quickly as possible. Hurry!","Find Peacekeeper Vaaniel at the western watchtower.",3},
[93927]={"<As you inspect the body of the dead peacekeeper, a bloody note falls free of his hands. Picking it up and reading it may give you a clue as to how to proceed from here.>","Collect the note you found near the dead peacekeeper and read it to determine your next steps.",4},
[93948]={"Since you are going to Valanaar anyway, please deliver the signet ring you recovered from the tower to Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar. \n\nHe will want this back, and more importantly, he will want to learn the fate of his nephew. Talaanis is the High Elder of Zephras Isle and more importantly, he is a good man who is well loved by the people, despite our current hardships. It pains me to think of how he will react to this news. Please express my condolences for his loss.","Deliver the Shadowsong Family Signet to Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",3},
[93949]={"We've been bugged.\n\nIt's skyhopper season in the lowlands, which means the pests are everywhere. One of the High Order mages reported that one of the insects that they killed had an enchantment of some kind placed upon it. When we inspected it closely it seems to be some sort of listening spell.\n\nWe suspect that the cult is using these enchanted insects as spies. Go and exterminate them for us. You won't be able to tell which are enchanted by looking at them, so you'll just have to kill them all.","Kill Skyhoppers in Valanaar until you've eliminated $1oa Enchanted Skyhoppers.",5},
[93952]={"Barkskin stand on weak roots. Deadwood claw at our land, each day their rot digs deep, sinks more. We cannot hold alone. \n\nDeadwood Den guards are the brunt of their strength. If you seek our trust, strike down those who foul the wood. When their Guardians fall, the rest of their tribe will weaken. We even our odds.\n\nBring them down, for balance, and help keep Hyjal whole.","Defeat $1oa Deadwood Den Guardians and return to Brerufa.",4},
[93963]={"Stormwind, Ironforge, and Darnassus all have unique peoples and cultures. As a guest of the Alliance here on Azeroth, you should take some time to visit each of our capital cities in turn. \n\nSpeak with Randal Emerson in the southern antechamber for directions to get you started.","Speak with Randal Emerson in Stormwind Keep to receive further instructions. Use the instructions received to locate and speak with King Magni Bronzebeard, High Tinker Mekkatorque, and Tyrande Whisperwind.",6},
[93976]={"While Gur'dok and I continue our work, we did fashion a particular blade for a friend--perhaps friend is too strong a word--for an acquaintance down at the docks. This particular individual is well known and connected all across the Kingdoms and beyond.\n\nTake this. When you deliver it, let her know I sent you. And tell her we're even.","Deliver the blade to Kreza Darkthorn's acquaintance at the docks east of Rog'mar.",1},
[94003]={"I am all that remains of the line of Skybreakers here on Zephras Isle. The rest were murdered by the Al'Aketh.\n\nThe only thing that outweighs my sorrow is my shame. My family's ancestral shield--the Skybreaker Bulwark--is now in the hands of a cultist named Zaal Stormshield. Family lore holds no harm may befall a worthy wielder of this shield.\n\nZaal is not worthy, of that I am sure. Find this man at the Shrine of Akir and reclaim my shield from him. Do this and I will teach you the Skybreaker Defense.","Reclaim the Skybreaker Bulwark from Zaal Stormshield at the Shrine of Akir.",5},
[94004]={"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Elixir of Ogre's Strength, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.",0},
[94006]={"Greetings, $n. You have progressed in your druidic studies far enough that I think it is time for you to meet one of the great spirits that reside here on Zephras. Urs'endris is a wise and noble spirit, who has taught druids how to take on the ursera shape for generations. Unfortunately his domain has begun to wither and fall into the sky like many other areas of Zephras.\n\nTo find him, travel northeast near the waterfall in the shadow of the Shrine of Akir. He should be able to instruct you further.","Speak with Urs'endris near the falls northeast of Valanaar.",5},
[94007]={"Now that you've gained a level of comfort in the wilds of the highlands, I believe it is time for you to seek your very own animal companion.\n\nGo to the port of Valanaar to the southeast, and speak with Quel'ana Quickgale there. He will instruct you in the art of beast taming.","Report to Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar.",2},
[94050]={"You now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills to train it. For this, there is none better than my sister, Quel'dora. She will give you the ability to train your new pet. \n\nGo with the winds, young $c.","Speak to Quel'dora Quickgale in Valanaar.",3},
[94213]={"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Lesser Mana Potion, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.",0},
