[94360]={"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Soul Pouch, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.",0},
[94369]={"Ansirem has told me much of the elemental lords and I am afraid that we have good reason to fear Al'Akir now that the wards that have hidden Zephras are down. If the Windlord chooses to attack us, we stand no chance to defend ourselves while we are here in his domain.\n\nHigh Elder Shadowsong needs to know of the danger we are in, and more importantly, what our intentions are for our mission to Azeroth. We will find the means to save our home. I swear it.","Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",1},
[94373]={"Aye, the time's come, young shaman. Ye've grown stout and sturdy, like the stone beneath our boots. Takin' up the shaman's path shows ye've got the wisdom o' the mountain, even before ye've proven yerself. Ye've the grit of stone to walk the earth's path.\n\nBut to earn its favor, ye must face it proper. South o' here, the Frostmane trolls live in a cave.\n\nBring me two of the necklaces they wear, crafted from the Iceclaw bears. Then we'll speak more of yer future.","Bring 2 Frostmane Bear Pendants to Teo Hammerstorm in Anvilmar.",4},
[94427]={"A key tenent of being a paladin is the pursuit of divinity. This is not the pursuit of godhood, but merely the pursuit of good itself, for good's sake. We've all arrived at this place due to tragedy of one form or another, and it would be easy to lose that grace that defined us as paladins in life.\n\nGo to the Undercity and seek out Tanis Alderwood in the Trade Quarter. They are in need, and they could benefit greatly from some grace.","Speak to Tanis Alderwood in the Undercity.",2},
[94434]={"Wait, you want to... help? Why would a paladin want to help a beggar like me?\n\nWell, I suppose that you could be of some assistance. \n\nIt's my wife you see. She, well... she's falling apart. I mean that literally. The apothecaries can stitch her back together right as rain, but they are about the Dark Lady's business and none are available to help. If you could perhaps bring me some fresh cloth then I could at least make her a wrapping to hold her together while we wait for the apothecaries.","Bring 10 Linen Cloth to Tanis Alderwood in the Undercity.",5},
[94435]={"I don't know why you'd go out of your way to help me, but I appreciate it. If someone sent you my way, tell them I appreciate them too. You'll always have a friend in Tanis Alderwood, $c.","Return to Danitha Morr at Bandarion Keep.",2},
[94436]={"It's time to demonstrate your ability to channel one of the light's greatest gifts.\n\nThe item I just gave you is called the Symbol of Life. Take care, as it may cause you some discomfort to handle a talisman of the light such as this. The light may be anathema to the force that created us, but it is still our guide and ally. The pain reminds us of this.\n\nGo see Deathguard Billmuth downstairs. He just arrived and he has petitioned us for aid. Show him and the Forsaken what a true paladin can do.","Speak with Deathguard Billmuth at Bandarion Keep.\n\nShould you misplace your Symbol of Life, return to Danitha Morr for a replacement.",1},
[94438]={"Falgan and I were sent on a mission to scout out scarlet activity in Venomweb Vale. We managed to sneak close enough to one of their camps to hear about new orders involving an attack on Brill. Before we could decide what to do next, I stepped on a twig and the noise alerted them to us.\n\nFalgan yelled at me to run, so I ran. By the time I realized he wasn't with me, I was halfway to Brill. That brave idiot probably stayed behind to hold them off for me.\n\nPlease, find my friend and help him if you can.","Take the Symbol of Life and use it to resurrect Deathguard Falgan at Venomweb Vale. \n\nShould you misplace your Symbol of Life, return to Danitha Morr for a replacement.",5},
[94440]={"These Scarlet Crusaders often carry satchels with their deployment orders. We know an attack is coming, but if we can recover their orders, we can warn the rest of the Deathguard and prepare an ambush. \n\nYou are clearly an impressive paladin. Kill these scarlet animals and retrieve a copy of their orders and bring them back to Deathguard Billmuth. He'll take it from there.","Retrieve the Scarlet Crusade Attack Plans from the Scarlet Crusaders at Venomweb Vale, and return to Deathguard Billmuth at Bandarion Keep.",4},
[94441]={"Please give my thanks to Danitha Morr and tell her that the rest of the Deathguard will hear about the service that the paladins of Bandarion Keep performed for us. \n\nYou have a lot of promise as a paladin, and I am proud to have those like you among the ranks of the Forsaken. Dark Lady watch over you, $n.","Speak with Danitha Morr in the keep at Bandarion Keep.",2},
[94465]={"Aye, ye've the strength to bear the totem o' fire, lad--but strength alone won't make ye ready.\n\nBeyond the Valley o' Kings, in the crags of Loch Modan, lies a hidden path to one o' our sacred peaks. There, Braldir Ashmantle guards the Shrine o' the Dormant Flame. \n\nTake this torch to him--it shows yer intent. Return it burnin' by the shrine's brazier, and I'll see ye earn the totem proper.","Bring the Torch of the Dormant Flame to Braldir Ashmantle in Loch Modan.",4},
[94467]={"The fire sapta's ready, $n. Now ye face the flame. Use it at the shrine, then climb to the peak. There, ye'll see the spirit--he'll not strike 'til ye do, but he'll know ye see him.$B$BStrike fast, lad. The longer ye wait, the stronger he burns. When he falls, take his glowing embers and place 'em in the brazier. Light the torch and earn the fire's favor.","Defeat the Minor Manifestation of Fire, and place the Glowing Ember in the brazier atop the Shrine of Eternal Flame.",6},
[94479]={"Picking up the rusting metal, you see another, shinier, engineering component. It looks like anything else of use has been picked clean.\n\nPerhaps somebody nearby recognizes this part or who might want to salvage it.","Search the Tainted Foothills for someone interested in the metallic piece you found.",1},
[94481]={"This hearty stew keeps our trainees fed, enough so that our enemies remain at a distance.\n\nBring this and feed our trainees to the west. Don't listen to any complaints. With how difficult defending our supply lines has become, they should be so lucky we're not feeding them dirt.","Feed $1oa Rog'mar Trainees at the training grounds.",4},
[94483]={"Our scouts have reported training camps by the river to the south. If I'd received word sooner, it would have saved us both the hassle of locating and removing the human filth in a timely manner.\n\nContinue your efforts, $n. Holding back the humans to their precious little keep will buy us time to focus on other matters at hand.\n\nBe swift about it.","Slay $1oa Farholde Priests and $2oa Farholde Scouts south of the river.",5},
[94484]={"A moment if you will, $n. Are you headed towards Shadowgale Forest? There is a druid conclave there in a cave to the northeast. I have been waiting on word from them but their correspondence is long overdue.\n\nWith Ban'aethall in ruins and all the unrest lately I worry something dire may have happened. Please, if you are able, go seek out Elegael Thornpaw and put my mind at ease.","Find and speak with Elegael Thornpaw in the northeastern part of Shadowgale Forest.",2},
[94495]={"If there's one truth ye need to learn about water, it's this: water means rebirth. It carves stone, cleanses filth, and heals the weary -- but only when it's pure. Taint it, and it'll ruin all it touches.\n\nIf ye seek the water sapta, find Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands. Her family dwells in a cave beneath the southern falls.\n\nGo on then, don't let the river outrun ye.","Find Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands.",2},
[94497]={"Ah, so ye've come seekin' the sapta, have ye? Well then, listen close, love. To find understandin' and earn the sapta, ye must seek water in its various forms. As ye gather the samples, keep yer eyes open. Watch the beasts that guard it, the land it nourishes, and how it changes lives.\n\nWe'll start simple: fill this skin at the base o' the falls, where the fresh meets the brackish. Go on now, and mind the marsh.","Fill the Empty Brown Waterskin at the bottom of the waterfalls below Hervdana's cave and return it to her in the Wetlands.",3},
[94499]={"Aye, Redridge drinks deep from Lake Everstill, but by the time the waters tumble down Stonewatch Falls, somethin' has seeped in. The murlocs down there are big, twisted brutes. Not like the ones ye find here or in the Loch. Lucky for the townsfolk they keep to the base o' the falls.\n\nBring a sampling to me. I've a mind to find out if it's magic, venom, or somethin' worse that's taintin' the waters near that old fort.","Fill the Empty Red Waterskin at Stonewatch Falls near the Nightcrawler Murlocs and return to Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands.",4},
[94504]={"Some may speak with you now, but not all. For more of our tribe to be what you know as friend, you must not rush.\n\nStay by our side, work with our young and old, and guard us from those who wish us harm.\n\nWhen you have more to bring to us, we will have more to share.","Raise your reputation with the Barkskin Burrow to Neutral.",3},
[94532]={"Though the gnoll presence has dwindled with the Twilight's encroachment, the threat remains.\n\nThe hills to the southwest are infested with their kind, disrupting trades and travelers alike.\n\nClear a path for our allies by removing the threat.","Kill $1oa Redridge Mystics, $2oa Redridge Trappers, and $3oa Redridge Brutes for Neza Bloodsnout at Rog'mar.",5},
[94533]={"Among the cackling inhabitants of the Bristle Hills southwest of here is an elder gnoll by the name of Snargl. The sounds emanating from this particular gnoll are quite unpleasant. Their presence inspires those around, creating a problem for allies and scouts who enter the area.\n\nA trophy as a memento of our having dealt with this most unpleasant gnoll fiend would fit nicely with my collection.\n\nBe swift about it, $n.","Locate Snargl in the Bristle Hills, kill him, and retrieve his snout for Neza Bloodsnout.",5},
[94535]={"Our allies mining ore from the hills to the south reported several attacks by gnolls in the area.\n\nTravel south, locate their camps and retrieve the stolen ore. Take it from their dead bodies if need be.","Gather $1oa Stolen Ore from gnolls in the Bristle Hills for Kreza Darkthorn.",5},
[94615]={"I've got no idea what happened to our horses. I got up one morning to feed 'em and they were all gone, just like that.\n\nLife outside Farholde's a bit rougher. Anything could've got 'em--animals, murlocs, orcs, you name it.\n\nIf we wanna narrow down our list of culprits, we oughta search around the stables for clues.","Search near the stables at Wheeler's Grange for evidence of the missing horses' whereabouts.",3},
[94672]={"Humans are not our only adversary within the Riverglades, $n, nor are they our most dire.\n\nA cult known as the Twilight's Hammer has begun a campaign against those they deem heretics in the eyes of their twisted gods. The ravaged remains of a human settlement to the west are but the first to fall to their conquest. No doubt Rog'mar will be next.\n\nWe cannot afford to let them establish a foothold so close to our doorstep. Go to this so-called Sunnyglade and thin their numbers.","Defeat $1oa Twilight Raiders and $2oa Twilight Neophytes within Sunnyglade for Tran'gul in Rog'mar.",5},
[94678]={"The gnolls have been a thorn in our side ever since we arrived. While less a threat than the Twilight's Hammer, they are aggressive, persistent and, worst of all, numerous.\n\nThe hills beyond this post are infested with them, making passage to the north dangerous, and posing a threat to those living outside the walls of Farholde Keep.\n\nIf we are ever to make these lands safe, removing the gnoll threat is imperative.","Kill $1oa Redridge Mystics, $2oa Redridge Trappers, and $3oa Redridge Brutes for Cedric Dalton at Southern Watch.",5},
[94679]={"Gnolls value strength above all else. By killing their strongest, we not only lessen the threat they pose physically, but also strike fear into their hearts.\n\nIn a den among the Bristle Hills is a notorious gnoll by the name of Snargl. His death would no doubt sow panic among the Redridge's ranks.\n\nBring me his snout, and be quick about it.","Locate Snargl in the Bristle Hills, kill him, and bring his snout to Cedric Dalton at Southern Watch.",5},
[94733]={"Alright, so you won a few battles. I think you might have what it takes to make it here after all.\n\nBefore I convince our next combatant to jump into the ring with you there's something I need from you first--food for Chub'chob's pet boar, Snufflesnout.\n\nI promised I'd look after it, and, well, this gig here's keepin' me quite busy. Trust me, this'll benefit the both of us.\n\nMosey on over to the east of Clugfist's clubhouse. You're lookin' for a shy fella who goes by the name Gobam.","Locate Gobam in Bolder'ok.",1},
[94737]={"Ok friend. Here is treat. Snufflesnout snort and be happy when she see this.\n\nAnd tell goblin please stop talk so much.","Deliver the bundle of goods to Jezap Jinglesprocket in Bolder'ok.",1},
[94744]={"You did well slowing the Twilight's Hammer. Their foothold in Sunnyglade has weakened and you've turned their ogre warriors against them. Now we take the fight to them.\n\nMy brother, Dag'rosh, has already gone ahead with a scouting party. I would have preferred he waited for you, but he is impulsive and overeager--like a true warrior. I'd be honored if you joined him in battle at their stronghold to the west.","Find Da'grosh in the hills west of Rog'mar.",1},
[94745]={"Do you see the fortress just west of here? The Twilight's Shroud, they call it. Filled to the brim with Twilight's Hammer cowards.\n\nThey may have walls and numbers, but their pitiful reliance on devilry and ancient gods makes them weak. Show them how vulnerable they really are!","Defeat $1oa Twilight Fanatics, $2oa Twilight Corrupters, and $3oa Twilight Champions within the Twilight's Shroud for Da'grosh.",5},
[94774]={"You've caught the attention of our superiors, $n. They've asked you to travel to the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind as soon as possible. Apparently they feel you've proven yourself already and are prepared to further your training. When you get there, find High Priestess Laurena. She will be able to guide you further. Good luck, and may the Light be with you.","Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.",2},
[94775]={"Elune bless you, good $r. I hope your Light finds you and protects you well this day.$B$BOne of your priests was here not long ago looking for you. He mentioned you returning to the Cathedral of Light as soon as possible to speak with High Priestess Laurena. It seems you've done well to garner such attention. I wouldn't spend too much time here--your people have need of you.","Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.",2},
[94776]={"Time's come for you to head to Stormwind, $n. High Priestess Laurena in the Cathedral of Light wants to speak to you. Gotta be somethin' really good or really bad for the High Priestess to want you there personally, but I'm guessin' you've only done well for yourself and it's a good thing that she wants to speak to ya.$B$BBut don't waste too much time 'round here. I'd head there as soon as you can.","Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.",2},
[94778]={"You're needed in Stormwind, $n. The High Priestess there, Laurena, says it's time for you to prove you're worthy of the next level of your training. Don't waste too much time finding your way there. You can find her in the Cathedral of Light in the center of the city. Give her my regards, and prove how worthy you are of such a calling. The Light be with you, $n.","Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.",0},
[94779]={"Praise be to Elune, and to your Light, $n.$B$BAbout this time, many of our order learn abilities reflecting their faith in Elune. If knowledge serves me, I believe the same holds true for your order also.$B$BWhen your business in Darnassus is complete, I would seek out one of your High Priestesses for further training.","Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.",2},
[94792]={"Many hunters prefer to travel with animal companions. With a beast at your side, you will find that you can survive even the most dangerous of circumstances. As they say, everything is easier with a friend. However, obtaining an animal companion is something that must be done with care. The balance of nature is delicate, and must always be respected.\n\nTake this Taming Rod with you to the forest. With it, you will be able to tame a Rockhide Boar and practice your skills as a hunter.","Use the Taming Rod to tame a Rockhide Boar. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Josephine Carson.",5},
[94793]={"You now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills to train it. For this, there is none better than Isaac Chan, a lifelong woodsman. He will give you the ability to train your new pet.\n\nGo with the winds, young $c.","Speak to Isaac Chan in Goldshire.",3},
[94819]={"$n, your High Priestess Mims would have an audience with you in Ironforge. Make haste, my clever friend, your next test quickly approaches. Although I wish I could bear witness to your race's own special rites, my place is here. But may the Light go with you in your travels. Mims should still be in the Mystic Ward once you reach the city. She will be waiting.","Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.",2},
[94824]={"Time's come for you to head to Ironforge, $n. High Priestess Mims in the Hall of Mysteries commands you to come speak with her. Gotta be somethin' really good or really bad for the High Priestess to want you there personally, but I'm guessin' you've only done well for yourself and it's a good thing that she wants to speak to ya.$B$BBut don't waste too much time 'round here. I'd head there as soon as you can.","Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.",2},
[94825]={"Just a short time ago, one of your priests was here looking for you, $r. He said that if I were to see you, I should direct you towards the Hall of Mysteries. He said it was very important, but I would not be overly concerned if I were you. His demeanor seemed positive... as though it were good news. I wouldn't take too long in making my way there if I were you.$B$BElune be with you, good $r.","Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.",2},
[94826]={"Praise be to Elune, and to your Light, $n.$B$BAbout this time, many of our order learn abilities reflecting their faith in Elune. If knowledge serves me, I believe the same holds true for your order also.$B$BWhen your business in Darnassus is complete, I would seek out your High Priestess for further training.","Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.",2},
[94842]={"We make our own fertilizer out here. It's a special formula of mine that reeks like hell, but grows trees like they're weeds.\n\nIt's a 1:1:2 ratio of crawfish shells, manure, and murloc heads. Tasty, right?\n\nThe manure's easy enough. We've got the ranch to the south for that. The heads and shells? Those you're going to have to go wading in the river for.\n\nIf you feel like lending a hand, we could sure use your help getting some fertilizer ingredients.","Gather 4 Jumbo Crawfish Shells, 4 pieces of Fresh Manure, and 8 Mudfin Murloc Heads for Halligan Turner.",5},
[94864]={"You've proven yourself by taming a boar and a wolf. Now it's time for your final challenge. Elwynn's balance depends on respect and skill. Take this Taming Rod and seek out a Young Forest Bear. Show that you can earn the trust of even the mightiest companion. \n\nCompleting this lesson will deepen your attunement to beasts.","Use the Taming Rod to tame a Young Forest Bear. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Josephine Carson.",5},
[94873]={"Either dominant centaur clan is likely to pose a good ally, but I ought to offer a word of caution regarding the Gelkis.\n\nI have trustworthy intel that suggests, between the Magram and the Gelkis, the latter are very much on the losing side. This may work to our advantage--desperation may push the isolated clan into opening up to outside help.\n\nI have prepared a tote of totems for you to take to their quartermaster, assuming they have one, in Gelkis Village. This may work in our favor.","Bring the Totem Tote to the Gelkis Quartermaster at Gelkis Village in the Desolace to significantly increase your reputation with that clan.  You must be of at least Neutral standing with the Gelkis Clan Centaur.",1},
[94877]={"When you look around you, what do you see? A broken home and a tired people.\n\nStormwind has left us to fend for ourselves, and we have less to do that with every day. Many within these walls are refugees who barely escaped tragedy without so much as even their own families.\n\nFarholde is no Stormwind, stranger. We lost a settlement in the northwest to the Twilight's Hammer, but we will not let them keep it. If you wish to fight, go to Sunnyglade and purge those savages from our lands.","Defeat $1oa Twilight Raiders, $2oa Twilight Shadowmancers, and $3oa Twilight Neophytes within Sunnyglade for Demar Brant.",5},
[94879]={"You've seen the ruined city to the north, yes? Sunnyglade? Demar tries sending troops, but we're no closer to reclaiming it. I have a better idea.\n\nIn truth, this attack by the Twilight's Hammer is not the first. They seem to be coordinating from a centralized location, and I would know where. While you're out doing what you adventurers do best, see if you can't keep an eye out for any documents they may have misplaced. With enough of them, I should be able to piece together their intentions.","Collect $1oa Twilight Pages from within Sunnyglade for Ashe Amberall in Farholde Keep.",5},
[94884]={"I've had enough of this cave. Once you clear your way out, I'll slip out amidst the chaos.\n\nI'm afraid I'm in too weak of condition to carry those samples, however. Their energy is overwhelming, and I've been trapped down here for Light knows how long. Once we get out of here, please take them to Lady Amberhall immediately. I must rest.","Bring the Filled Crystal Catalyst to Ashe Amberhall in Farholde Keep.",3},
[94885]={"The log is full of meticulous recordings on the comings and goings of Twilight's Hammer forces throughout the Riverglades. \n\nThe author is nowhere to be found, but this information could help shed light on enemy movements.\n\nSomeone in Farholde will want to see this.","Deliver the Field Marshal's Log to Demar Brant in Farholde Keep.",5},
[94886]={"As helpful as you've been here in Farholde, I believe your talents could be put to better use elsewhere.\n\nA patrol of ours went missing some time ago. They were in charge of our western borders, but with the information Miss Amberhall has uncovered, I fear they walked right into the Twilight Hammer's central encampment.\n\nWe can handle the cleanup in Sunnyglade ourselves. If the good lady is right, it's critical that we check on our wayward sergeant. He could use all the help he can get.","Find Sergeant Riftan near the Twilight's Shroud to the west.",1},
[94891]={"Seems like things are quieting down around here for now, but I want to keep an eye out. You want to send Amberhall a report? Send her this.\n\n<Sergeant Riftan tosses Kilgar's head back to you.>\n\nThat ought to shut her up. At least for a while. Good work out there.","Return to Ashe Amberhall in Farholde Keep.",5},
[94892]={"It's too late for me, stranger. I'm not going to be making it out of this one. Take my crest to the Knight Commander. Warn him...\n\n<Ryan's eyes begin to glaze over as he mumbles to himself.>\n\nI'm sorry. I should have come home. Abigail...","Return Marshal Ryan's crest to Knight Commander Demar Brant in Farholde Keep.",5},
[94893]={"So, his final thoughts were of Abigail?\n\nI know this is not your business, friend, but I must ask you to deliver the news of the Marshal's passing on my behalf. Ryan's betrothed, Abigail Lawson, did not join us when we established Farholde Keep. The two of them apparently had a disagreement, and while I do not know the specifics, I do know that she now resides within Stormwind City.\n\nPlease take the Marshal's crest to Terry for me. I don't think my presence would be a welcome one.","Deliver Marshal Ryan's Crest to Abigail Lawson in the Cathedral Square of Stormwind City.",5},
[94894]={"Lady Amberhall told me of your exploits with the Twilight's Hammer. I'm impressed. But concerned.\n\nFarholde started its campaign originally to remove the Horde from our homeland. While that remains our primary goal, we cannot take this sudden surge in cultist activity lightly. If our pleas to Stormwind remain unheard, we will be overwhelmed as we face foes on two fronts alone.\n\nWith the evidence you carry, perhaps they can set aside their pride long enough to listen. At this point it's our only option.","Deliver Kilgar's Head to Bolvar Fordragon within Stormwind Keep in Stormwind City.",6},
[94896]={"You look like a capable adventurer. Do you happen to be headed towards Shadowgale Forest? Ban'aethal lies deep in the forest; that's where we're all from.\n\n<Ealaane gestures to the other refugees.>\n\nWe've recently had to evacuate Ban'aethal, as it began to fall into the sky. It was sudden and in the middle of the night. If you are headed that way, would you please look for any belongings left behind? The forest and village are far too dangerous for us to return to now.","Collect $1oa Abandoned Belongings from the ruins of Ban'aethal.",5},
[94897]={"If you are traveling to Ban'aethal, I have a selfish request. My love, Resaan... I believe is no longer a part of this world. He had tried to go back to get supplies even though I begged him to stay. It has been over a week already and I fear the worst.\n\nPlease, if you find him, bring him home. If he has perished then I beg you to please bring me his heirloom.","Find Resaan in the Ruins of Ban'aethal.",5},
[94911]={"Greetings, young $r. I can see that you have much promise in the druidic arts. There is one who you may want to speak with in the city of Thunder Bluff by the name of Turak Runetotem. He will teach you how to reach the stronghold of the Cenarion Circle on Kalimdor, Moonglade. \n\nYou will be welcomed there, and the druids of the circle will impart their knowledge upon you. \n\nAs your people would say--go with the wind's blessing, young one. I wish you good fortune in your adventures.","Speak with Turak Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.",5},
[94914]={"All druids are welcomed to the sacred lands of Moonglade. Keeper Remulos--Moonglade's guardian--keeps watch over all druids who hibernate there. I'll teach you the spell that lets you transport yourself there. Cast it whenever you seek Moonglade's knowledge or solace.$B$BAs for your first lesson here on Azeroth, travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven about the path you're now on. Good luck, young druid.","Use the spell \"Teleport: Moonglade\" to travel to Moonglade. When you arrive, speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven.",2},
[94923]={"<Robbie leans in to talk to you, as if sharing a grave secret.>\n\nPsst! Hey $gmister:miss;, I need your help!\n\nMy sister got me a hat for my birthday but I lost it playing in the river. I'm not allowed to be down there because of the murlocs so I can't ask Dad or Ellie for help because then they'll know where I was!\n\nIt's a good hat. I bet one of those murlocs found it and kept it for himself!","Find Robbie's Hat somewhere along the river near the murlocs.",4},
[94926]={"Like most ogre weaponry, this hammer is large, unwieldy, and well-worn. A creature of any other race could hardly swing it at all.\n\nTo you, it is of little more use than a trophy, but perhaps someone at Farholde would appreciate knowing of Komuk's demise.","Take Komuk's Maul to Farholde Keep as proof of the ogre's demise.",6},
[94928]={"These hides are to be delivered to Powderfuse Port. It is a goblin-run port to the northeast.\n\nWhen you get there, deliver the hides to Friz Frazzlespark. Tell her they're from Cornelius. The details of our trade have already been worked out, so she'll know what they are for.","Deliver the Bundle of Lion Hides to Friz Frazzlespark at Powderfuse Port.",1},
[94929]={"I know I said that was it, but I promise, I wouldn't ask this if it weren't important. It's a shipment of utmost urgency.\n\nAn old acquaintance resides in a keep within the Riverglades. To get there, travel northeast through the bogs avoiding the deadly creatures within. Along the northeastern hillside sits an old path. Travel its road all the way through the hills and when you hit the fork in the road stay north, then east. You should see Farholde along the eastern shore.\n\nI thank you for your aid.","Bring the Shipment to Demar Brant at Farholde Keep in the Riverglades.",1},
[94930]={"<A handwritten label appears on the side of the crate. On the right side is a map with a large red circle along a southeastern shoreline north of a poorly drawn temple surrounded by water and some kind of winged creatures. On the left is a note in massive font.>\n\nPROPERTY OF FRIZ FRAZZLESPARK\n\nPOWDERFUSE PORT\n\nWARNING: NOT for tampering. Do NOT open without supervision.\n\n<An additional note appears at the bottom of the label.>\n\nIf lost, return to Friz Frazzlespark. Powderfuse Port. Riverglades.","Deliver the Lost Shipping Crate to Friz Frazzlespark at Powderfuse Port in the Riverglades.",1},
[94968]={"Of the few that managed to infiltrate the cave, most have perished. It seems these Twilight have a foothold much larger than we thought. We will not stand by while these cultists continue to ravage these lands and make sacrifices of our allies. We end this now, $n.\n\nInfiltrate this stronghold, slaughter their forces and bring me proof of their leader's demise.","Infiltrate Krol'dok Stronghold and return to Krom'rosh with proof of their leader's demise.",6},
[94969]={"Don't ask. You wouldn't believe me if I told you.\n\nLet's just focus on getting me out of here! Oh, and you as well, of course.","Escort Marcus Tilwell to safety.",5},
[94971]={"One of the most important parts of a paladin's arsenal has always been their warhorse. These specially consecrated animals bear paladins and their arms into battle, and are as fearless and bold as the best of us.\n\nWhile our situation has changed, our need for steeds to bear us into battle has not. It's time that you had such a mount for yourself.","Speak with Danitha Morr to learn to summon your Warhorse.",2},
[94972]={"With their location revealed, it is likely that within this stronghold are secrets kept well hidden from those we have encountered thus far. It would be wise for us to locate and recover any information that may be of use to our fight against these cultists.\n\nSee what you can uncover, $n. I await your return.","Recover the Tome of Twilight from Krol'dok Stronghold.",6},
[94973]={"<The moulding appears to be for a key.>","Find someone in Rog'mar who may know about the mould.",5},
[94975]={"Our work here is not finished, $n. These cultists have inflicted unimaginable pain upon our allies and rendered these lands for their taking.\n\nWe will not tolerate these actions any longer.\n\nTo the north lies a hidden cave network, masked by the rugged terrain. Our scouts spoke of cultist movement under the veil of darkness.\n\nSeek out this cave and find where these cultists are hiding. It's time we deliver a message they won't soon forget.","Collect $1oa Cultist Ears from the Twilight's Hammer in Krol'dok Stronghold.",5},
[94979]={"You've proven you can tame the river's crawler. Now it's time to test your skill on open ground. The plains of Zephras echo with the cries of the galestrider, a proud, winged hunter that runs like the wind.\n\nTake this Taming Rod and seek one out. Travel to the lowlands and earn its trust.\n\nShow you're ready for the trials yet to come.","Use the Taming Rod to tame an Ornery Galestrider in the Gustberry Lowlands. \nPractice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar.",5},
[94980]={"<The moulding appears to be for a key.>","Find someone in Farholde Keep who may know about the mould.",5},
[94982]={"Our scouts mentioned a network of caves to the northwest along the mountains, hidden by natural surroundings. Most who sought information from deep within have yet to return. I fear they may be lost.\n\nThose watching from a distance mentioned a Twilight presence moving in and out of the caves, often in darkness.\n\nLocate this stronghold. If it is what I think it is we must deliver a deathly blow to their leader. Only then may we continue our efforts to remove them from these lands.","Infiltrate Krol'dok Stronghold and return to Commander Brant with proof of their leader's demise.",6},
[94983]={"The stories our scouts shared were quite horrid. I'll spare you the gruesome details. What we've discovered confirms previous reports of a cultist hideout.\n\nTo the north lies a cave, well hidden by its surroundings. This cave leads to... well, a place we've yet to infiltrate. We believe it's a foothold, nestled deep within the mountains.\n\nIt's time we repay the cultists for their actions against our allies.\n\nVenture north, seek out our enemies, and return to me with proof of their demise.","Collect $1oa Cultist Bangles from the Twilight's Hammer in Krol'dok Stronghold.",6},
[94984]={"No matter our efforts, the Twilight forces persist. We've deduced they must be coming from somewhere else.\n\nWith the new pet you brought me, I was able to politely ask our dear Twilight Thrall if it knew anything about where its former masters were coming from. Of note was mention of shadow magics and an ogre by the name of Nar'gurk in a hidden stronghold north of Sunnyglade.\n\nSeek him out. Kill him and recover what you can. There must be something we can learn from these efforts.","Kill Nar'gurk within Krol'dok Stronghold and recover any valuable information.",6},
[94997]={"We mustn't linger. Take these to the keep at once.\n\nFind Ashe Amberhall. She may be a pain, but she's well respected in her field of study. Perhaps she can shed some light on what energies are contained within these objects.","Bring the Satchel of Cursed Mementos to Ashe Amberhall in Farholde Keep.",5},
[95026]={"Escapin' war don't mean we be safe here. Dem creatures to da east been plaguin' da area all dis time.\n\nMaybe you be ready for a challenge, eh?\n\nStrike 'em down. Ain't nobody gonna be missin' dem after all.","Eliminate $1oa Forgotten Soldiers and $2oa Fleshflay Raveners.",5},
[95027]={"We always need more arrows for hunting and fighting, and for feathers, we use the white feathers of the Hyjal owl. They're naturally fluffy and soft, but I stiffen them up with a mixture designed to make them perfect for fletching.\n\nYou can get feathers from the owls, of course, but they also leave behind feathers in their nests, which you can find all over to the south of here.\n\nBring back a bundle of feathers, all right?","Head south into the valley and collect owl feathers from their nests.",5},
[95034]={"I think you should know that it wasn't actually the Gnolls who attacked us on the road.\n\nWe were actually attacked by a giant, wolf-like creature that I now know as a \"worgen\". It dispatched our guards and came for me, but Banon threw himself in its path. I managed to get a spell off which startled the creature, causing it to flee, but Banon was already badly bitten. He insisted I leave him there but I refused.\n\nWe were limping back here when the gnolls found us. What came next was terrifying...","Speak with Lumina Windsinger in the Sepulcher.",1},
[95036]={"Trevan tells me that the worgen are a major threat to the citizens of Silverpine Forest. Despite their strength and resilience they can be killed, but there is one in particular that just doesn't ever seem to stay dead due to unknown magic.\n\nThat's the one that attacked us. He is known as Old Fire-Eye and he is the biggest and meanest of their kind. To put him down, we'll need a special kind of weapon.\n\nSpeak with Trevan and he will supply you with a list of what is needed to forge such a weapon.","Speak with Trevan Rol in the Sepulcher and bring him the materials he requires.",3},
[95059]={"Time for a special delivery.\n\nKnight Commander Demar Brant at Farholde is waiting for this. For some reason he always makes me say his full name. What an odd fella.\n\nAnywho, you can find him holed up in the keep southwest of here. Massive stone fortress. Ya can't miss it.","Deliver Frazzlespark's Crate to Knight Commander Demar Brant in Farholde Keep.",1},
[95063]={"Ok, listen up. You've showed quite a bit of prowess in the ring. You've managed to upset Chub'chob more than words can explain. Sure glad I ain't you right now.\n\nJust in case you was wonderin', I should remind you that your entry fee does not cover accidental death.\n\nIt's been great knowin' ya, but you're on your own from here on out, bub.\n\nBest of luck to ya.","Defeat Chub'chob, Bloodmaster of Bolder'ok, in the Bloodmaster's Ring, then share the news of becoming the newly crowned champion of the Bloodmaster's Ring with Clugfist at Bolder'ok.",6},
[95107]={"One chief of the Deadwood, Deeproar, barks in the depths of their den. He was once of no burrow, and in a night of bad blood, he fell sway to their spells.\n\nNow, he feeds on their sour sap, with twice the cursed roar.\n\nGo. End his foul ways. Take his staff and bring it here, so I know he holds it no more.","Kill Chieftain Deeproar and return his staff to Elder Pinespeaker in Barkskin Burrow.",4},
[95108]={"With far sight, we have seen their den. Deadwood brew dark rites in their pots. They feed this foul mix to their young, so bad roots take. Then they learn to fight with vile ways.\n\nGo, stop this spread. Slay the dark ones and smash their stew.","Kill two Deadwood Death Mystics and destroy two Deadwood Cauldrons within Deadwood Den.",4},
[95111]={"In Tarren Mill there is a weaponsmith known as Ott. By all accounts he is an unremarkable smith, selling simple blades to travelers. I purchased a sword from him myself, and when I took it to the undercity for maintenance some time later, the smiths there were surprised at its quality. They assumed it came from a well-known master smith, but no, it was just Ott.\n\nI'd like to give this orc a chance to do something truly special. Take the materials to Ott in Tarren Mill and offer him the commission.","Speak with Ott and ask him to forge your blade.",3},
[95118]={"Murlocs, murlocs, murlocs! That's all I ever hear about; from the sailors, the fishermen, even my own kids! Everyone's on my case about 'em! They're a nuisance, I admit, but I got a port to run here!\n\nHelp a guy out, would ya? Kill a couple 'a those things and I'll make it worth your time.","Kill 8 Murloc Oracles and 8 Murloc Warriors along the Eastwind Shore.",5},
[95119]={"You know the Eastsea crew? Real unsavory bunch, and that's coming from the guy running a place called \"Powderfuse Port\".\n\nThey're destructive, bloodthirsty, and, worst of all, cutting into my bottom line. They steal cargo, and sink ships, both of which end up costing me the big bucks!\n\nWe gotta take down their whole operation, starting with the ones closest to here. You can find 'em along the beaches to the north.","Kill $1oa Eastsea Buccaneers and $2oa Eastsea Musketeers along the Eastwind Shore, north of Powderfuse Port.",5},
[95121]={"Welcome to Fimbo's cafe on the water! Today's menu is roasted boar, and roasted fish...same as every day...\n\nThis menu needs a shake up, badly. I've had my eye on a new seafood stew recipe, but I'm gonna need some fresh meat. A few murloc eyes and some crab meat oughta do.\n\nYou can find both along the beaches nearby. Can't beat some good ol' fashioned local ingredients!","Gather 12 Murloc Eyes and 6 pieces of Sand Crawler Meat for Fimbo Greasemitz.",5},
[95125]={"These are some truly fine materials, $c. You honor me by allowing me to forge this blade for you and I only hope that I can live up to your expectations.\n\nPlease, stand back so that I may begin the forging process.","Watch as Ott forges your blade.",3},
[95126]={"Here's the blade. You said that a paladin named Trevan sent you? Please extend my thanks to him for this opportunity when you next see him. Go with honor, friend.","Bring Ott's Masterwork to Trevan Rol in Silverpine Forest.",3},
[95140]={"I see that you have your weapon now, $c. I pray that it will not fail you.\n\nThe locals tell me that Old Fire-Eye hunts in a large area south of here and you can generally find him near the gates to Gilneas. Find him, and use your new blade to end him. When it is done, return and you will have the gratitude of the Windshapers.","Use the Moonsilver Blade to destroy Old Fire-Eye in Silverpine Forest.",6},
[95141]={"Far to the northeast beyond Stonard lies an embattled land along the eastern coast known as the Riverglades.\n\nMany have sought to lay claim to these lands, but few have succeeded. There is one, however, whose experience battling our enemies proved enough to settle a small outpost known as Rog'mar. Through countless attacks, it still remains.\n\nAs ruthless as Krom'rosh may be, his will has served our allies greatly. If it's battle you seek, head northeast to seek out this old friend of ours.","Report to Krom'rosh at the Rog'mar outpost in the Riverglades.",1},
[95144]={"Hey, bub. Got a package that needs to go to an old friend of mine. Whatever you do--\n\nDO NOT OPEN THE PACKAGE!\n\nTake this--carefully--to Friz Frazzlespark across the seas over to our sister port in the Riverglades. And before you ask, no I would not suggest swimming. Didn't work out so well for the last guy. Oh, and don't tilt it, shake it, or make any sudden movements.\n\nI recommend heading east to Steamwheedle Port. The ship from there usually provides safe passage.\n\nBest of luck to ya!","Deliver Fizzgrimble's Mysterious Crate to Friz Frazzlespark at Powderfuse Port in the Riverglades.",1},
[95148]={"As much as I'd like to deliver the blood-soaked message to the knight commander himself, I'd also like to keep my post. I've cleaned it up a bit so it's less... well, bloody.\n\nGiven the recent gnoll uprisings, I'm afraid the task of delivering the news falls upon you.","Deliver the Southern Watch Gnoll Report to the knight commander at Farholde Keep.",1},
[95161]={"If you're looking for Jeremy Heartweaver, your best bet is to talk to his newly adopted mother, Avette Fellwood out in Duskwood. Sweet woman. Likely needs another pair of hands for her work, but it beats staying in the orphanage.\n\nIf you see little Jeremy, do be sure to tell him we're all thinking of him, won't you?","Deliver the Blood-Stained Letter to Avette Fellwood in Duskwood.",1},
[95183]={"You want ogre weapon? Me know no. You small. Can't hold good.\n\nYou bring Hamur more rocks, me make you tiny weapon. Good for tiny creature.\n\nFind good rocks for good weapon. Hamur has discerning eye. Not just any rock will do. Find rocks near river outside Bolder'ok.","Gather $1oa Good Rocks for Hamur in Bolder'ok.",3},
[95184]={"The rigors of training for battle are one thing, but these trainees don't yet understand the difference between a training sword and the well-kept blade of a seasoned veteran.\n\nI think it's time we show our recruits how a sharpened blade can be the difference between victory and death.\n\nIf you can find us a few sharpening stones, we'll put them to good use. There are certain craftsmen known to study this trade. I'd suggest starting there.","Bring $1oa Solid Sharpening Stones to Ember Bladewhisper at the Farholde training grounds.",5},
[95189]={"<A weathered crest depicting the mark of Lordaeron. With so few relics left after the kingdom's fall, someone in Stormwind would be very keen to get their hands on this.>","Return the Crest of Lordaeron to Lady Dena Kennedy in Stormwind City.",7},
[95195]={"<The old Alliance insignia appears to have belonged to a soldier of Lordaeron. These ruins are likely filled with similar medals that living relatives would be grateful to have returned to them.>","Collect $1oa Bloodied Insignias and take them to General Marcus Jonathan in Stormwind City.",7},
[95204]={"<A weathered crest depicting the mark of Lordaeron. With so few relics left after the kingdom's fall, someone in the Undercity would be very keen to get their hands on this.>","Bring the Crest of Lordaeron to Oran Snakewrithe in Undercity.",7},
[95212]={"We're getting ready to send a team of rams to reinforce the Alterac expedition, but we've run out of material to make their saddles.\n\nCollect pelts from the largest, fiercest leopards to the east and bring them to me. It's biting cold up there and our forces deserve nothing but the finest pelts to keep them warm!","Collect 6 Pristine Leopard Pelts and deliver them to Amberstill Ranch.",4},
[95216]={"Welcome to the most vital organ of the Undercity: The Apothecarium! Here we experiment on the most virulent of Azeroth's exotic specimens.\n\nYou've caught me in a good mood, so I will let you in on my latest investigation. It appears there is a particularly venomous arthropod stalking the ruins above our fair city. Its toxins are said to eat through even undead flesh. How exhilarating!\n\nI wish to validate these claims. Should you find yourself withering away from its bite, I should love a sample.","Collect the Highly Toxic Strain from Witherfang in Ruins of Lordaeron for Theodore Griffs in Undercity.",7},
[95217]={"So you're looking to learn the blacksmith's trade? Maybe we can help each other.\n\nThe supply shipment's late, and I need materials for some repairs around the camp. If you get me what I need, I'll teach you some of my techniques. Sound fair?","Collect 12 Copper Bars and 4 Toughened Boar Hides and deliver them to Frast Dokner.",4},
[95250]={"What do you want, $r? Can't you see there is a war to be won?\n\nMy master has already charged into the fray and has ordered me to maintain my post. It has been quite some time, however.\n\nI doubt you'll survive ten minutes in combat, but if it keeps your simple mind busy, why don't you seek out the Grand Marshal. He is the tallest, most statuesque hero you've ever laid eyes on. You'll know him when you see him.","Collect the Head of the Baron in the Ruins of Lordaeron and bring it back to Captain Truman.",5},
[95254]={"Calling all anglers!\n\nI'm in the market for some crab meat. Not just the usual shreds either, I'm talking whole claw. I've seen a big one crawling around under the docks, stealing bait and cutting lines.\n\nI'll pay a reward to anyone who brings me that thing's pincer. You'll also get a helping of the dish I whip up.\n\n-- Fimbo Greasemitz","Bring Trapclaw's Pincer to Fimbo Greasemitz.",5},
[95261]={"That monster...with the long neck, just like you said. I've seen 'im around those islands -- out on my boat. I tried <hic> tellin' folks, but ohh nooo, you can't <hic> believe ol' Argo. He's just some...some...drunkard fisherman! Makin' up stories!\n\nWe'll show 'em...soon as I get some bait...\n\nHey! Quit standin' around! I'm gonna need entrails, a LOT of 'em. Any beast from around here. The smellier <hic> the better. I'm also gonna need some Rotflesh mushrooms. Those grow in that cave by Windstead.","Collect $1oa Beast Entrails and $2oa Rotflesh Mushrooms for Argo Brinewhistle.",5},
[95262]={"Can't say I've ever thought much about Alcaz. Near as I can tell, it's an abandoned outpost from the third war of little significance. Never heard nuthin' about a prison there. \n\nWell, there's nothing for it--we've got to get you in there and see what you can see, especially if there's a chance that the king is there.","Enter Alcaz Prison and learn what became of the King of Stormwind.",6},
[95263]={"<The King is dead--killed in an escape attempt just before the Naga attacked. This is devastating news and will shake Stormwind to its core. You need to return to Sully and tell him what you've learned as quickly as possible.>","Return to Sully McCleary in Dustwallow Marsh.",2},
[95264]={"Shaw needs to know as soon as possible. Head back to Stormwind and deliver the news. Please, I beg ye, tell no one else. This could be disastrous for Stormwind and it needs to be handled delicately.","Bring the news to Matthias Shaw in Stormwind.",2},
[95267]={"The last part's <hic> easy...just take that big ball 'a guts, aaand chuck it in the water! Er...not here though...that'd be a disaster.\n\nGo to those <hic> murloc islands, where ya found the drawing. Look for fresh wreckage in the water. That's where you gotta throw the bait.\n\nSoon as that thing sticks its head up, chop it off! We'll make a decoration of it...for the boat!","Use the Big Ball o' Bait to lure out the sea monster. Then, bring its head to Argo Brinewhistle.",5},
[95283]={"Lok-tar, $n. I find myself in need of assistance with a serious matter. \n\nSome time ago we dispatched a contingent of Kor'kron Elite to Dustwallow Marsh on a special mission. The problem is, we are far past their scheduled check-in with no word from them.\n\nHead down to Brackenwall Village in Dustwallow Marsh and speak with an orc named Nazeer Bloodspike. No one is more knowledgeable about the state of Dustwallow than he. Find out what you can.","Speak with Nazeer Bloodspike in Brackenwall Village.",2},
[95284]={"A small force of Kor'kron soldiers passed through here a few days ago. Never told me why they were here, and I didn't ask. They bought supplies, took a bit of rest, then moved on.\n\nThe Kor'kron are the elite of the elite and tougher than elekk hooves, but I can't help feeling that something went wrong.\n\nI did overhear one of them mention \"the island\", and there's an island called Alcaz just off the coast. It's a really nasty place. Get some friends and look into what befell these Kor'kron.","Find the missing Kor'kron Elites.",2},
[95285]={"<Sergeant Ulka struggles to sit up to speak with you. You offer your hand in aid, but she merely swats it away.>\n\nAlright recruit... let's get you caught up.","Speak with Sergeant Ulka to learn more about the situation on Alcaz Isle.",2},
[95294]={"Friz sure knows how to get her point across. Well, you won't hear any objections from me. The Eastsea pirates won't interfere with her business. In exchange, maybe we can come to an arrangement. Pirating's a little difficult when you've got a scorned goblin sending marauding adventurers after you all day.\n\nRun along back to your master, $c. Let Friz know there's a new captain in charge, and he foresees a profitable relationship in our future.","Return to Friz Frazzlespark in Powderfuse Port.",1},
[95314]={"Before the Scourge invasion, the reclusive village of Shadowvale was known for its Whispering Elixir. Distilled from herbs found only in Tyr's Fall, the elixir was sought by apothecaries, mystics, and poisoners alike even after being banned in the city.\n\nI've had requests from a number of buyers eager to get their hands on some elixir. Travel to the ruins of Shadowvale deep in the Whispering Forest to the west. I'm prepared to offer significant compensation if you can recover some bottles for me.","Collect $1oa Bottles of Whispering Elixir from Shadowvale, then return to Carolai Anise in Brill.",5},
[95315]={"Word from one of our scouts suggests a large force of enemies amassing to the far, far south, well beyond the Wetlands.\n\nEven more curious is there appears to be an alliance settlement out there. Farholde? The name sounds familiar.\n\nLet's not wait on this. Best to begin the conversation before it's too late. We're dealing with enough here as it is.\n\nTake this correspondence and deliver it to whoever claims to be the leader of this detachment.","Deliver Captain Nials' Correspondence to Demar Brant at Farholde Keep along the southeastern coast in the Riverglades.",1},
[95318]={"So in order to really disrupt operations here and get me out of this cage, we're going to have to kill four very powerful mortals. This cage has demonic wards on it that won't be dispelled until all four are dead, and that key can't be used until the wards are down.\n\nLook, you seem like |5$r that can hold your own but I'm going to need a bit more convincing that you can actually take on these stupid warlocks before I give you any good info.\n\nLike killing a ton of these warlocks for starters. Easy, no?","Slay $1oa Ashen Acolytes.",5},
[95319]={"Listen, I know you can smell the fel blood pools behind me and I'm sure you've seen the crystals that grow out of them. These crystals have special properties from the ashes of Archimonde that rain down on this side of the hill.\n\nSomething about how they are formed makes them especially good at draining fel energies, which is a big problem for someone like me, but they can still have their uses.\n\nI want you to gather some for me. Try and get a few kinds. I'll know what I need when I see it.","Gather $1oa Fel-Slime Crystals and $2oa Pristine Fel-Slime Crystal.",5},
[95322]={"Your timin' couldn't be better, friend. I was just on my way to collect my shipment from the Bloodsail Buccaneers. They're good friends of mine. Always happy to supply anything Friz is willin' to pay for.\n\nBut, ahem, just in case, it couldn't hurt for you to be my liaison. A good caravaneer knows it doesn't hurt to show off a little muscle. Just as a deterrent, of course.\n\nThey said they left my stuff in a chest on the hill outside of town for safekeepin'. Why don't you take a look for me, eh?","Find the Bloodsail Trunk outside of Booty Bay in Stranglethorn Vale.",4},
[95325]={"I already spent good coin on that crate. We ain't just going to let them have it!\n\nYou want your shipment? Go to the Venture Co's camp up north and find out who's responsible for this backstabbin'! This ain't about money anymore, $n. This is about justice! And maybe a little about the money.","Find the Venture Co. Ledger in the Venture Co. Camp near Lake Nezferiti in Stranglethorn.",4},
[95327]={"Looks like a deal's a deal. The Venture Co. got their comeuppance, Friz gets her loot, and everybody's happy. Overall a pretty smooth transaction if I do say so myself.\n\nNow scram, I got another shipment comin' in soon from some Southsea Pirates.","Return to Friz Frazzlespark at Powderfuse Port in the Riverglades.",5},
[95378]={"It is time to cut off the heads of this hydra, if you catch my meaning.\n\nThere are three leaders who need to be killed in order to slow the operations here. Conveniently, they also need to be slain to remove the wards on my cage.\n\nTyaeha can be found in the House of Diseases by the creepy tree. Dazka is in the Alchemist ward with all the potions, and that fool Frezzlie is undoubtedly next to the slime pits along the northern ridge of the encampment.\n\nGo slay them and bring me their bones!","Retrieve the bones of Frezzlie Popwhiz, Tyaeha Darkoath and Dazka Shadowsleep.",5},
[95379]={"Brashann Grimdark, Master of Vessels.\n\n<Felflick's mouth curls into a snarl.>\n\nHe was the one to subjugate me at the summit. HE is the reason I am here in the first place.\n\nHis work with these fel-ash crystals are the backbone of this operation. He's been obsessively experimenting with anchoring souls in these crystals and his work has not gone unnoticed by those Blackthorne creeps.\n\nUse this pristine crystal to drain his power, then put an end to him and bring me his soulstone.","Slay Brashann Grimdark and search his body for his soulstone.",5},
[95383]={"<Wharfmaster Steamfizzle inspects the coin you offered him.>\n\nWhoa-ho! Ol' Friz sure is training the new generation right. Apologies for the delay, $Gsir:ma'am;. You're here to deliver a crate to someone in town, right? I don't know anythin' about that, but if I did, I'd go talk with Tazzik on the dock. He seems to be interested in things like that.\n\nBut be quick about it though, yeah? Don't need folks gettin' the wrong idea, ya know.","Deliver Friz's Secret Stash to Tazzik in Steamwheedle Port.",1},
[95384]={"<The strange symbols on the magical scroll confound you. Though you do not speak the language recorded, you don't sense any particularly volatile forces within. Perhaps a collector of odd magics would find some use for the scroll.>","Bring the partial scroll to Dudd Fizzlescroll in Booty Bay.",5},
[95385]={"<Faint magic emanates from the scrap of scroll. The language is unfamiliar, though you intuit that it is not dangerous. Most would find the parchment useless, but there may be a unique collector that may find some use out of it.>","Bring the partial scroll to Dudd Fizzlescroll in Booty Bay.",5},
[95417]={"Clubtoe see friends go. Some no come back. Some come back purple. Dat weird. Purple ones no act like friends no more.\n\nWhere others go? Why they no come back? Make Clubtoe think.\n\nYou hit hard. Maybe you go find friends in cave? Maybe you turn purple. Dat weird too.","Find missing ogres in the caves beneath Sunnyglade for Clubtoe.",1},
[95418]={"Me done with Twilight. Clubtoe free ogre now.\n\nMe go find Clugfist. He biggestest ogre Clubtoe ever see. He leave Twilight. Take many friends with him. It Clubtoe's turn. Me join free ogres. They go to the hills. Clubtoe miss hills. No more smashing rocks. Maybe you come sometime?\n\nMe stay here till coast is clear. You take Chogg'Zac's heads back to friends. Well. Maybe one head. Me get one too. Fair trade.","Deliver the head of Chogg to Tran'gul in Rog'mar.",1},
[95420]={"Clearly these wayward ogres are no friends to the Twilight's Hammer. We orcs have an honored history fighting alongside ogres, and it may be time to call upon those old alliances again. And this head may be the key.\n\nThere have been reports of ogre activity in the hills far to the north. If this Clubtoe is to be believed, that must be where this clan calls home. Go to their stronghold and offer this trophy as a token of our friendship. With luck, they will listen to your proposal before they step on you.","Deliver Chogg's head to the ogre city to the north.",1},
[95424]={"Here ogres value strength and blood.\n\nWeak ones leave Bolder'ok. Go back to Twilight's Hammer.\n\nYou no big. Maybe you strong. Show Clugfist strength and smash weak ogres. If tiny creature can.","Kill $1oa Twilight Maulers and $2oa Twilight Firecallers for Clugfist in Bolder'ok.",5},
[95425]={"Klunk once Clugfist's greatest champion. Him strong. Me give Klunk mighty weapon.\n\nBut Clugfist wrong. Klunk weak like others. He leave Bolder'ok. Return to Twilight's Hammer. Take ogres with him to cave east to water. Take mighty weapon with him!\n\nThat Clugfist weapon! Bash Klunk's skull and take back Skullbasher. He nobody's champion!","Collect Skullthumper from Klunk for Clugfist in Bolder'ok.",5},
[95431]={"As I've shadowed our enemy's movements, I have discovered a weakness among their ranks. Ogre dissidents have begun to rebel, seeking the same freedom as their Bolder'ok kin. Word of your deeds has spread. We must exploit this.\n\nI spied a Bolder'ok warrior heading to the caves west of here in search of his brothers and sisters. Find him, and join his efforts to rally his people.","Look for the Bolder'ok ogre in the nearby cave.",1},
[95432]={"When Crag'rog hear $r-ling free ogres, Crag'og want free ogres too.\n\nWith tiny $c here, we smash Twilight together. Break them bones. Make them scream. Free ogres! Then be home in time for stew.","Recruit $1oa Ogre Miners.",3},
[95494]={"I need someone with a strong sword arm and some extra time on their hands to help me gather some lion hides. It stings my pride to ask a stranger for this aid, but I took an injury to my leg recently. Until I heal, I'm in no shape to go hunting myself but I have obligations to keep.\n\nThe big ones in this area generally have the best hides, so start with those first.","Collect 6 Savannah Lion Hides from the Savannah Matriarchs and Savannah Patriarchs in the Barrens.",5},
[95495]={"These hides are bound for a tanner who I often trade with. He is something of a hermit and he lives alone on the top of the ridge behind me. Climbing up a steep hillside isn't something I can manage easily right now so I'd be in your debt if you could make this delivery for me.\n\nOh, and about this tanner's... appearance. You need not be alarmed. In spite of his looks, he is no threat. I swear this is true.","Bring the Bundle of Hides to the hermit on the ridge overlooking the Dry Hills in the Barrens.",1},
[95508]={"Yes, I used to be a member of the Kul Tiras navy. After Lord Admiral took Theramore and started his campaign in Durotar, I had... \"objections\" to his methods. Particularly the methods involving executing civilians.\n\nThere's more to the story but... wait... what's that?\n\nThere's a group of men coming up the ridge!","Help Walton survive the encounter with Terry Longdrink and the Kul Tiras marines.",5},
[95534]={"<The note is singed in places, but is still readable.>\n\nRumor has it those old bellows have a mind of their own, springing to life when no one is watching. I don't care if it's a ghost story, you'd better get to the bottom of it before I return.\n\nThere's great power in Strahnbrad, I know it.\n\n< The rest of the note is singed and torn, as if burnt by fire magic. >","Solve the mystery of Strahnbrad and report your findings in town in Hillsbrad.",5},
[95561]={"<The loud cries of baby Dawnbright echo through Farholde Keep. Tessa looks at you with a tired smile.>\n\nOh, hello there adventurer. Sorry for the noise. Little Emma here seems to be quite fussy today, but I'm not sure why. Maybe some food will help.\n\nDo you think you could help me find something for her to eat? My husband stepped out to get some supplies so my hands are a little too full to get them myself. If you could find a few apples around here I could make a lovely mash for her.","Collect $1oa Fresh Apples for Tessa Dawnbright in Farholde Keep.",3},
[95569]={"The owls are under threat by the fel corruption that afflicts the mountainside, and the creatures poisoned and enraged by those energies. Many owls have abandoned their nests for safer places higher up the mountain. Others have fallen in defense of their young.\n\nFor the owls to have a future, their eggs must be protected and their fledglings nurtured. Bring the abandoned eggs to me. You may find eggs in abandoned nests at the base of trees north and east of here.","Rescue $1oa Hyjal Owl Eggs and bring them to Ketharas.",5},
[95601]={"<This dead ogre must be one of the friends Clubtoe was looking for. The Twilight's Hammer seem to be conducting rituals on their members, empowering some and killing more.\n\nThese ritualists and their monstrosities must be stopped before they spread.>","Kill $1oa Empowered Brutes and $2oa Twilight Ritualists then return to Clubtoe in Sunnyglade.",5},
[95602]={"Me hate smashing rock. All day me smash. Chogg'Zac say so. He big boss. Say we smash tinies, but now we work for tinies. That stupid.\n\nWhy smash rock? Me no know. Find shiny light in rocks. Chogg'Zac like shiny, me guess. Are you here for shiny light too? Others won't like that. They really like light. They draw pictures with it.\n\nClubtoe not get it. Light make Clubtoe feel sick. Me hate light. Me want SMASH shiny pictures! But Chogg'Zac be mad. Squish Clubtoe. That bad. But someone should.","Destroy $1oa Twilight Ritual Circles found throughout the caves underneath Sunnyglade.",5},
[95603]={"Since brother Lowley and I began serving Farholde in a more secular capacity, the church here has fallen into disuse. I'd like to think that once the fighting is over, we will be able to bring the Light back to this place. Although, I fear that may not be for a long while...\n\nStill, we need to keep the church in working order, in the hope that day will come.\n\nTo that end, a colony of bats has taken to roosting in the upper stories of the church. It would be a great help if you could remove them.","Kill 5 Roosting Duskbats in the Farholde Cathedral for Sister Rowland.",4},
[95621]={"This morning I spotted a group of humans searching for something in the valley below. I managed to use my rifle's scope for a better look, and it was clear that they were soldiers sporting the livery of Kul Tiras. \n\nIf you'd be willing to take work from me, travel to where these soldiers made camp near the wrecked caravan to the south. Kill any you find and try to learn why they are here.","Travel to the wrecked caravan and learn more about why the Kul Tirans are here.",4},
[95642]={"You there! Thank the light you've come. Did Amberhall send you to find me?\n\nNo? Figures as much. Ashe Amberhall sent me down here to investigate the Twilight's Hammer. As you can see, they are digging for something within the Riverglades, but I need a sample of their witchcraft to figure out what.\n\nIt's imperative Farholde gets those samples. Please, $c. Take this catalyst. It's enchanted to absorb the powers of the cult. Runes, cultists, it doesn't matter. Just hold it aloft and it will do the rest.","Absorb $1oa samples into the Crystal Catalyst from Twilight's Hammer cultists and Twilight Ritual Circles in the cave underneath Sunnyglade for Apprentice Claire.",5},
[95643]={"As Lady Amberhall's apprentice in the dark arts, I may not look it but I'm usually quite capable of handling things on my own. I did not, however, anticipate an entire cave of void-infused ogres.\n\nIf you managed to get all the way down here without being captured, you must be powerful yourself. I was not so lucky with those ogres and their masters roaming about. Do the world a favor and kill the hideous beasts. Nothing good comes from a fanatic with a purpose, empowered or otherwise.","Kill $1oa Twilight Ritualists and $1oa Empowered Brutes within the caves underneath Sunnyglade.",5},
[95646]={"These brackish wetlands hold a greater well of unsalted southern waters. It pains me, yet within my roots I sense a corruption seeping through that mountain gully.\n\nThe creatures, like those in our lowlands, react more bitterly to the taint. Lacking the sea's hardening salt since life's dawn, they have little strength against such evil.\n\nGo to those highlands, and bring me the Highland Horror's root core.","Kill a Highland Horror within Excavation Sites and bring its root core to Rethiel the Greenwarden in the Wetlands.",6},
[95647]={"My husband, Ardin, has a rare gift for sensing nature. He'll scale any peak to gather the herbs and flowers I need for my alchemy, keeping our shelves and pantry stocked.\n\nBut I fear he's wandered into trouble. An excavation crew passed through seeking supplies. They spoke, among other things, of towering grasses unlike anything they'd ever seen. Those were what he told me he had to go see for himself. He's been gone too long!\n\nIf you learn anything of him, I'd be grateful.","Find Ardin Grassman in the Excavation Sites.",5},
[95663]={"The Dragonmaw are a formidable clan.\n\nThey're known for binding magic strong enough to make dragons serve, and rumor claims they're preparing some display of it in the Wetlands. Whether truth or bluster, the Deathstalkers can't act on half-formed whispers. Broken symbols carried only that much to me.\n\nA deathstalker agent needs a hand in the hills above the Dragonmaw encampment. Meet her there. She'll reveal the next steps.","Travel to the Wetlands and meet the Deathstalker Agent in the hills above the Dragonmaw camp.",1},
[95697]={"Zamja tells me we need more homestyle cooking.\nIf we start selling raptor, she thinks it'll draw in customers who don't usually visit Borstan's Firepit.\n\nHer idea is not so bad. But I want something that rises above the smells of our birth villages. We're in Orgrimmar! Borstan should serve a grand take on their familiar favorites.\n\nA hunter recently came back from the Wetlands with a giant talon from the thicket raptors in the Excavation Sites.\n\nUp for a job?","Enter the Excavation Sites in the Wetlands and bring back Thicket Raptor Meat.",6},
[95737]={"From time to time, I correspond with others in my craft--herbalists or eccentrics who study rare plants and local oddities. We trade discoveries, and sometimes warnings of what lies ahead.\n\nOne alchemist in the Wetlands wrote of an excavation team her husband was part of, uncovering signs of a long-lost primordial grass... but she never sent word of its abundance or accessibility.\n\nIf you can, check on Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor.","Speak with Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor.",2},
[95748]={"This is odd. This piece of the tablet you have brought me refers to the lost city of I'lalai as if it is a massive sprawling civilization. But the ruins off of the reef are not large enough to be something of that size.\n\n$n, to the north of the Vile Reef there is an ancient troll ruin on the hills along the coast. A tablet that contains legends of the lost troll city is within. I wish to study this legend further.\n\nTake this hide and charcoal to create a rubbing of this tablet, then return to me.","Use the hide and charcoal to create a rubbing of the Third Troll Legend tablet.",5},
[95753]={"<The totem pulses with wild magic. The image of a ghostly wolf appears in your mind, beckoning you. \n\nIt appears to be offering you a challenge.\n\nAnother totem--a twin to the one that your hand now rests upon, appears in the distance just beyond the large sun-bleached skeleton nearby.>","Reach the other Odd Totem at the end of the massive skeleton before time runs out.",3},
[95766]={"The cycle of renewal has finally begun. The ancients... shall rise again, and the power of the natural world take its course... to bloom.\n\nYou... have helped us tip the scales in nature's favor. Perhaps... we can yet make a larger impact... on a more dire situation.\n\nHead west... where the land itself is ashen... and you may find an entity who can help. She may look like just a small bird... but her power is great.","Find the strange bird in the corrupted lands on the southwest slope.",1},
[95769]={"Every day be a challenge when you living rough like we do! Takes a toll on your tools, your clothes, your whole life. Good thing it can't take our spirit!\n\nWe be really hurting from our clothes and blankets wearing out. You do some tailoring, right? So maybe you can bring me some Bolts of Runecloth and I can fix a few holes?","Bring $1oa Bolts of Runecloth to Mez'dan in Elderwild on Mount Hyjal.",3},
[95770]={"After rereading the legend, it doesn't seem like we are in the wrong place for the lost city, but perhaps there is yet some detail that has been overlooked.\n\nIn my younger years I used to dive in the Vile Reef ruins, but that was before the murlocs settled there. If memory serves there was a cavern there.\n\nI have heard that there are now naga gathering in that region, which is unusual. I want to know what has lured them there.\n\nGo and explore just west of the Vile Reef and return to me with any news.","Explore the Vile Reef and find the cavern entrance.",5},
[95771]={nil,nil,5},
[95772]={"Me brother tried draggin' me off tae the Wetlands with some diggin' crew out o' Loch Modan. Said they were headin' into hills no dwarf's ever set boot in for some sort o' excavation.\n\nAye, I'd 'ave gone, if I wasn't already behind on this pile o' girdles I've got to refit.\n\nDaewyn normally writes after he sends off, though. Haven't heard a thing, gives me a strange feelin' this time.\n\nIf yer marchin' that way, mind checking in on me brother?","Look for Dorin Songblade's brother, Daewyn, in Whelgar's Excavation Site.",6},
[95774]={"The healer who saved me could not save her, and she has died in battle. Her name is Olgra, and I will never forget her.\n\nYou did not find her adornments on her body? She wore many jewels of polished bone.\n\nSlay the Razormane Raiders near where she fell, and find her precious works of art!\n\nI will place them with the memorial that I build in her memory.","Slay quilboars and collect $1oa of Olgra's Adornments for Mankrik's memorial.",5},
[95775]={"What I am about to ask you is no small feat, $c, and will likely require strong allies to accomplish.\n\nI want to know more about the ruins on the other side of the cavern the naga are guarding. If my suspicions prove correct, it could indeed be the lost city of I'lalai. The amount of lost historical knowledge at our fingertips could be unrivaled, but I am too old to venture myself.\n\nEnter the ruins and gather etchings of any tablets you find there, then return to me.","Use the hide and charcoal to create rubbings of the tablets found in the Drowned City.",5},
[95776]={"You have done well to slay the naga just off of our coast, but the fact that they are in our waters in such numbers means there is yet a larger threat.\n\nI have spoken to Kin'weelay, and he thinks these Brinescale naga are infiltrating the ruins of the Drowned City. If the naga are there, then they are up to no good and are likely searching for something.\n\nWe can't let them get their hands on anything that could compromise us here and it is time to put an end to this. Slay their leader and return to me.","Slay Var'Taka in the Drowned City.",6},
[95787]={"<Loremaster Dibbs' hands shake as he reads the scouting report and the troll legends.>\n\nCould it be? By this account it sounds like the lost troll city of I'lalai has risen just off the coast of Stranglethorn! We must investigate immediately. Why, if my research is correct this could be the archeological discovery of the century!\n\nPlease, I know it is a long trek back to Stranglethorn but if you find yourself in this Drowned City, collect any legends you find there and return them to me.","Use the hide and charcoal to create rubbings of the tablets found in the Drowned City.",5},
[95788]={"The Skullsplitter fetishes Brother Nimetz sent with you are indeed powerful, though I do not think they contributed to Kurzen's condition, or at least not directly.\n\nStill, if the rumors are true and the lost troll city of I'lalai has indeed risen from its watery grave, it is possible the dark magics used to raise the doomed city may be related.\n\nIf you dare to venture into the Drowned City of I'lalai, please gather any troll fetishes you find and bring them here to me for further study.","Collect $1oa I'lalai Fetishes from trolls in the Drowned City.",5},
[95789]={"Hey pal, you look like you can handle yourself in a fight.\n\nBaron Revilgaz has me keep'n my ear to the ground for magical objects. Word on the street is that a sunken troll ruin has mysteriously become, eh, un-sunk, which means there are a lot of unclaimed goods, if you catch my meaning.\n\nProblem is, it's also caught the eye of pirates! Not just any pirates, the Saltseers specifically collect magical artifacts. I need you to go into the Drowned City, clear them out and take their stolen artifacts.","Collect $1oa Voodoo Infused Artifacts from Saltseer pirates in the Drowned City.",6},
[95791]={"The Saltseer pirates have been a thorn in my side recently and knowing they're in the Drowned City makes it worse! I mean they're always bad news, but there is one captain in particular I want outta the picture. That damned Captain Dreadrise!\n\nHe and his crew are very accomplished at gathering all the magical artifacts I've been after, and I'm tired of the competition.\n\nI want you to remove Captain Dreadrise and his Saltseer Coroners from the picture. Permanently.","Slay 3 Saltseer Coroners and Captain Dreadrise in the Drowned City.",6},
[95793]={"Ah, a $c. I see great strength and determination in you--qualities necessary to rid these lands of evil.\n\nThe demons that walked these lands during the great battle were defeated, yet some still remain. It is important to prevent them from escaping.\n\nThe ruins to the east are dangerous. Carry your strength into their den. Destroy the unwelcome before our lands perish.","Slay $1oa Felguard Sentinels in Dae'gun.",5},
[95795]={"<You cover the dwarf's body with his cloak.>\n\nTravel to Lakeshire and personally inform Dorin Songblade what became of his brother within the Excavation Sites.","Return to Dorin Songblade.",6},
[95798]={"$n, I want you to take this I'lalai Fetish to my friend Abra in Dalaran. I would love to have her examine it if she has the time to do so.\n\nShe is also particularly interested in troll practices and magic, so I believe this discovery will be exciting for her to unravel.\n\nDo be careful, though. The Kirin Tor can be a bit particular about who they let into their grand city. If you haven't already become a noteworthy visitor, you may need to find a way into their good graces.","Bring the I'lalai Fetish to Abra Cadabra in Dalaran.",4},
[95803]={"Now that we've claimed the head of the tarnished commander, I need you to deliver it to the Undercity. Sylvanas Windrunner mistrusts us greatly, and all but openly disparages us.\n\nDeliver Rudolph Gelhardt's head to the Dark Lady. Show her that we tend to our own house and are devoted to the prosperity of the forsaken.","Bring the head of Rudolph Gelhardt to Sylvanas Windrunner in the Undercity.",5},
[95809]={"I need a moment to rest before I find my own way out.\n\n<He pulls some reeds from his pack and quickly braids and bends them into a heart.>\n\nTake this, and bring it back to Caitlin. Let her know I'll be home soon! Now that we have a path cleared out thanks to you, I'll gather my bushels and follow your trail.\n\nThank you.","Return to Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor.",6},
[95810]={"You pick up a fractured piece of the rock-mech automaton. It has a texture unlike anything you've touched before, a composite material of unknown makeup. This is certainly bound to be more 'device' than 'debris.'\n\nProspector Whelgar himself at his excavation site might have something useful to share about the relic.","Bring the Titan Relic to Prospector Whelgar in the Wetlands excavation site.",2},
[95882]={"An Alliance scouting party has been seen on a small island northeast of Rog'mar. They are led by a scoutmaster who has made tracking enemy movements increasingly difficult. The bastard even named his filthy pet after me as an open mockery. He knows I'm hunting him.\n\nThis human has eyes everywhere, and they need to be put out. I already claimed one before he managed to flee. Bring me his other as proof that the scoutmaster is no more. Show him he is not as untouchable as he thinks.\n\n-- Neza Bloodsnout","Bring the Scoutmaster's Eye to Neza Bloodsnout in Rog'mar.",6},
[95883]={"<The preparations for a hastily-assembled ritual are gathered unceremoniously on the altar. According to the scrap of note, everything has been gathered. All that's missing are the offering of blood and the Tortured Soul.\n\nThe undead around you look tortured enough. They may have what you seek.>","Collect a Tortured Soul from the nearby undead in Beren's Peril in Silverpine Forest.",4},
[95885]={"<All that's left now is the offering of blood.\n\nThe note scrap mentioned a 'willing sacrifice.'\n\nAn intense sense of dread washes over you.>","Use the Tortured Soul to give an offering of blood at the Offering Stone in Beren's Peril.",5},
[95924]={"Ye there! Aye, I'm talkin' ta ye! We've made the discovery of a lifetime down in Un'Goro! Can ye believe it?\n\nThere's just one problem... our dig site's been overrun by voracious beasts of the killin' nature. Very unpleasant indeed.\n\nWith yer help, we can reclaim our camp and git back ta workin'. Now, what do ye say? I'll make it worth yer while.","Slay 6 Ravasaur Matriarchs, 9 Ironhide Ravasaurs and Venomridge in Shaper's Terrace.",5},
[95925]={"$C, we've made the discovery of a lifetime! I can't believe it; the ruins in Un'Goro are open!\n\nWe've already sent a team but they have encountered... trouble. If you're headed in there anyway would ya be able to finish this map?\n\nIt sounds like there's an Achromatic Crystal in there and an unearthed watcher somewhere near a giant Western Gate that sounds interesting.\n\nThe other landmarks that would be helpful are the Pillar of Assimilation, the Western Gate and the Regrowth Vestibule.","Find Interesting Landmarks in Shaper's Terrace and fill out the explorer's map at each.",5},
[95934]={"My surveying tools show signs of a never-before-seen mineral in these caves. Cubic draconia, I call it. Probably worth a fortune.\n\nExciting as this is, no one's gonna come help me dig it up if I can't show 'em proof that it exists. Sure, I have the readings from my tools, but people like to hold a big shiny crystal, not look at charts.\n\nI'm sure there's a few crystals poking up from the dirt in there. If you're willing to dodge a few dragons and get one, you'd really be helpin' a gal out.","Find a piece of Cubic Draconia for Gelinda Coppergleam.",5},
[95943]={"G'day, $Glad:lass;. Name's Bertrand, Bertrand Ironbrow! At yer service.\n\n<Bertrand extends a filthy hand.>\n\nThese fine folk contracted me tae oversee construction of this here keep. What they lack in experience they make up for in spirit! Problem is, I misplaced me tools.\n\nHad a bit of a run in with a few Twilight in a small grove northwest o' here. Had to choose between me life or me tools. On one hand, I'm alive. On the other... ye see where this is goin'.\n\nThink ye could help find me tools?","Locate the Foreman's Crate and return it to Bertrand Ironbrow in Farholde Keep.",4},
[95951]={"'Ey boss-$Gmon:lady;, ya need help from ol' Tan'jani? Don't worry about it, I fix you up good.\n\nOrcs be good at hittin' humans with axes, but when you wanna stick 'em before dey see ya comin', that's when you call on the headhunters. You wanna learn to stick 'em too? I see it in your eyes, heheh.\n\nFirst we get you your own spears. Dis one's mine. Go to the human camp to de west and take their wood. Take knife with ya. You can sharpen their lumber into good spears for stickin'. Den bring 'em back.","Collect Wood Bundles from Peasant Woodpiles in Turner's Logging Camp then fletch them into $1oa Makeshift Stickin' Spears.",5},
[95955]={"You got de spears, now ya gonna learn how to throw dem.\n\nDe Riverglades be full o' crocolisks. Nasty tings. Snap you up if ya ain't quick. Perfect for target practice, heheh.\n\nGo stick yourself a bunch of dem. Den you come back to ol' Tran'jani for ya prize. If ya can stick a crocolisk, ya can stick any'ting.","Impale $1oa Freshwater Crocolisks then return to Tran'jani in Rog'mar.",5},
[95975]={"Tess says little Emm can't sleep without me? And you did all that for them? A total stranger? Damn it. What was I thinking...\n\nEven if I can't guarantee a perfect world for her, I still need to be a part of it. What am I even fighting for if I can't hope for a brighter future?\n\nThank you for helping my family in my absence, friend, but it's time for me to go home. If I could ask one more favor, can you pick some flowers and take them to Tess? Let her know I'll be home soon? I need to clean up first.","Gather $1oa Wildflowers and deliver them to Tessa Dawnbright in Farholde Keep.",5},
[95981]={"Taking away their pendants is just the first step. If the Kirin Tor really are shipping a steady supply of relics from Dalaran, we must stop them at the source.\n\nSearch the roads around Ambermill for Dalaran's wizards and watchers. Their presence has allowed free access across our borders for too long. If we can cull their numbers, that should put a stop to these pendants making it into Silverpine Forest in the first place.","Slay $1oa Dalaran Wizards and $2oa Dalaran Watchers for Shadow Priest Allister in the Sepulcher.",5},
[95982]={"Folks keep dumpin' their furry friends here like I know what I'm doin'. And then they blame me if they come back and their horse or wolf or... whatever they brought is dead or ran off. What do I look like, I'm runnin' a charity?\n\nYou look like you know your way around a trough. Mind whippin' me up some grub I can use to keep these beasties in check?\n\nIf you can't make it yourself, someone might be willin' to sell you some. And hurry! Last thing I need is a stampede of hungry animals.","Bring $1oa Briny Seafood Stew to Jasper Geartoggle in Powderfuse Port.",5},
[95983]={"The skeleton is badly mangled. Deep markings on its limbs vaguely match patterns of teeth and claws. Many days beneath the beating sun have made the bones pale and brittle as well. The brutality of both the attacker and the weather have rendered the victim's identity a mystery.\n\nYou can't take the whole skeleton with you, but you could bring its skull to the nearby watchman and see what he knows.","Bring the Gnawed Skull to Watcher Cornelius at Terral's Watch.",2},
[95986]={"The whistle's made, $n. \n\nTake it, and go to the top of the hill where the lions are. Should be just north of here.\n\nOnce you're there, blow the whistle, and our man-eater should appear. I'd tell you not to come back if you don't manage to kill him, but you'll probably be dead anyhow.\n\nNow then, off with you. Let's see if you fare better than our skeletal friend.","Use the Tallstrider Call to call forth the leader of the lion pride. Slay the beast and retrieve its hide for Watcher Cornelius at Terral's Watch.",5},
[95992]={"Dese waters be treacherous. My headhunters keep the paths clear as dey can, but there be a beasty stalkin' de rivers even we cannot catch. Excitin', eh?\n\nBoss say we gotta clear it out, so we got a little competition goin'. Find de white one patrollin' de rivers and bring me its fang. Whoever sticks this slippery crocolisk win de whole pot. Just don't get snapped yourself, heheh!\n\n-- Tan'jani","Bring Ghostmaw's Fang to Tan'jani in Rog'mar.",6},
[95998]={"Well howdy there, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. Good for you. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nIt's a big wide world out there and you'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful. Not sure how your outdoorsman skills are but I reckon I could teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire, get comfy. I'll walk you through it.","Sit near Sam's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.",4},
[95999]={"Wanted! Incinerator Gar'im, Leader of an orc incursion in Render's Valley. Purported to be working with the Blackrock of Stonewatch Keep.\n\nBeware of Incinerator Gar'im. He and his Shadowcasters are extremely dangerous. A handsome reward will be given to any brave soul that can deliver proof of Incinerator Gar'im's demise to Magistrate Solomon.","Deliver the Broken Staff of Incinerator Gar'im to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire.",6},
[96010]={"Although I am sure we can attribute the damage to both pylons to the reckless centaur stomping about, I suspect the timing of their rampage resulted in the shards being separated. I know little about their quarrels, but I do know there are at least two main factions that have trespassed into Shen'dralas: the ferocious Magram and the cunning Gelkis.\n\nKeeping these treasures in the midst of a battlefield would be unwise. By now, I am assuming they have taken their trophies back to their own villages.","Recover shards and fragments of the pylons, found guarded at the Magram and Gelkis villages. Return them to Mordent Evenshade.",4},
[96015]={"We should be thankful that our foe is stupid. An army of ogres at their disposal, and the Twilight's Hammer have them working in the mines nowhere near the fight. I don't know if I chalk it up to mismanagement or an internal struggle, but either way they're in no position to defend themselves.\n\nThat's where we come in. With the cult's focus divided, we have an opportunity to strike the enemy while they're vulnerable and split them further. Go to this mine and sow some chaos among their ranks.","Defeat $1oa Ogre Miners and $2oa Twilight Subjugators in the cave near the Twilight's Shroud for Sergeant Riftan.",5},
[96026]={"Dese good rock. Now need finishing touch. More rock.\n\nOnly rock can make rock stronger. Dat the way of rocks.\n\nMe see some tinies make extra heavy rock. Bring me heavy rocks and me make weapon.","Deliver $1oa Heavy Weightstones to Hamur in Bolder'ok.",4},
[96031]={"You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\n\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.","Speak with Gretta Finespindle in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[96047]={"So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a $c.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.","Speak with Thamner Pol in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[96055]={"Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.","Speak with Reyna Stonebranch in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[96059]={"Now that you've begun your journey into being an enchanter, I reckon I can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp once you've learned the ropes.\n\nIt's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.","Speak with Thonys Pillarstone in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[96067]={"You may have noticed my mechanical companion here, G45-B4G. Whirlin' around in that burlap chest of his is the one, and only, working prototype of my gas-powered engine.\n\nI figure it's in need of some stress testing. How'd you like to take him on in a fight? I can power him up with the gas you've collected.\n\nOh, and don't worry about hurting him. He can't feel a thing!","Help Sleebo test his creation.",4},
[96078]={"$n, we Darkspear keep much of our traditions alive by oral storytelling. We pass legends such as these to the next generation, teaching lessons and weaving cautionary tales to our younglings.\n\nThese etchings must be taken to our spiritual leader, Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village. He is one of the wisest Darkspear and he will wish to hear the truth of this tale.\n\nI have prepared an extra copy of this tale for you as well. If you ever lose your copy, I would be happy to create another, for a small fee.","Take the tablet etchings to Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village in Durotar.",4},
[96082]={"I will fashion the cloth you've given me into bandages. In the meantime, please take these ones that I have already made, and dress the wounds of the soldiers who need it. It should be a matter of basic first aid.\n\nYour assistance here is both necessary, and highly appreciated. I simply cannot be everywhere at once.","Bandage up 3 Wounded Soldiers for Brother Lowley.",3},
[96084]={"I will spare you the grisly details, but these soldiers are violently ill. The nature of their sickness leads me to believe there is an issue with either their food or their water.\n\nI've already checked the crops coming in from the nearby farms, so this only leaves the water, which comes from the local rivers. The best place to collect a sample is from the pools in the plains to the north. Nearly every river runs through the area, so it would be wise to check for contamination there.","Collect a sample of drinking water from the plains for Sister Rowland at the chapel in Farholde Keep.",5},
[96101]={"Greetings, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.","Sit near Raan's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.",4},
[96102]={"Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\n\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.","Speak with Snang in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[96104]={"These markings are from a lion. By the look of them, this one is especially large--the leader of the nearby pride.\n\nI would gladly hunt the beast myself, but you have first claim. Instead, I will aid you.\n\nI can make a whistle that mimics the call of a wounded tallstrider. You can use it to lure the lion out. I'll just need one of their beaks to give it the right sound.\n\nThere are tallstriders all over the plains. Find me a beak and the hunt can begin!","Bring an Intact Tallstrider Beak to Neza Bloodsnout at Rog'mar.",5},
[96105]={"The whistle is made, $n.\n\nTake it and go to the top of the hill south where the lions dwell.\n\nOnce you are ready to face your quarry, blow the whistle and the beast should appear.\n\nI wish you luck in your hunt. May you return in glory.","Use the Tallstrider Call to call forth the leader of the lion pride. Slay the beast and retrieve its hide for Neza Bloodsnout at Rog'mar.",5},
[96108]={"Arrows are always essential, but sometimes you need something more potent to take down your prey.\n\nThis is where poison coatings come into play. They ruin the meat, but if you need something dead, they do the job.\n\nPoisons can either be brewed or, if you are brave, gathered. You strike me as the latter.\n\nThe vipers by the pools to the south produce a powerful venom. If I have estimated you correctly, I think you could collect some of it.","Bring 4 samples of Glade Viper Venom to Neza Bloodsnout at Rog'mar.",4},
[96125]={"Now that the lion hides have been collected, and the orcish poachers culled, I can finally get a break.\n\nAt least, that's what I would say, if the man who was supposed to relieve me of my watch wasn't missing.\n\nDunston Willis, explorer extraordinaire, went to investigate the ogre settlement to the north a few days ago. He said he'd take over my post upon his return.\n\nFind him. If he's alive, bring him back here. If he's hanging up on meat hooks, bring me proof so Demar can send me someone else.","Find Dunston Willis somewhere among the ogres in Bolder'ok.",1},
[96135]={"Euck, just bein' around these blasted totems is givin' me the willies--but that's good. This much twisted corruption will be exactly what we need tae summon the quilboar's elementals.\n\nGo to the Thousand Needles and find a suitable spot for your defenses. The steam pools should work. They're rich with fire, earth, water, and air alike. Place these totems and be ready for a fight. The Razormane won't take too kindly to yer interference.","Use the Twisted Totems to put an end to the quilboar ritual.",5},
[96137]={"A small dagger belonging to the self-appointed ranger, Ira, who kept the forests safe by preventing the beasts within from attacking travelers.\n\nWith Ira's spirit still wandering the woods, perhaps her unfinished business was to clear out the worg that continue to claim victims throughout the forest.","Defeat $1oa Young Black Ravagers and $2oa Black Ravagers then return to Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire for more information.",5},
[96138]={"A bow left by the spirit of Merrick Valor, famed Watcher who prided himself on keeping the roads safe from encroaching enemies.\n\nWith Merrick's spirit still wandering the roads, perhaps his unfinished business was to clear out invaders near his home in Raven Hill. The ogres south of town may be what's troubling his spirit.","Defeat $1oa Splinter Fist Warriors and $2oa Splinter Fist Taskmasters then return to Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire for more information.",5},
[96139]={"In dark times like these, it's important we remember our heroes as much as our foes. Darkshire would not still be standing if it weren't for the bravery of folk like the good Lady Althea or those who lost their lives at Raven Hill.\n\nHave you read much on Raven Hill? No, of course not. Its history was wiped out along with its people. My library, impressive as it is, has little on the subject.\n\nIf you happen to find anything, I'd appreciate it if you brought it here. Those folk deserve to be remembered.","Search Raven Hill for anything of interest and return to Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire.",4},
[96204]={"Now that I'm free I'm going to make these vile creatures regret ever laying eyes on a Windshaper.\n\nLet's get out of here, $c.","Accompany Lumina Windsinger and help her escape Fenris Keep.",5},
[96209]={"The ancient, Orokai, stands vigil just outside of town. Take this to him. The ancients are wondrous and wise. Provided this branch has not been separated from its parent tree for too long, he will be able to \"speak\" with it to learn what tales it has to tell.\n\nYou can find Orokai to the southwest of the town, not too far away.","Seek out Orokai in Moonglade.",1},
[96246]={nil,nil,0},
[96260]={"Have you heard what befell the burial ground at Gloomrise? Giant spiders--rumored to have a venom so strong that it can wake the dead--have spread like wildfire. Nasty business, if you ask me.\n\nOne of the scouts dispatched to investigate returned half dead and covered in an incredibly resilient, crystalline spider silk. I harvested what I could, but I would highly value more samples of this silk for additional study.\n\nBring me more of this crystalline silk and I will reward you.","Gather $1oa strands of Crystalline Silk from Gloomrise Spinners.",4},
[96261]={"As is often the case with infestations such as the one we are facing at Gloomrise, a single powerful matriarch often leads to the rapid spread of a hostile spider population.\n\nIf we wish to drive these beasts off for good, we'll need to seek out the progenitor and end her. When you go to Gloomrise, seek out the broodmother there and destroy her. I'd advise you to bring allies, and be ready for anything. These seem to be no ordinary spiders.","Kill Broodmother Valraxx at Gloomrise.",6},
[96264]={"So yer a big shot shaman now, eh? Ye've mastered the elements and want tae put 'em to good use? I think I got just the thing.\n\nIf ye want the elements' respect, ye gotta repay yer debts to 'em. They help you, you help them. And right now they need all the help they can get from those who would abuse their power.\n\nEarth's rumblin', $n. It speaks of the quilboar amassin' for some ritual of terrible power. We need tae go investigate their kraul and see what they're up to. Bring me back whatever ye find.","Defeat Charlga Razorflank in Razorfen Kraul and collect information on the quilboar's plans.",6},
[96296]={"<The second you near the pulsing nodule it falls from the tree, exposing a weeping green sap. It seems the tree has corruption within its bark that has spread deep, but the tree is not yet dead.\n\nLooking around it is clear it has spread to some of the surrounding trees, but not all suffer from the same level of corruption.\n\nPerhaps it is not too late to save the infected trees nearby.\n\nSurely the Highfeathers would be grateful if you remove as many corrupted knots as you can find.>","Find and remove $1oa Corrupted Knots from the trees nearby.",4},
[96321]={"I... don't have much time, mortal. You must take this staff, a branch of the world tree... corrupted... wrong. I carried it here...\n\nThe Wild Gods... they must know. Take it to her. The... crow...\n\n<The dying Wild God grows still and his eyes stare blankly ahead. What little is left of his corporeal form seems to break apart and drift away. There is a faintly glowing branch on the ground, with a sickly green crystal affixed to its head.>","Find someone on Mount Hyjal who may be interested in the Faintly Glowing Staff.",1},
[96335]={"Wow! That was impressive. The way you took down that dragon was really something!\n\nWhile you are here... do you think you might be able to help me get out of this ball and chain?\n\nIf he hasn't fled or been killed already, the torturer they call 'The Questioner' should have the keys to these shackles. Get the key from that sadist and bring it to me.\n\nI promise that I'll make it well worth your while if you do.","Recover the Alcaz Shackle Key from The Questioner in Alcaz Prison.",2},
[96337]={"I told you that I'd make it worth your while to free me. I don't have any gold for you, but I have something better.\n\nTake this. It will help you find a treasure more valuable than gold. Do what you want with it, but if anyone asks you where you got it, tell them that the person who gave it to you died. \n\nTell them he was vaporized by dragonfire... blown out to sea.","Use the note provided by Mason Connery to find his hidden treasure.",5},
[96376]={nil,nil,6},
[96377]={nil,nil,6},
[96381]={"Was spyin' on the shore of Alcaz with my trusty lookin' glass whilst you were off eavesdroppin' on Lady Proudmoore. I think the island may be under attack. I saw naga--lots of them, chargin' onto shore. \n\nThe enemy of my enemy is certainly not my friend when it comes to naga, so let's do the world a favor and take some of them out. I also spied what looks to be the leader--a spellcaster type barkin' orders. Take her out as well, if you can.","Enter the Alcaz Prison and slay $1oa  Strashasz Soldiers, $2oa Strashaz Enchantresses, and bring the head of Tidemistress Ca'zass to Sully McCleary.",5},
[96390]={"Dark Iron spies have infiltrated Dun Morogh. To what end I canna' be sure, but this is a problem we need to nip in the bud before it is allowed to grow.\n\nHead eastward to Ironband's Compound and kill the Dark Iron spies that you find there.","Slay $1oa Dark Iron Spies in Dun Morogh.",5},
[96391]={"The map you are holding seems to show a complex series of underground tunnels and highways that all seem to converge on a point underneath Ironforge itself.\n\nYou can't be sure what the runes say as they are written in the ugly jagged rune language of the Dark Iron dwarves, but you can guess at the purpose of these tunnels. As you are reading the map, a gust of wind washes over you and you can faintly hear a dwarven voice carried on it. Earthseer Farsen needs to see this.","Deliver the Dark Iron Map to Earthseer Farsen in Dun Morogh.",5},
[96392]={"Greetings to ye, friend. My name is Earthseer Farsen and I'm visiting Dun Morogh from Aerie Peak. As I was travelin', I couldn't help but notice that we have, well... a bit o' a Dark Iron Dwarf problem.\n\nIf ye have a moment, I can show ye what I mean. I've got a bit o' magic that should do the trick.","Speak with Earthseer Farsen and ask him to lend you his far sight to observe the Dark Iron threat.",4},
[96393]={"Gather some allies and head down into the caverns beneath Old Ironforge. Enter the Hall of Thanes there and push to the lower vaults. \n\nMy Dark Iron is a bit rusty, but I can make out a name--one Durgen Dirgehammer. It's likely that he's the commander. Take his head and deliver it to King Magni Bronzebeard. \n\nOh, and when you do, tell him his old friend Farsen sends his regards!","Enter the Hall of Thanes beneath Old Ironforge and claim the Head of Durgen Dirgehammer.",6},
[96394]={"Something has disturbed the tombs down in the Hall of Thanes, and strange noises have been heard coming from deep within the vaults. The spirits of the dead are light sleepers, and whatever is going on down there seems to have startled them.\n\nHead down there and see what you can do about that for us. If any of the dead are awake--well, put them back down!","Kill $1oa Enraged Apparitions, $2oa Tormented Souls and put the spirit of Anvilmar to rest.",5},
[96395]={"The... Thane... my mighty... Thane... he... needs to... rest.\n\nPlease... help him... help him... rest...\n\nConsumed... by... ancient... grudge... No... rest...","Put the spirit of Faldrim Anvilmar to rest and then return to the Ghostly Attendant in the Hall of Thanes.",5},
[96403]={"You there, adventurer... I could really use your aid.\n\nI was sneaking--uh... 'patrolling' in the vaults when a force of Dark Iron dwarves emerged from the depths in mole machines! I don't know what they are here for, but there is priceless loot--uh or, rather... I mean, 'important cultural heirlooms' down there! Please, recover any such relics you see and return them here.\n\nI assure you that anything you recover will be catalogued and returned to its proper place of honor.","Collect $1oa Dwarven Heirlooms from the Hall of Thanes.",6},
[96408]={"Last night one of our mountaineers spotted a campfire on a hillside to the east. It looks to be pretty high up, overlooking the Gol'Bolar Quarry.\n\nIt's probably nothing, but I'd like you to go check on that camp. If they are friendly, no harm done. If they aren't friendly... well, you know what to do.","Investigate the campsite overlooking the Gol'Bolar Quarry.",4},
[96494]={"With the perimeter scouted, you've proven useful and trustworthy enough to bring into the fold.\n\nI'm here representing SI:7's efforts to gain crucial information important to the Alliance. Not just anyone is privy to this knowledge. Mind your discretion.\n\nA druidic cult known as the Blackthorne Pact has taken root nearby, operating in service to something they call the Wild King.\n\nFind the domain of this \"Wild King\" and mark it. Then we can report back to Stormwind with certainty.","Find the Blackthorne reinforcement point at the entrance to Hyjal Summit.",1},
[96550]={"The aged scabbard is embellished with carved designs and markings. This matches the description spoken by the war veteran. A dramatic view of the land below is a breathtaking sight.\n\nPerhaps simply holding the scabbard in your hand while remembering the veteran's words will beckon the spirit to this memory.","Use the Embroidered Scabbard to speak with the war veteran and hear his story at the overlook in Elderwild.",2},
[96559]={"Every Gnomish test pilot knows that one must be prepared for the worst-case scenario when taking to our great skies!\n\nThat's why we never leave the hangar without our pilot survival kits. They have a self-activating beacon attached that will radio our position home as soon as you open it. Not to mention being stuffed full of other useful supplies.\n\nIf you can find that pack wherever it fell, by all means open it immediately and help yourself to the contents. You'll still be doing me a favor!","Locate Fenwick Togglespring's Pilot Survival Kit.",3},
[96561]={"<You unfold the simple parchment.>\n\nTo my Rowdy Redridge Rebels,\n\nThe lumberjacks here say the gulpers in that pond are biting like they're racing each other to the bait. Good fish, better eating. After this war is over, we're due an angling competition between friends.\n\nThe setting is simple: we stand on the center island and fish till the sun slips behind Hyjal's highest peak.\n\nWhoever catches the most, doesn't have to gut 'em for our dinner!\n\n-- Tobin --","Find the fishing pond near the destroyed Alliance lumbermill in the Cradle of Tranquility.",3},
[96604]={"Lok-tar, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.","Sit near Brakk's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.",4},
[96605]={"Greetings, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.","Sit near Kaga's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.",4},
[96606]={"Greetings, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.","Sit near Lyreena's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.",4},
[96607]={"Greetings, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.","Sit near Eleanor's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.",4},
[96608]={"Greetings, $c. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.","Sit near Eric's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.",4},
[96609]={"Are you familiar with Silvermoon Shimmerwine? It has a delicate flavor that is entirely unique to the vineyards of Eversong and it is the one thing I truly miss from my homeland.\n\nUnfortunately, it is extremely hard to find on this side of the Thalassian Gate.\n\nI had a patron bring me a bottle that he claimed to have \"liberated\" from blood elves in northern Azshara. If your adventures take you to that region and you can recover more bottles for me, I would handsomely reward your efforts.","Bring $1oa bottles of Silvermoon Shimmerwine to Arille Azuregaze in Dalaran city.",5},
[96626]={"So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\n\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.","Speak with Tomas in Goldshire to learn to become a cook.",3},
[96627]={"$n, you have proven your competence as a protector thus far. That is why I am now entrusting you with an unusual task.\n\nI've heard of a new adventurer down the road by Goldshire. Go and see what he's doing.","Speak to Sam Sarsparilla near Goldshire.",4},
[96628]={"Wait, $n. I have another ask of you, before you brave that tunnel.\n\nMy mountaineers have reported an adventurer that's shown up just outside of Kharanos. Could you deliver these supplies to him?","Deliver the Supply Bundle to Eric Brighthammer near Kharanos.",4},
[96629]={"So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\n\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.","Speak with Gremlock Pilsnor in Kharanos to learn to become a cook.",3},
[96630]={"<The journal appears to be quite plain, detailing the life and adventures of someone you've never heard of.\n\nThere are multiple entries mentioning camping. It seems to be quite... fun.>","Bring the journal to Lyreena Duskblade near Dolanaar.",4},
[96634]={"So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\n\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.","Speak with Zarrin in Dolanaar to learn to become a cook.",3},
[96638]={"More and more adventurers like yourself have been seeking glory and fortune outside of the safety of Thendal Grove. There's one such adventurer who has made a camp outside of Shen'dar Village, along the road leading southwest out of Thendal Grove.\n\nSeek him out and see what you can learn from him that may help you in your own travels.","Speak to Raan Wildwind near Shen'dar Village.",4},
[96646]={"So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\n\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.","Speak with Zerril Softbreeze in Shen'dar Village to learn to become a cook.",3},
[96652]={"<The journal appears to be quite plain, detailing the life and adventures of someone you've never heard of.\n\nThere are multiple entries mentioning camping. It seems to be quite... fun.>","Bring the journal to Brakk near Razor Hill.",4},
[96655]={"So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\n\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.","Speak with Cook Torka in Razor Hill to learn to become a cook.",3},
[96656]={"$n, you have proven yourself trustworthy in your endeavors against the Scarlet Crusade so far. That is why I am now entrusting you with an unusual task.\n\nI've heard of a new adventurer down the road by Brill. Go and see what she's doing.","Speak to Eleanor Shackleton near Brill.",4},
[96658]={"So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\n\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.","Speak with William Pickman in Brill to learn to become a cook.",3},
[96659]={"Wait, $n. I have another ask of you, before you leave us.\n\nThere is an adventurer by the name of Kaga Wildhoof who has made camp just outside of Bloodhoof Village. She has greatly helped me in the past, and now I see my chance to repay her. Could you deliver these supplies to her?","Deliver the Supply Bundle to Kaga Wildhoof near Bloodhoof Village.",4},
[96661]={"So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $c. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\n\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.","Speak with Pyall Silentstride in Bloodhoof Village to learn to become a cook.",3},
[96676]={"Well, informant, you're being promoted.\n\nTake these updated orders to Johun at his base camp in Hyjal. There's some additional equipment in here that he'll be needing for our operations in the Summit.\n\nYour assistance in these matters is pivotal to our overall strategy in Kalimdor, $n. Tarry not.\n\nYou are dismissed.","Bring the Alliance Equipment to Johun \"Punchy\" Dillas in Hyjal.",6},
[96735]={nil,nil,0},
[96771]={"In the region known as the Riverglades to the southeast, there is a place called the Krol'dok Stronghold. A highborne known as Zalfan Moonshadow has been seen there in the company of the Twilight's Hammer.\n\nI'd pay handsomely if you'd rid the world of this cretin for me. He brings shame to the proud lineage of the highborne by consorting with fanatics and using stolen arcane knowledge in their service. There are few enough of us left without worms like him sullying our good name.","Travel to Krol'dok Stronghold and slay Zalfan Moonshadow.",6},
[96772]={"Timear and I have been scrying the area on Kalimdor known as Alcaz Island and we've all but confirmed the presence of a powerful magic user there. The mage in question was able to dispel our probes, but before she did, I was able to glean an image of a tome of some sort. I believe it was a journal, written in ancient draconic script.\n\nI don't know what is in that book, but I'd like to study it. We want you to travel to the hidden prison beneath Alcaz Island and recover that book for us.","Recover Zarla's Journal from the depths of Alcaz Prison.",6},
[96773]={"There is a servant of the Lich King that makes his home deep in the quilboar lair known as Razorfen Downs. It is known to us that he makes use of a scrying orb known as \"The Coldbringer's Eye\" to direct the movements of his lesser minions elsewhere.\n\nGo into Razorfen Downs and retrieve the Coldbringer's Eye on our behalf, $c. The Kirin Tor would pay handsomely to obtain this artifact so that we may study it and understand its inner workings.","Recover The Coldbringer's Eye from Razorfen Downs.",6},
[96775]={"Ol' Mazu'kon got a bone to pick with a Witch Doctor that go by the name of Zum'rah and I be thinkin' you can help me out with that. \n\nZum'rah practice all his bad voodoo in the Sandfury city of Zul'Farrak, far to the south in the deserts of Tanaris. Go there. Kill Zum'rah, and bring me his head.\n\nTrust me mon, the world be a better place with his head stuck on pike outside my hut than it be sittin' on his shoulders.","Slay Witch Doctor Zum'rah and bring Zum'rah's Head to Mazu'kon in Mulgore.",6},
[96779]={"Sometimes, $r, a single cut in the right place will drop a foe dead. The same is often true of organizations.\n\nOur agents have identified a key target among the ranks of the Syndicate: a man by the name of Lord Tomas.\n\nHe plays an instrumental role in the functions of Durnholde Keep, in Hillsbrad Foothills. If you wish to be of service to Ravenholdt, go to Durnholde and eliminate him. The quicker, and quieter, the better.","Find Lord Tomas inside Durnholde Keep, in Hillsbrad Foothills, and kill him. Then, return to Myrokos Silentform.",5},
[96781]={"We have noticed a Syndicate scouting party prowling around the ruins of Alterac, led by a man named Barton.\n\nThey're clearly searching for something, but I cannot know what without reading his scouting reports.\n\nI ask that you pickpocket the report from him, rather than killing him outright. Barton's death will tip off the Syndicate that we're on to them, and they will certainly take counter-measures to cover their tracks.\n\nIf you hope to find him, he is most likely among the Syndicate at Strahnbrad.","Steal Barton's Scouting Report by pickpocketing it from him. Then, bring the report to Myrokos Silentform at Ravenholdt Manor.",5},
[96782]={"It seems our friend Barton here has made this very easy for us. He is after two heirlooms of the Perenolde family within the ruins of Alterac. The Blade of House Perenolde, a sword, and the Royal Aegis of Perenolde, a shield.\n\nFrom the report, it seems these armaments are within two towers among the ruins. Best we acquire them before the Syndicate does.\n\nThe ogres occupying the ruins are fierce, but I trust you should be able to sneak past them without needing to bloody your blade at all.","Find the Blade of House Perenolde and the Royal Aegis of Perenolde among the ruins of Alterac. Then, bring them to Myrokos Silentform.",5},
[96783]={"Stromgarde Keep is one of the Syndicate's largest strongholds. Many of the organization's most important dealings take place behind its walls.\n\nI have received word of a certain trade taking place between members of the Syndicate somewhere in Arathi Highlands, and I'm certain the details of this trade can be found somewhere in Stromgarde.\n\nTo infiltrate the keep without arousing suspicion, you'll need a disguise. See if you can find one among the Syndicate outside the keep, at Northfold Manor.","Steal a Syndicate uniform from Northfold Manor to infiltrate Stromgarde Keep.",5},
[96786]={"Falconcrest sent some guys to do a handoff at the southern part of Thoradin's wall. I don't know what they're picking up. Must be good, because everyone involved has kept it a total secret. I don't think the guys picking it up even know what it is.\n\nThat's all I've got. Don't make me regret telling you that.","Break up the secret deal, and take the object being traded to the Syndicate. Then, return to Myrokos Silentform at Ravenholdt Manor.",6},
[96799]={"<Lieutenant Connar listens as you tell him the reason you are here.>\n\nSo, Danneth has an orphaned nephew in Dalaran? If you haven't spoken to him about this yet, I'd suggest you do so. He doesn't exactly seem like the parenting type, but he might surprise me.\n\nIf he does want to go and collect the boy once he's recovered, he has my blessing to take leave for that.","Speak with Sergeant Danneth at Nethergarde Keep.",3},
[96800]={"You there, $c. I have a matter I could use assistance with.\n\nI just so happen to be writing a thesis on the ancient Wildhammer runemasters of Grim Batol, and there's a particular tome I need to complete my research. According to our ledgers, a mage by the name of Doan checked the book out of the old Dalaran library before the Third War and never returned it!\n\nArcanist Doan is now holed up in the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades. Retrieve this book for me and you'll be well rewarded.","Retrieve the book The Lost Magic of the Runemasters from the Scarlet Monastery.",5},
[96821]={"We see fewer and fewer travelers from Razor Hill these days. The scorpids were never much fun, but now I hear there are spiders making their nest along the road.\n\nIf your travels take you up north, kill some of the spiders on your way. Then, let Razor Hill know the path's a bit safer for them.","Kill 6 Ridgeshade Creepers and 6 Ridgeshade Lurkers in southern Durotar, then report to Gar'thok in Razor Hill.",5},
[96822]={"We lost many brave warriors of the Horde when we sacked Tiragarde Keep. Now that the humans have reinforced the ruins, we cannot collect their remains to properly honor their deaths.\n\nGo to the ruins surrounding the keep, and search for the weapons left by our fallen kin. We will display them in a place of honor.","Collect the Raider's Battleaxe, Raider's Bow, and Raider's Shield from the Tiragarde Keep outskirts, then return them to Turroc in Razor Hill.",4},
[96833]={"Gh... Ghan. Sur... Okk... Ghansurok. That's the fel chimaera's name. I thought I could manage out here... ugh... alone. No chance. Picked me clean into the air.\n\nStuck my dagger through its closest eye I could find, and I fell farther than the tree tops.\n\nI wasn't the only one who bit off more than I could chew this time. Haha--agh... I shouldn't make myself laugh, this hurts bad enough.\n\nBroken bones we could mend, but... the venom... is too vile.\n\nPass on a warning. I beg you!","Pass on the warning of the aggressive chimaera known as Ghansurok to others on the mountain.",1},
[96873]={"The trolls east of here have lost their will to the witchdoctor, Zalazane. He uses many cruel magics to keep hold of his prisoners' minds, but one of his favorite tricks is to make them wear pendants wrapped in evil binding spells.\n\nPractice your enchanting skills by stripping the magic from these pendants, and bring me the results. And don't accidentally put one around your neck, if you value your freedom!","Pa'zula in Sen'jin Village wants you to collect 3 Luminous Residue. Luminous Residue can be obtained by disenchanting Hexed Pendants dropped by trolls in the Echo Isles.",4},
[96875]={"Orgrimmar is always expanding, $c. And when the peons need hides to line the walls and roofs of our new buildings, they come to me!\n\nThe hides of the lizards in Thunder Ridge are typically too thick for armor, but they make excellent building material. Bring me some of their hides, along with a few lighter cured hides. Let's see your skill with leather!","Kamari in Orgrimmar wants you to collect 5 Rough Lizard Hide from beasts in Thunder Ridge, along with 2 Cured Light Hides.",5},
[96877]={"The enormous hoof serves as proof of your victory over the mighty lizard.","Deliver Halikor's Hoof to Orgrimmar.",6},
[96895]={"Not sure if you heard, but two emissaries of the Argent Dawn just passed through here. I don't mind the Argent Dawn, but I don't like them poking around Tirisfal unsupervised either. They were both Forsaken... but that doesn't make me any less nervous.\n\nOne of them just passed by here, headed southeast. There's a group of scourge cultists snooping around the outskirts of the city in that direction. If those two heard about them, there's no doubt that would have caught their attention.","Find the Argent Dawn member near the entrance to the Undercity.",3},
[96896]={"Danitha and I fought against the Scourge in the defense of the Undercity when Naxxramas attacked. We lost many good friends that day, including the hero after which this keep was named--Garek Bandarion.\n\nHe might just have been the first Forsaken to rediscover how to wield the Light as a paladin. I am encouraged to see his legacy and potential live on here with Danitha and her cohort.\n\nIf only the rest of the Forsaken felt the same way...","Observe the conversation between Danitha Morr and Leonid Barthalomew the Revered.",1},
[96897]={"The Scourge are a blight on our lands, and their living servants are the worst of them. The people of Tirisfal have enough to deal with between the mindless dead and the Scarlet Crusade. If you wish to do some good, help me put an end to this scum.","Kill $1oa Dark Neophytes and $2oa Dark Enforcers in Tirisfal Glades.",5},
[96898]={"It wasn't long ago that the citadel of Naxxramas bore down upon this city, intent on wiping the Forsaken off the map. Both the Forsaken and the Argent Dawn lost much that day to secure the future of the Forsaken.\n\nDuring the battle, the great necrotic focusing crystal mounted atop Naxxramas was shattered and its fragments were scattered all over this area. I suspect that is what the cultists are here for. Help me recover the fragments and deprive the Scourge of them.","Gather $1oa Necrotic Crystal Fragments in Tirisfal Glades.",5},
[96899]={"You've done a great thing for the cause of the Argent Dawn here today, and I thank you. I don't know how familiar you are with the fortress of Bandarion Keep, but my commander and I were headed that way to meet with the paladins that reside there. That was before we learned of the presence of the Cult of the Damned.\n\nIf you'd like to learn more about the Argent Dawn and our mission, seek out my commander at Bandarion Keep, to the northwest of here. I'll remain here to mop up the rest of this mess.","Meet Leonid Barthalomew at Bandarion Keep in Tirisfal Glades.",3},
[96912]={"Heya pal, step right up! You look like you know which end of the sword goes where! \n\nIt just so happens that I have a long list of challenges that only the most elite fighters will be able to accomplish. Wanna take a stab at it?","Win 10 duels.",0},
[96913]={"You again, eh? Ready for the next test? I hope you aren't squeamish. You might need to bleed for this one... or preferably make the other guys bleed first.","Complete 3 Warsong Gulch battles.",0},
[96959]={"War.\n\nBy the time I heeded the call of our clans, the battle had passed, and only ashes answered my blade.\n\nMy purpose is forged anew.\n\nThis mountain remembers strength--ancient power riding its winds and holding its water. I would earn the right to walk its spine, to reach the fallen stronghold that lies upon the road to the summit.\n\nDemons profane these graves. Before I fight at your side, I must know you stand capable. Light the two bonfires and return to me. Their flames draw our enemy out.","Light the two bonfires in Dae'gun and return to Yashiro.",3},
[96964]={"If the hermit truly wants his little gambit to leave the nest and fly, it will likely need a potent energy source. One that can sustain itself without collapse.\n\n<Jereman looks to the sky and clacks her beak together as she considers.>\n\nAh, yes. I know just the clever creature we can consult. Go north into the area you mortals refer to as Dae'gun, the one with the demons, and seek out the fox Wild God Renalard. I believe he will have a solution to our little puzzle.","Speak to the Wild God Renalard.",1},
[96971]={"Say, while you're out and about prancing in my lands, would you mind doing me a favor?\n\nOnce the war had been won, many of the various armies up and left. For whatever reason, they decided some of their supplies were not worth taking. That, or they all died. Who could say?\n\nRegardless, these supplies are of use to my kits and me. Unfortunately they also tend to be where the demons are. Take this tuft of fur with you and use it on the demons to distract them while you grab the tools.","Collect $1oa Abandoned Supplies.",4},
[96983]={"You're capable, fast, fearless. Fire will draw the demons from their hiding places, and with them, their warlords. They will come seeking dominance. Instead, they will find vengeance waiting. This is the moment where the will of the mountain speaks through us.\n\nCome, let us carve a path through these hellspawn and end their reign. My blade yearns to cleave through their ranks.","Fight your way through Dae'gun with Yashiro.",6},
[96984]={"You may not have our best interests at heart, but I won't deny an extra pair of hands. And if Dalaran falls, it takes everything with it--including your Undercity.\n\nSo, your benefactor wants in? Fine. I'll imbue your key to work past my wards so you can enter the city. Once you're in, meet me at the Violet Citadel where this all began. With everything going on the Kirin Tor will be too busy to stop you.\n\nScavenge what you will, but whatever happens, our first priority is to prevent a catastrophe.","Collect the Arcane Mote in the City of Dalaran for Magus Wordeen Voidglare in Tarren Mill.",7},
[96986]={"Within the underbelly of the mage city to the north is a traitor to our kind. A necromancer of disturbing talent. He raises an army of undeath right under the Kirin Tor's nose.\n\nI care not for the fate of the mage city, $n, but this grave knight spits in the face of everything we Forsaken stand for. Put an end to him. Show him no one is beyond the reach of the Dark Lady.","Defeat Atrexis the Grave Knight in the City of Dalaran for Melisara in Tarren Mill.",7},
[96988]={"With the city of Dalaran under siege by their own constructs, this is the perfect opportunity to, let's say, borrow a few samples.\n\nImagine an army of arcane-powered abominations. The Dark Lady would have no choice but to recognize my alchemical prowess. Maybe even grant me head of the Royal Apothecary Society?\n\nGo to the city and find the constructs' cores. They are unlikely to give them willingly, so do what you must.","Collect $1oa Cracked Sentry Cores in the City of Dalaran for Doctor Martin Felben in Undercity.",7},
[96989]={"Ey mon! Today be a big day for ya, I see. Ya think you're ready to take de reins of one of these fierce creatures, huh?\n\nMost be underestimatin' how intelligent and savage these beasts be. Ya won't be findin' a better, faster or more lethal companion once ya be bonded with it.\n\nSo, you be havin' an important choice to make. Ya raptor and you will be traversin' the world together, and the raptor will also be needin' to choose ya in return.\n\nGo an' take a look and return to me when ya made ya choice.","Inspect the riding raptors to choose your first mount.",0},
[96991]={"The climb grows steeper from here, as you say. Even an empty pack weighs on tired legs. I would ask another kindness of you, traveler. Take my excess gear and carry it ahead to the Summit, where Marn Euhron aids in restoring a foothold near Nordrassil.\n\nI will follow at my own pace when my ceremonies here are complete. When I arrive, I will reclaim them from him and assist him in their work. This way, we both honor the journey and gifts of the mountain.","Deliver Galvinquam's Belongings to Marn Euhron in the Summit.",4},
[96992]={"You know, they packed enough tools to get the essentials started, but there's never enough fastening material. Only so much cordage-winding my hands can take.\n\nResourcefulness is even better than being prepared.\n\nTake an empty bag to the burned-down remains of the alliance buildings around the Cradle of Tranquility southwest of here, and fill it with as many nails and brackets as you can find in the ashes.","Look through the burned buildings in the Cradle of Tranquility for $2oa Metal Brackets and $1oa Nails and return to Johun \"Punchy\" Dillas in Hyjal.",3},
[96994]={"Lok'tar, $c. Come to bond with your first wolf? Good.\n\nThere is no stronger bond than that of an orc and their wolf. They are no mere mount, but are a lifelong companion and friend.\n\nOurs is not a bond chosen by vanity. No, each orc and wolf forms a special bond that goes beyond a mere purchase.\n\nThey will choose you as much as you will choose them. You will understand when you meet them.\n\nGo and find which wolf speaks to you. Return to me when you have your answer.","Inspect the riding wolves to choose your first mount.",0},
[96996]={"Now that you have completed your training, it would seem the winds wish you to bond with your first strider.\n\nThese galestriders have been ridden by our ancestors for generations. Despite their wispy and slender appearance, they are steadfast and fierce mounts.\n\nYou and your strider will traverse the world together, so you have an important choice to make. Fear not, whatever choice you make will be the right one.\n\nGo examine the striders and return to me when you have made your choice.","Inspect the riding striders to choose your first mount.",5},
[96997]={"Greetings, $c. I imagine I can guess what has brought you to my stables today.\n\nIf you are looking for a mount, you have come to the right place. Be warned though, riding an undead steed is not for the faint of heart.\n\nAs such, you have an important choice to make. You and your undead steed will travel the world together for good or ill. Fear not, whatever choice you make will be the correct one.\n\nGo examine the undead horses and return to me when you have made your choice.","Inspect the undead riding horses to choose your first mount.",0},
[96999]={"Whoever wore dis fought wit' purpose. An' Sen'jin be a small village... blood an' kin run close dere.\n\nSomebody back home be missin' dis wrap--and da warrior who carried it.\n\nWhen ya trek to Echo Isles, take dis wrap wit' ya. Bring it home to Sen'jin. Dey'll know who it belong to--and dey'll honor ya for seein' it returned.","Take the War Paint Wrap to someone in Sen'jin Village.",5},
[97003]={"You there, $c. I need your aid. There are rumors of a beast that makes its lair deep in a cave at Thorn Hill, northeast of here. The Razormane call it Chol'aruk or \"The Ravener\". It's supposedly five times the size of a normal quilboar with a thirst for blood that can never be sated.\n\nMost don't believe the tales. But I do--because I've fought its like before.\n\nSeek out its lair and slay Chol'aruk. Bring me its head. I warn you though--prepare well and do not go alone.\n\nBlood and thunder, $c.","Bring the head of Chol'aruk to Gur'ak in the Barrens.",6},
[97005]={"There are rumors of a colossal abomination that makes its lair at a cave to the northwest of here, on the plateau known as Thorn Hill. The Razormane call it Chol'aruk or \"The Ravener\" and those that have seen it say it's so massive that it can swallow an orc whole.\n\nFew believe such tales, but I do... because I've fought one like it myself. On the honor of those I lost to these things, this beast must die.\n\nGather strong allies and find the lair of Chol'aruk. Kill the abomination and bring me its head.","Bring Chol'aruk's Head to Bainham in the Barrens.",6},
[97017]={"Ah, it's a big day fer ya I see; here for yer first ram are ye?\n\nThese rams are the most steadfast and sturdy in all of Azeroth. They're fiercely protective of their rider. Aye, you'll have a hard time finding a more stalwart companion for yer journeys.\n\nSo, you have an important choice to make. You and yer ram will traverse the world together so choose wisely! Not to worry lad, whatever choice you make will be the right one.\n\nGo see the rams and return to me when you've made yer choice.","Inspect the riding rams to choose your first mount.",3},
[97022]={"Danitha Morr has ordered you to report back to Bandarion Keep to receive additional training. Please make your way back to the keep as quickly as you are able.","Speak with Danitha Morr at Bandarion Keep.",2},
[97045]={"Greetings! Are you here to examine our horses?\n\nThese steeds are descendants from both the historical Lordaeron stock and our own local horses. You won't find a more steadfast companion for your journeys.\n\nChoosing one may be difficult as they are all excellent and trained to be steady even when in danger. Don't forget, you and your horse will traverse the world together. I'm sure whatever choice you make will suit you best.\n\nGo examine the horses and return to me when you have made your choice.","Inspect the riding horses to choose your first mount.",0},
[97048]={"Listen, I can't repay you right now, but I'm a cook on Captain Aransas' ship. I'll be sure to put in a good word for you when I get back to Booty Bay. You should speak to the captain when you get the chance. I'm sure she'll be grateful to have me back.","Speak to Captain Aransas in Booty Bay.",5},
[97074]={"Hello, $c! It would seem you are now seasoned enough as an adventurer for me to teach you how to ride a saber, for a fee of course.\n\nLelanai will provide you with a free mount once ye have trained with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts ye would like. There are many creatures out in the world, and each requires their own riding skill, but you will have to find trainers for each.\n\nSpeak to me when you have enough coin, and I will teach you all I know about riding sabers.","Learn the Apprentice Riding skill from Jartsam.",0},
[97119]={"In addition to seeing to the spiritual needs of the people here, I feed them as well. I'm not exactly a trained cook, but after five years, I've learned a thing or two about preparing food!\n\nI'm sure that folks here would love a taste of something different. I remember, before we assembled on the mountain, there was a goblin from Everlook who was serving platters of tiny, Savory Stag Sliders... I would love to taste one of those again. We have plenty of stags up here, too! Think you can cook some up?","Bring $1oa Savory Stag Sliders to Ortak Lomgok in Elderwild.",3},
[97130]={"Lan'dalock and I have been discussing a recent development in the south seas involving an ancient Gurubashi ruin that has suddenly appeared off the coast of Stranglethorn Vale.\n\nSuch a site has significant archeological value. We'd be highly interested in obtaining one of the idols that certain witch doctors amongst the ancient Gurubashi would use as a ritual focus for their blood magic.\n\nEnter this \"Drowned City\" and recover one of these idols for us.","Recover an Ancient Gurubashi Idol from the Drowned City.",6},
[97170]={"Hello, $c! It would seem you are now seasoned enough as an adventurer for me to teach you how to ride a horse, for a fee of course.\n\nKatie will provide you with a free mount once ye have trained with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you would like. There are many creatures out in the world, and each requires their own riding skill, but you will have to find trainers for each.\n\nSpeak to me when you have enough coin, and I will teach you all I know about riding horses.","Learn the Apprentice Riding skill from Randal Hunter.",0},
[97171]={"Greetings! Are you here to examine our horses?\n\nThese steeds are descendants from both the historical Lordaeron stock and our own local horses. You won't find a more steadfast companion for your journeys.\n\nChoosing one may be difficult as they are all excellent and trained to be steady even when in danger. Don't forget, you and your horse will traverse the world together. I'm sure whatever choice you make will suit you best.\n\nGo examine the horses and return to me when you have made your choice.","Inspect the riding horses to choose your first mount.",3},
[97173]={"The Blackmaw furbolgs in the mountains overlooking Azshara have been dabbling in dark magic. While a primitive people being corrupted by demonic magic is nothing new for Azeroth, Lan'dalock and I would like to study their spell foci.\n\nTravel to the stronghold known as Blackmaw Hold and recover one of the Blackmaw Ritual Totems for us. Only the most powerful of the Blackmaw's shamans will be carrying one of these, so bring allies and take care.","Recover a Blackmaw Ritual Totem from Blackmaw Hold.",5},
[97175]={"No worthy endeavor is completed without some sacrifice, and this first task requires just that.\n\nYou must acquire High Priest Zayus's exorcism censer for your task. Even though its use will be for good reason, due compensation must be given for it.\n\nProceed to Orgrimmar and speak with the High Priest Zayus there. Zayus will seek a...\"donation\" for the loss of his censer. It will be a small price to pay when all is said and done.","Travel to Orgrimmar and get High Priest Zayus's Exorcism Censer. You will need to make a donation of 150 gold in order to secure it.",1},
[97176]={"I have added some dirt from the tainted ground of Terrordale in the Eastern Plaguelands to the censer. Go there and use this censer to find areas with the greatest signs of corruption. You'll know these areas by the green necrotic auras that rise up from the ground at the location where tormented souls congregate.\n\nUse the censer to reveal these spirits. Free them from their torment. When you have put these souls to rest, return and we will discuss the next steps.","Use the Exorcism Censer to drive out the tormented spirits in Terrordale. When you have destroyed 25 Terrordale Spirits, return to Danitha Morr at Bandarion Keep in Tirisfal Glades.",5},
[97177]={"With the blessings of the loa, take the censer. I be usin' it more than once to exorcise bad voodoo spirits, and it should serve ya well for the trials what be comin'.\n\nYou best be headin' back to Danitha now, $n. Ya quest continues with her.","Return the Exorcism Censer to Danitha Morr at Bandarion Keep in Tirisfal Glades.",1},
[97178]={"A paladin's charger needs a proper barding or it is little more than a mindless beast. The barding used by your charger not only needs to be of the finest materials possible, but must also be suitable for attunement to the spirit realm.\n\nThere is a smith outside of Tarren Mill that has done great work for our paladins in the past. He is a modest and unassuming orc, but his work is superb and is well-suited to our needs. Seek him out and commission him for this task.","Speak with Ott at the village of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",1},
[97185]={"In this satchel you will find the items you will need for your trial. Use the divination scryer in the heart of the Great Ossuary's basement to bring forth accursed spirits to face justice. The power of your judgements will be extremely valuable in this battle, so use them wisely.\n\nOnce you have dispersed these spirits, Darkreaver will appear. Defeat him and claim the lost soul of the charger. Show it the path of justice and retribution that you walk and with luck, it will take its place at your side.","Use the Divination Scryer in the heart of the Great Ossuary's basement in the Scholomance.  Doing so will bring forth the spirits you must judge. Defeating these spirits will summon forth Death Knight Darkreaver.  Defeat him and reclaim the lost soul of the fallen charger.\n\nGive the Spirit of Retribution and the Blessed Enchanted Barding to Darkreaver's Fallen Charger.",7},
[97188]={"Greetings, $c! You are now seasoned enough as an adventurer for me to teach you how to pilot a mechanostrider, for a fee of course.\n\nMilli will provide you with a free mount once you have trained with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you would like. There are many creatures out in the world, and each requires their own riding skill, but you will have to find trainers for each.\n\nSpeak to me when you have enough gold, and I will teach you about riding mechanostriders!","Learn the Apprentice Riding skill from Binjy Featherwhistle.",0},
[97196]={"There is a servant of the Lich King that makes his home deep in the Death's Head quilboar lair known as Razorfen Downs. It is known to us that he makes use of a scrying orb to observe and direct the movements of his minions elsewhere.\n\nWith this artifact, we'd be able to hunt down the covert agents of the Scourge and put an end to them and the threat they pose to Kalimdor forever.\n\nGo into Razorfen Downs to the lair of Amnennar the Coldbringer and retrieve the orb known as the Coldbringer's Eye for me.","Recover The Coldbringer's Eye from Razorfen Downs.",6},
[97198]={"The Blackmaw furbolgs in the mountains overlooking Azshara have been corrupted by dark and sinister magic. We do not know the full extent of the corruption and what impact it may have upon the elements in the area, but we hope to understand it better.\n\nTravel to the stronghold known as Blackmaw Hold and recover one of the Blackmaw Ritual Totems for us. Only the most powerful of the Blackmaw's shamans will be carrying one of these, so bring allies and prepare for a difficult battle.","Recover a Blackmaw Ritual Totem from Blackmaw Hold.",6},
[97200]={"Ey, welcome $c! Ya now be seasoned enough as an adventurer for me to teach you how to ride one of our raptors, for a fee of course.\n\nZjolnir will provide ya with a free mount once you have trained with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts ya would like. There are many creatures out in the world, and each requires their own riding skill, but ya will have to find trainers for each.\n\nSpeak to me when ya have enough gold, and I will teach ya about raptor riding.","Learn the Apprentice Riding skill from Xar'ti.",0},
[97203]={"Greetings, $c. It would seem you are now seasoned enough as an adventurer for me to teach you how to ride a skeletal steed, for a fee.\n\nZachariah will provide you with a free mount once you have trained with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you desire. There are many creatures out in the world, and each requires their own riding skill, but you will have to find trainers for each.\n\nSpeak to me when you have enough coin, and I will teach you about skeletal horses.","Learn the Apprentice Riding skill from Velma Warnam.",0},
[97204]={"Greetings, $c. It would seem you are now seasoned enough as an adventurer for me to teach you how to ride a kodo, for a fee of course.\n\nHarb will provide you with a free mount once ye have trained with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you would like. There are many creatures out in the world, and each requires their own riding skill, but you will have to find trainers for each.\n\nSpeak to me when you have enough coin, and I will teach you about riding the noble kodo.","Learn the Apprentice Riding skill from Kar Stormsinger.",0},
[97205]={"Hello, $c! It would seem you are now seasoned enough as an adventurer for me to teach you how to ride a galestrider, for a fee of course.\n\nI will provide you with a free mount once ye have trained with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you would like. There are many creatures out in the world, and each requires their own riding skill, but you will have to find trainers for each.\n\nSpeak to me when you have enough coin, and I will teach you about riding galestriders.","Learn the Apprentice Riding skill from Genn Fairweather.",0},
[97225]={"When we fled the isles that Zalazane and his ilk now inhabit, we left behind many precious idols that help us commune with spirits we worship: our loa. They are of grave importance to our tribe.\n\nThe followers of Zalazane show no reverence for our loa and have scattered these idols across the largest of the isles.\n\nThis is an action that will not go unnoticed if we are not able to collect these idols, and offending a loa is a grave matter.\n\nGo, find as many loa idols as you can and return them to me.","Collect $1oa Forgotten Loa Idols from the Echo Isles. Bring them to Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village.",5},
[97236]={"A fresh specimen from a beast of this size is quite a find. Perhaps someone in Aldrassil familiar with the study of spiders would be interested in the fang.","Deliver the Fang of Githyiss to someone interested in the study of spiders in Aldrassil.",5},
[97242]={"Yelmak doesn't want his apprentice breaking anything. Well, anything more than he already has.\n\nHe told me the young mixer in training has too much pride to ask for help when he really needs it. Yelmak wants to give him a taste of a particular home-brewed recipe.\n\nGather a mix of cattail and speargrass cuttings taken from the plants growing around the water in the Valley of Honor. I'd get them myself, but if I left the shop, Whuut would surely know we're catering to his mood.","Take some cuttings from the Cattails and Speargrass growing around the water flows in the Valley of Honor and return to Kor'geld in Yelmak's Alchemy and Potions.",1},
[97243]={"Even though we are in the realm of Skywall, this is still the elemental plane. The spirits of all four elements speak to us, if we deign to listen. One among us Windshapers is in particular attunement with the element of fire. A shen'dorei by the name of Olariaan Swiftburn.\n\nBring this to him at the Shrine of Flames in the Gustberry Lowlands. You'll find it tucked away along the edge of the island, west of Valanaar.","Bring the Torch of Dormant Flame to Olariaan Swiftburn at the Shrine of Flames in the Gustberry Lowlands.",3},
[97244]={"There is an Al'Aketh Skypriest called Faladiel. He was once a caller of the flame and a stalwart Windshaper. Like so many Al'Aketh, he mortgaged his loyalty for power and his hands are now stained with the blood of his former brothers and sisters.\n\nYou will find Skypriest Faladiel at the farm to the northeast past Valanaar, just to the south of the Shrine of Akir. Kill the betrayer. Bring me his heart. It is a gruesome task, but it is needed for the ritual we are to perform.","Slay Skypriest Faladiel in the Gustberry Lowlands and collect Faladiel's Heart.",5},
[97245]={"The residents of the Shen'dar Highlands speak of an ancient forest sprite called Kuramaa. They say it lives inside of a twisted stump at the summit of a hill near the highlands Anchor Pylon.\n\nGo to the highlands and find this stump. Rap your fist upon the bark and Kuramaa will appear. Best the spirit in combat, and bring me its wooden mask.\n\nBe warned however, this entity will be exceptionally resistant to much of your magic. Only the touch of flame will lay low the spirit.","Find the home of Kuramaa in the Shen'dar Highlands, and defeat the spirit in combat. Bring Kuramaa's Mask to Olariaan Swiftburn in the Gustberry Lowlands when you are victorious.",5},
[97246]={"My son, Migi, always takes off to play with his friends all day. I tell him to pick up a lunch at Borstan's, but I know he almost never does, because he comes home starving. These kids think their games are more important than their own bodies!\n\nPlease, stop at Borstan's Firepit and tell him you're there to deliver Migi's lunch. You can almost certainly find Migi behind Grommash Hold with the rest of his friends.\n\nDuties keep me here during the day and I can't watch over his every meal.","Visit Borstan's Firepit and tell him Thatog wants you to deliver Migi's lunch to him personally.",1},
[97249]={"Now that I know his parents worry about how much he's actually filling that belly, I've got an idea. \n\nThey made me promise not to pack the same meal every day, so Migi grows a taste for more than one thing. Still, whenever the smoker's full and we're making sweetglazed hog belly sandwiches, he always shows up for lunch. We've started crumbling the leftover crispy glazed bits as a topping--something we can add daily. \n\nTake this to him. Maybe he'll start showing up early and bringing friends!","Bring Migi's Lunch to him behind Grommash Hold.",1},
[97250]={"Traveler, have you plans to head toward Dustwallow Marsh? I have heard mutterings that a few human soldiers have taken a stand at its border and are toppling the landmarks left behind by our tauren pathfinders.\n\nRumor has it that a favored tavern has burned to the ground, and in typical Alliance fashion, they immediately cast their blame onto the Horde! I cannot know whether there is any truth to their claim, but their incursion onto OUR land must not stand.\n\nKill first, investigate later!","Slay Alliance soldiers encroaching into the Barrens at the border to Dustwallow Marsh, then return to Grunt Logmar at Camp Taurajo.",6},
[97270]={"There must be more to the Maul than this!$B$BPerhaps the loud Spectator who oversees the event at Dire Maul will know!","Speak with Griniblix the Spectator above the Maul in Dire Maul.",1},
[97275]={"Whuut is a prodigy. That much is true. But he doesn't yet have the experience, wisdom, and time on the stirring rod to know how to respect alchemical processes.\n\nHe is exhausting all of the rarest and most exotic reagents we have available without pausing to practice and refine his basic skills.\n\nGive him this potion I've brewed with a quick tonic method. He'll reconsider everything he's doing when he learns how local remedies and careful touch are the first true mastery.","Give Yelmak's Potion to Whuut.",4},
[97277]={"Oi, had me back turned gettin' the boar roast ready when I heard me pal Gozwin screamin' fer his life!\n\nWicked fangs and a blur are all I saw when I turned. Such huge paws! A snow leopard was draggin' its gnomish catch away. I grabbed me shotgun and fired above the beast. It dropped him and sprinted off.\n\nLuckily, it hadn't done more than give ol' Goz some deep scratches.\n\nHead back to camp in the northwestern hills and retrieve Gozwin's Mechanic's Log. Kill that snow leopard too if you see it!","Find Grund and Gozwin's camp in the hills to the northwest. Recover Gozwin's Mechanic's Log and kill the Snow Leopard Prowler.",4},
[97279]={"With an influx of new recruits like yourself, it's been hard to keep our weapons supplied. Our weaponsmith, Kzan, is running low on training weapons and I'd like to see what kinds of skills you possess to get an idea of what I have to work with. Luckily for you, I have a solution to both.\n\nWhile you're out there cutting your teeth on boars, salvage six abandoned training weapons. Our failed recruits left them laying on the ground. Once you do, return them to our weaponsmith Kzan behind me in the Den.","Collect $1oa Abandoned Training Weapons, then return to Kzan Thornslash in the Den.",5},
[97281]={"<Before you is a strange orb with a dull surface. When picked up a small electrical current seems to vibrate from within. Upon closer inspection, it looks as if a dark mist swirls within and every so often a small electrical spark can be seen.\n\nIt is clear the harpy was using it for some purpose. Perhaps Rezlak would be interested in this object?>","Bring the Dull Stormy Orb to Rezlak near Drygulch Ravine.",5},
[97287]={"You have done well to infiltrate the city of mages, but I believe it is time for us to be more... negotiatory.\n\nAs much as it pains me to admit, there is no other place on Azeroth with such a vast knowledge of the arcane. My brilliant work still pales in comparison to the ancient wisdom the Kirin Tor have amassed over the years. I think it's high time we are granted access to this exclusive order, don't you think?\n\nTake the mote you acquired. They will surely give anything to get it back. Anything.","Speak with the Image of Archmage Modera near Dalaran.",1},
[97288]={"<As the creature falls, its head comes toppling off. It seems as if it has been reattached several times, and the connection gets weaker with each reconnection.\n\nSomeone in the Undercity would know more about this unique abomination.>","Deliver the Abominable Head to Master Apothecary Faranell within the Undercity.",5},
[97289]={"We craft abomination heads all the time, but this one is special. It belonged to a Grand Marshal of the Alliance once. A particularly unpleasant one. Othmar, I believe its name was. The Dark Lady had the pleasure of dispatching this one herself.\n\nOoh the secrets it could tell if it could talk. And it can! If we reattach it to an appropriate host.\n\nGo ahead and place it next to the available body in the next room. But don't attach it. Not yet.","Bring the Head of the Baron to the body of Othmar in the Undercity.",5},
[97290]={"You... abomination...\n\nWhy should... help you...\n\nBe gone...","Report your findings to Master Apothecary Faranell in Undercity.",5},
[97291]={"With the head reattached, all we need now is to bind it to the Dark Lady's will. This should not be a problem. The beast barely has brains left as it is after all the beatings it's taken.\n\nWe simply need to motivate it.\n\nFetch me a Toxic Skullcap from Miss Grisette in the Trade Quarter. Oh, and some Blisterweed from our local herbalist trainers, the Alliestars. Feel free to just take some, they owe me. And lastly a bit of Essence of Agony. Any old poison vendor should do.\n\nWe have a potion to make!","Collect a Toxic Skullcap from Tawny Grisette in the Trade Quarter, Blisterweed near the Herbalism Trainer, and Essence of Agony from the poison vendor in the Rogues' Quarter for Master Apothecary Faranell in Undercity.",5},
[97292]={"I have concocted a lovely serum that our new guest is sure to find quite... stimulating.\n\nTake this. Feed it into the workings dripping from above him. Let's see if we can't show him why it's in his best interest to serve loyally.\n\nAnd try not to drop it. I can't afford a new assistant.","Inject the Hissing Serum into the system above Othmar's body for Master Apothecary Faranell.",5},
[97326]={"Hey! You've got time to help us out! I know you do, I can tell by the way you smiled watching the game we're playing.\n\nThis spot behind Grommash Hold is nice because it's clear enough for us to set up our figures. But what stinks is we don't have enough rocks for chairs or tables.\n\nYou're big and strong... d'ya think you could carry back some medium-sized rocks, smooth enough to sit on if we need a rest?","Return $1oa Smooth Boulders to Thra behind Grommash Hold.",3},
[97327]={"It breaks my heart to admit, but my brothers and sisters inside Blackmaw Hold are irreparably corrupted.\n\nIf you bring me some of their personal belongings, I can at least give their families something to remember them by. Every bundle you recover will serve as a symbol of your service to my people.","Enter Blackmaw Hold and recover $1oa Blackmaw Pouches for Ekkal at the Ruins of Eldarath in Azshara.",5},
[97328]={"<As you sift through the debris left behind by a horrible zeppelin crash directly above, you find evidence of a hefty shipment of supplies that has long since been plundered of all its value. Even the shipping labels have been torn and shredded, leaving only the words 'Booty Bay' barely legible on one.\n\nCountless two-toed footprints and several patches of divotted earth all lead toward ruins in the northwest.>","Recover $1oa Stolen Shipments from the Ruins of Zul'Kunda in Stranglethorn Vale and return your haul to someone in Booty Bay.",5},
[97378]={"$n, you have proven you are a strong and dutiful hunter and I am impressed by your bravery. It is only because of this I offer you this hunt.\n\nA wind serpent hunts along a road off the coast of Feralas and has been ambushing travelers, and leaving their corpses strewn about the road. It is clear she does not hunt out of necessity. This is a creature that no longer shares the Earthmother's blessing.\n\nThe windserpent Mirrorscale makes her lair at the bottom of the waterfall along the coast of Feralas.","Bring Mirrorscale's Wing to Melor Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.",5},
[97386]={"$n! Your arrival is timely, as always.\n\nYou have provided valuable assistance to the defense of Grom'gol, and we are grateful. After your recent push against the ogres nearby, we sent out a scout to see if there are more out there that may try to enact vengeance against us. As it turns out, there is a cave far to the east that they have claimed as their hovel.\n\nGather a friend or two and make it very clear that we will not tolerate another threat to our settlement, now or ever!","Commander Aggro'gosh of the Grom'gol base camp wants you to kill ogres at the Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mount.",6},
[97404]={"There are two old matriarchs, long aged past their cub rearing cycles. Perhaps they are sisters. They could also be two kindred bears who've shared a similar passing of seasons.\n\nRegardless of what has brought them together, they still have a ferocity and will to live that demands respect. Attempting to set up a camp like this one has been difficult for us, with these two grizzled Shardtooths.\n\nBring back the heads of Kuroma and Kamuro, and try to end them swiftly, skillfully, and with mercy.","Kill the old shardtooth matriarchs, Kuroma and Kamuro, and return their heads to Sarna Brownhorn.",5},
[97413]={"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.$B$BThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together. Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces.  Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.$B$BI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","Return to Mokvar in Orgrimmar with a set of Lightforge Boots, Lightforge Legplates and Lightforge Spaulders.",7},
[97420]={"I have a favor to ask of someone, and you look helpful!\n\nYou see this baby here? Ain't she a beaut? This is my newest racer, designed and built all by myself, because SOMEONE wouldn't help. I plan on taking this to the races in Thousand Needles, but it needs a little extra kick.\n\nNow, I'm too handsome to be a goblin, and I know better than to trust their tech, but I know the Venture Co struck liquid gold over at the lake. I'm sure they won't mind if you, erm, borrowed some? They won't even notice!","Acquire $1oa Drums of Crude Oil from the Venture Co. operations at Lake Nazferiti, then return to Knaz Blunderflame in Stranglethorn Vale.",5},
[97446]={"Ah, I've been expecting you $c. It would seem the winds have brought you to me this day. You have come seeking a kodo, correct?\n\nThe kodo is a noble beast that is slow to anger, and you would be hard pressed to find a more dependable companion.\n\nToday you have an important choice to make. You and your kodo will travel the world together, so find which one speaks to you. Fear not, whatever choice you make will be the right one.\n\nGo examine the kodos and return to me when you have made your choice.","Inspect the riding kodos to choose your first mount.",0},
[97447]={"Well met, $c. I've something that might interest you.$B$BI have in my possession a set of armor much like the one worn by those of your profession, but of much higher quality. I'd be willing to trade the bracers for ordinary ones in exchange for a small favor.$B$BThe blood of the frostsabers and bears that inhabit Winterspring has properties I'm in need of at the moment. Bring me a sizeable sample of it along with the bracers and a small amount of gold. You shall find the effort worth your while.","Acquire 15 Winterspring Blood Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Bindings of the Elements to Deliana in Ironforge.",5},
[97448]={"You kept your word and brought the device built by Mux. I believe a reward is in order if I'm to keep you interested in saving my skin. Bring me the belt and set of gauntlets that you wish to upgrade. I promise the ones I give you in return will be far superior.","Bring a Cord of the Elements and a set of Gauntlets of the Elements to Deliana in Ironforge.",7},
[97449]={"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.$B$BThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the medallion back together. Return to Deliana and tell her that Bodley is her only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to her about any rewards you've arranged for.$B$BI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","Return to Deliana in Ironforge with a set of Boots of Elements, Kilt of Elements and Pauldrons of Elements.",7},
[97485]={"Blessings of An'she, friend.\n\nWe tauren have a tradition of scattering incense to the winds and I was hoping you'd be interested in honoring this tradition.\n\nYou will need to craft the incense by purchasing herbs from Nida, cedar from Nata, sinew thread from Mahu in the mid rise, and ceremonial flint and tinder from Naal on the upper rise. Once you have these items, combine them and spread them off the south facing cliff of Hunter's Rise.\n\nYou will find a mat and incense at the ceremonial site.","Purchase a Bundle of Herbs from Nida the herbalist, a Bundle of Cedar Twigs from Nata the enchanting supplier, and Sinew Thread from Mahu the leatherworking supplier and Ceremonial Flint and Tinder from Naal the cooking supplier.\n\nCombine the items and sprinkle the incense off of Hunter's Rise.",3},
[97530]={"A merchant caravan took a wrong turn through the desert and got jumped by the Dunemaul ogres. Only reason they made it out alive is 'cause they tossed some cargo overboard to distract the brutes.\n\nMust be this merchant's got friends with the nobs runnin' ships and zeppelins, 'cause now they want ME pickin' up what got lost.\n\nI'm stuck here working. But if YOU see a nice shiny bangle while you're beatin' on ogres, I'll make it worth ya while.","Security Chief Bilgewhizzle of Steamwheedle Port in Tanaris wants you to recover a particularly shiny bangle bracelet lost near the Dunemaul ogre compound.",5},
[97534]={"Pssst, wanna know somethin'? It's easier to make profit in a place like this than you think... it's all about knowing how to market! I've seen what these tech-heads do when they get their hands on something they think they can turn into a fuel cell.\n\nEven better if it's still glowin' or sputtering steam.\n\nWhy don't we strike a deal? Bring back some of the parts that fall off their machines in the desert, and I'll kick you back a share of the coin I get from selling the salvage back to the junkers!","Quinn wants you to recover $1oa  pieces of Desert Debris and return to her in Gadgetzan.",4},
[97539]={"This encampment is being left to rot. The siege damage stands, unrepaired, as if neglect were policy. I won't permit that same decay here. The infirmary answers to me, and I intend to keep it functional.\n\nWe are nearly out of supplies. I'm going to need more equipment--enough to keep the workers and guards on their feet.\n\nUnder pressure, we can make quite an effective field suture using twisted spider silk.\n\n$C, bring me some from the spiders that stalk these highlands.","Return 12 Surgical Spidersilk to Doctor Gregory Victor in Hammerfall, Arathi Highlands.",5},
[97558]={"One part of undeath no one mentions is what happens when we are injured. How does the skin of an undead heal itself?\n\nWell, it doesn't.\n\nOurs is a cursed life, $n. We must take from the living to further our own existence.\n\nWhen we sustain an injury, we must replace our skin which usually means animal hides. Since different hide thicknesses are better for different places on our bodies a variety is key!\n\nBring me wing membranes of a duskbat, hides from a darkhound and skin of a Vile Fin murloc.","Bring Shelene Rhobart $1oa Duskbat Wing Membranes, $2oa Darkhound Hides and $3oa Vile Fin Murloc Skin.",4},
[97884]={"You look like a healthy, able-bodied $r. I am looking for someone to travel to Sunnyglade, in the Riverglades just north of the Redridge Mountains.\n\nMy family owned an armory there, once. Now I imagine it is a burnt husk, but I would have you retrieve a tome containing my family's ancestral armor crafting techniques. It was originally in the basement, so hopefully it has not succumbed to the elements just yet.","Travel to Sunnyglade in the Riverglades and recover the tome of Tremayne Family Blacksmithing Techniques.",5},
[97891]={"You! Quickly, I need you to bring this potion across the slime canal to Doctor Martin Felben in the Apothecarium!\n\nIt has a very limited shelf life, and no I can't go myself, my knees rattle and pop out if I attempt to run.\n\nJust another lovely side effect of undeath, apparently.\n\nBut we're wasting time! Here, take this and go!\n\n<Alessandro makes a shooing motion.>","Bring the Unstable Potion to Doctor Martin Felben in the Apothecarium within the time limit.",5},
[97901]={"Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.","Speak with Jhag in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97902]={"Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.","Speak with Mukdrak in Razor Hill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97903]={"So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a $c.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.","Speak with Rawrk in Razor Hill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97905]={"Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.","Speak with Jandi in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97906]={"You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\n\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.","Speak with Karolek in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97907]={"Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess.","Speak with Krunn in Razor Hill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97914]={"Auberdine is a humble place, $c. You won't hear its name spoken in the boughs of Darnassus. Most reference only what the Sundering took from us--the thriving cities of Ameth'Aran, Bashal'Aran, and... Lathar'Lazal.\n\nYet Auberdine remains in their shadow.\n\nI would see our work here recognized. A new vessel connects us to the kingdom of Stormwind, bringing life and supplies to our shores. I beseech you to join its next voyage, and bring this letter to a human called Baros Alexston.\n\nMake our home known.","Bring Thundris' Letter to Baros Alexston in Stormwind.\n\nThundris mentioned a boat in Auberdine that can take you there.",3},
[97915]={"So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.","Speak with Alchemist Mallory in Elwynn Forest near Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97917]={"Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.","Speak with Betty Quin in Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97918]={"Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.","Speak with Sprite Jumpsprocket in Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97919]={"So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a $c.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.","Speak with Michelle Belle in Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97922]={"You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\n\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.","Speak with Adele Fielder in Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97926]={"I wish it was that easy to help, $c. I really do.\n\nShould you choose to spend more time in our lands, you will find that many are without. Stormwind's coffers are not what they once were, and what remains is spread thin.\n\nGive this reply to the elder the next time you see him. It's not what he's hoping for, but it's all I have to offer right now.","Bring Alexston's Reply to Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine in Darkshore.",3},
[97930]={"Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.","Speak with Twizwick Sprocketgrind in the Venture Co. Mine in Mulgore to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97931]={"So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a $c.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.","Speak with Vira Younghoof in Bloodhoof Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97932]={"You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that.","Speak with Uthan Stillwater in Bloodhoof Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97934]={"You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\n\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.","Speak with Chaw Stronghide in Bloodhoof Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97935]={"Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess.","Speak with Brek Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97938]={"So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.","Speak with Cyndra Kindwhisper in Dolanaar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97939]={"So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons.","Speak with Elisa Steelhand in Auberdine in Darkshore to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97940]={"Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.","Speak with Alanna Raveneye in the Oracle Glade in Teldrassil to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97942]={"So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a $c.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.","Speak with Byancie in Dolanaar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97944]={"Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.","Speak with Malorne Bladeleaf in Dolanaar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97946]={"You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\n\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.","Speak with Nadyia Maneweaver on the road to Darnassus from Dolanaar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97949]={"Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.","Speak with Radnaal Maneweaver on the road to Darnassus from Dolanaar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97950]={"Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\n\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.","Speak with Trianna in Darnassus to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97953]={"Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.","Speak with Vance Undergloom in Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97954]={"Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.","Speak with Graham Van Talen in Undercity to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97955]={"So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a $c.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.","Speak with Nurse Neela in Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97958]={"You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\n\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.","Speak with Shelene Rhobart on the road to Undercity from Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97959]={"Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess.","Speak with Brom Killian in Undercity to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97960]={"Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.","Speak with Rand Rhobart on the road to Undercity from Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97961]={"Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\n\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.","Speak with Bowen Brisboise on the road to Brill from Deathknell to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97965]={"So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a $c.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.","Speak with Naleeia Tattermend in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97969]={"You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, $c. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\n\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.","Speak with Indari Sunseam in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97971]={"Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.","Speak with Mendalass Tattermend in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[97985]={"Fascinating, aren't they? This is the first time I have ever been privy to the secrets of abomination creation.\n\nI have been studying these notes, and it appears we need a heart. A massive one!\n\nI hear there is a thunder lizard there of impressive size called Stormheart, that patrols along the canyon edge in Thousand Needles. With a name like that it must have the perfect heart. I must have that heart!\n\nOh, also I suggest you bring friends. Stormheart isn't known for being docile.","Slay Stormheart in Thousand Needles and acquire its heart.",6},
[97987]={"Around the time these cliffs collapsed, I heard elvish ballistae firing. Bolts struck dangerously close to my home along the road to Quel'Thalas.\n\nI fled, leaving the avalanche of trees and rubble behind. I heard shouts in what could only have been shen'dorei! It was harsh even to my ear. I caught only a few words: \"traitor,\" \"blood,\" \"enemy.\"\n\nMy suggestion: take this knowledge to Saera Wirraway, a high order skyborne in Stormwind's Park. Though not of one line, we once shared a heart for answers.","Speak with Saera Wirraway in Stormwind in The Park.",5},
[98013]={"Steel yourself for your time in the ruins, young one... you will not be granted free passage there.\n\nScores of cursed Highborne, now known as naga, roam the once great city. Travel northeast and dispatch them from this land.\n\nWhat they once were... is no more. If they aid the Twilight's Hammer, they can bring only further pain to the forests that once gave them shelter.\n\nWar is what they seek, $c. War... is what we will bring.","Eliminate $1oa Stormscale Myrmidons, $2oa Stormscale Sorceresses, and $3oa Stormscale Warriors for Arbal at the Grove of the Ancients.",5},
[98021]={"If you'd like to get started doing some good in our world, I'd recommend reporting to a man named Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall to the south, at the settlement known as Sentinel Hill. His people are in need of aid.\n\nAfter journeying here from another plane of existence, the problems our lands face may seem small. I assure you, the aid you provide to those impacted by such problems means everything to them, and you will grow stronger for your labors.\n\nGood luck out there, adventurer!","Report To Gryan Stoutmantle at Sentinel Hill in Westfall.",3},
[98042]={"<As you tear away the single page from the Twilight Tome, a foreboding voice floods your mind, uninvited.>\n\nThey have failed.\n\nYou will be forgotten.\n\nThey will lose the eye they gained.","Obtain a Peerless Eye from a Twilight Disciple or Thug at the Master's Glaive in Darkshore and find someone in Auberdine who is willing to take it.",5},
[98059]={"Hillsbrad's council hasn't answered our new magistrate's letters. The last word I pried out of a passing merchant from the town did little to justify their silence.\n\nWe're only asking for a small platoon--yet I'm told multiple siege ballista rest in pristine condition within a walled-off compound.\n\nWalk into their town hall like a citizen returning a census request, and place this neatly upon the bookkeeping table.\n\nReturn to me when the deed is done.","Place the Sealed Company Request you were given on the bookkeeping table within Hillsbrad's town hall.",5},
[98067]={"General Feathermoon ensures all sentinels have time to pray to Elune. A proper huntress wields not blade alone, but gifts of the goddess to overcome our enemies.\n\nYou may help with my daily duties. Place sentinels around the city--start with the tunnels leading beneath Cenarion Hold to the north, the bank at the center of town, the inn in the Craftsman's Terrace to the northeast, and the city gates. The guards can assist you.\n\nSomething is amiss in Teldrassil--we must remain vigilant.","Place Sentinel Owls at the entrance to the Cenarion Hold depths, the Darnassus Bank, the Craftsman's Terrace Inn, and the City Gate for Sentinel Dalia Sunblade in the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",4},
[98070]={"The Screeching Canyon is home to a local band of harpies known for their ferocious nature and raiding tactics. They have ambushed the last few supply caravans that have been brave enough to traverse this place.\n\nI fear if something isn't done soon, there will be no caravans that will dare make the trek to Freewind Post.\n\nGo, slay as many of these harpies as you are able. Return to me once the deed has been done, and I will reward you well for your efforts.","Slay $1oa Screeching Harpies, $2oa Screeching Roguefeather Harpies and $3oa Screeching Windcaller Harpies.",5},
[98071]={"Worked a bit o' a trade with the Dun Garok brew-kin. We're not the only ones missin' the vineyards of the Fallrook family, it seems! Most o' the best bottled years are long since drank, but we do have cases of the wine still in the cellars. \n\nBring this case of Fallrook Varietal to Dun Garok in the southeast and leave it with 'em by their gatherin' fireplace at the bottom of their fort.\n\nIn return, carry a sack o' the Homebrew Hops back with ye.\n\nThat keep is the closest thing to home around here!","Deliver the bottles of Fallrook Varietal to Dun Garok in southeast Hillsbrad Foothills, and bring back a sack of their Homebrew Hops.",5},
[98072]={"You're quite the go-getter! I have just one more favor to ask, if you're up for something a bit more dangerous.\n\nThe crocolisk trade is steady money, but they're small fish compared to what whelp scales will bring. Folks will pay top dollar for a sack of those.\n\nCrocs of the sky, I call 'em! There's no way my apprentice could get them--but it seems right up your alley!\n\nYou'll find whelps far to the east, along the Green Belt. But be careful, there's nasty orcs in those hills!","Collect 8 Pristine Crimson Scales and bring them to James Halloran in Menethil Harbor.",5},
[98093]={"I'm so glad you saw me!\n\nThe weather was lovely this morning, so I walked from Camp Taurajo down the golden road. When it came time to head back, I couldn't--a pack of hyenas started circling, and Stormhide lizards blocked my only escape.\n\nScrambling up this tree I went, and now there are too many foes about at this hour for me to make the run home through the fields.\n\nWould you mind clearing out these Stormhide and Hecklefang Stalkers for me?","Sulhasa in southern Barrens wants you to clear out $1oa Stormhide lizards and $2oa Hecklefang Stalkers in the area so she can leave the tree safely.",5},
[98094]={"Now that we can trust you to deliver critical information to our forward spies, there's an extra task for you.\n\nBring this to Deathstalker Masoj almost directly south of us. He'll have more for you to do once you get there and hand this to him. He is posted on elevated terrain north of the rotten vineyard they call Nethander Stead.\n\nOur plan to take control of these lands continues steadily.","High Executor Darthalia wants you to deliver updated orders to Deathstalker Masoj, south of Tarren Mill, outside of Dun Garok.",3},
[98095]={"Our high command inserts strategic troops using bat riders. Key points around the foothills have lost their signaling beacons.\n\nTake these vials. Uncork them in three locations: the hills bordering Dun Garok, the plateau overlooking Dunholde Keep, and the last on the ridge of the Headland above the town of Hillsbrad. The vapors that emanate will be like a potent tuning rod to the senses of the bat, drawing them to the desired drop-off points once more.\n\nLook for crushed empty vials and renew our marks.","Deathstalker Masoj needs you to place the three Apothecary Vials on peaks around Hillsbrad Foothills and return to him.",5},
[98109]={"Hailen last said she was only going to survey the north reaches, so if it was her you found, there must be more to the story. Her last report contained useful intelligence regarding the stalwart ranger redoubt of Quel'Lithien Lodge.\n\nThere is a high elf, Adon, that resides northwest of the ruins of Northdale, near the road to Quel'Thalas. He might have a better understanding of the elven movements through these territories.\n\nI'll ensure we have a burial for this soul, whomever it may be.","Speak with Adon the high elf northwest of the ruins of Northdale, on the road to Quel'Thalas.",1},
[98156]={"$n, you have been so helpful to me I hate to ask for yet another favor. It will be some time until I am able to return home to Stormwind. I was wondering if you would mind delivering these pelts to my sisters in my stead?\n\nI am sure you are more likely to return there before I am able to. Please deliver these pelts to my sisters Kelly and Kimberly in Stormwind. They can usually be found in the Park.","Bring the Package of Pristine Pelts to Kimberly Grant.",5},
[98166]={"Greetings! Are you here to examine our horses?\n\nThese steeds are descendants from both the historical Lordaeron stock and our own local horses. You won't find a more steadfast companion for your journeys.\n\nChoosing one may be difficult as they are all excellent and trained to be steady even when in danger. Don't forget, you and your horse will traverse the world together. I'm sure whatever choice you make will suit you best.\n\nGo examine the horses and return to me when you have made your choice.","Inspect the riding horses to choose your first mount.",3},
[98190]={"You'll want to take this to Stormwind right away. Proud as I am that this keep and harbor bears King Terenas Menethil II's name, we are a calm harbor in a very nasty storm of enemies. It's just not safe here.\n\nThe Dragonmaw in particular would sacrifice much to loot something like this... and I shudder to think of what they'd do with it.\n\nDon't bother going up the chain of command on this one, $Glad:lass;. Go straight to Highlord Fordragon with this. He'll know where it will be best kept.","Bring the Menethil Statuette to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind Keep.",1},
[98191]={"King Terenas was a good man. A devout man. Beloved by his people, and truly the reason we have this Alliance at all.\n\nThe irony is he was humble--he hated these sorts of memorials, and so precious few exist. And of those, few survived Lordaeron's fall.\n\nIt seems the Light has coalesced in this statuette. It would be best kept in the Cathedral of the Light in Cathedral Square, in the center of the city. Bring it to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker for safekeeping.","Bring the Menethil Statuette to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in the Cathedral of Light.",5},
[98197]={"This harbor was first built by the Old Horde as a staging ground for their naval invasion of Hillsbrad. Completely circumvented Lordaeron's defenses!\n\nSo many lives lost...\n\nWhat's worse is that fleet was built with the very resources they stole from Khaz Modan!\n\nPlenty of it remains in the harbor after Admiral Proudmoore routed the brutes and built this place for the Alliance. We'll need it to bolster the town's defenses with the Dragonmaw on the move.","Recover $1oa Khaz Modan Timber and $2oa Khaz Modan Iron from Menethil Harbor for Valstag Ironjaw.",5},
[98203]={"The Witherbark know we be huntin' them like the traitors they are. Makin' plans and hideouts to keep their tribe in the shadows even after we burn 'em for their deceit.\n\nOur scouts be findin' a cave west of Hiri'watha. One witch doctor, Ti'ik, he bring his voodoo inside--rot, decay, an' wrigglin' larvae for some foul magic.\n\nWe not lettin' that filth crawl through our homes while we sleep. Go, take his head, and crush whatever they be growin'. \n\nHe be tough, so don't go underestimatin' him, ya?","Kill the Witherbark witch doctor known as Ti'ik in a cave west of Hiri'watha and return with his head.",6},
[98205]={"My associate Gizzix and I are looking to set up an outpost, and I can smell an opportunity here!\n\nOr maybe that's just the swamp gas. Either way, I could use some help.\n\nThe little black dragons flyin' around here haven't exactly been \"friendly\". They even singed poor Miss Melly!\n\nLook, I have some good coin for you if you're willing to get rid of some of these horrible dragon whelps.\n\nSo, you in or not?","Slay $1oa Searing Hatchlings and $2oa Searing Whelps.",5},
[98208]={"I came to Menethil Harbor from Auberdine, from the great tree Teldrassil, to recover a bloom of great import to my people.\n\nMy people's ship the Flying Osprey crashed here many moons ago, joined with the Kul Tiran Third Fleet. Among its cargo was the flower known as Nord'el--Bloom of the Heavens in your tongue--bloomed under a full moon at the peak of Mount Hyjal, our former home.\n\nPlease help me retrieve it! The wreckage is just south of the city, but it is inhabited by fierce murloc raiders!","Recover Nord'el for Sylessa Duskwhisper in Menethil Harbor.",4},
[98209]={"Would you please deliver Nord'el to elder Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine?\n\nThe boat from here should be able to get you there swiftly.\n\nI apologize for the request, I truly do. I remain fatigued from my journey here--and from fleeing those murloc devils when I first attempted to retrieve the sacred bloom!","Bring Nord'el to Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine in Darkshore.\n\nYou recall Sylessa mentioning a boat in Menethil Harbor can take you there.",3},
[98216]={"Old Gods?! This cannot be good news at all!\n\nI've made out a new bit on the stone that speaks of a guardian of some kind. Whatever it is, it must be linked to the stone!\n\nTake it with you and see if you can find a big Titan construct of some sort in the excavation. Read this here final passage on the stone and see what happens!\n\nIf I'm right, you'll activate the thing. Take it out if so, but try to preserve anything interesting! We simply must know more!","Use the Goaz Stone near the Goaz Warder and bring its Titanic Keystone back to Prospector Whelgar.",6},
[98219]={"Thank you again for delivering the statuette safely, $n.\n\nI could use your help with something else. There's a member of the city guard who was reassigned to duty in Southshore out in the Hillsbrad Foothills.\n\nHis father was a friend of mine, and while I don't disagree that he could use the lesson... I'd still like to see him succeed. He would really benefit from someone like you helping him out.\n\nThere is a boat that can take you that way from Menethil Harbor, if you are passing back through.","Speak to Lieutenant Farren Orinelle in Southshore in Hillsbrad Foothills.",1},
[98221]={"In the Second War the Dragonmaw built a fleet where we now stand, intending to take Hillsbrad. They nearly succeeded!\n\nThey were routed by the red dragons, left to mere stragglers deep in the mountains. However, there has been a surge in activity in their encampment northeast of Menethil.\n\nDun Algaz is proof that they intend to march to war once again and retake this land. Find their attack plans, take note of any critical information, and destroy them. We need to know where they will strike next!","Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Keep wants you to destroy the 4 sets of Attack Plans in the Angerfang Encampment.",5},
[98223]={"This book has been badly burned--perhaps by the dragonfire that destroyed much of the Dragonmaw clan.\n\nOf what little is legible, it seems to describe rituals relating to the use of the Demon Soul that the clan had used to control the dragons.\n\nIt is far too incomplete to be of real use, but based on roughly inserted pages on animal hide it seems Nek'rosh had attempted to salvage it. Freshly dried ink mentions a \"Shadow Council.\"\n\nCaptain Stoutfist in Menethil Harbor would want to know about this.","Bring the Tattered Spellbook to Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Harbor.",3},
[98230]={"After the War of the Three Hammers that tore dwarven life as we knew it apart, the Wildhammers settled here, founding the mountain fortress of Grim Batol.\n\nIt was a wondrous place. Gryphons soared everywhere you looked, diving down through the wetlands to grab a fish.\n\nIt didn't last long, sadly.\n\nHowin Kindfeather is one of the first Wildhammers to return in ages. Keeps to himself, far outside of town. Follow the road east--you'll find him eventually. He could surely use a hand.","Find Howin Kindfeather east of Menethil Harbor, along the road.",1},
[98245]={"I don't know who I hate more: the bloody Dark Irons, the Dragonmaw, or the drakes they rode.\n\n<Howin spits.>\n\nI aim tae make things right. But we're gonna need some supplies.\n\nThese whelp scales will protect against dragonfire a good bit, but they're a pain in the arse tae weave together.\n\nThe Razormaw raptors up in Raptor Ridge to the northeast and Saltspray Glen to the northwest are so named for their pointy chompers--they oughta break through the scales.\n\nBring me a handful of the incisors.","Collect $1oa Razormaw Incisors for Howin Kindfeather.",5},
[98246]={"I'll need some eggs if my plan is going tae work. Bassbeak needs a nice an' full belly--I ain't in the business of hoppin' on the back of a surly gryphon.\n\nThey need to be perfect--no cracks or anything.\n\nTake some from the Razormaw raptors--they're known for having yolks the size of a gnome's noggin. You can find 'em in Raptor Ridge to the northeast and Saltspray Glen to the northwest.\n\nLet's make it a nice even dozen, just to be safe.","Gather $1oa Perfect Razormaw Eggs for Howin Kindfeather.",5},
[98247]={"<A torn shipping label can be found on the side of the now fully stocked crate. Though the intended recipient is torn off, details of its origin still remain.\n\n\"Property of the Azeroth Commerce Authority. Please return empty crates or unfulfilled shipments to our local trade hub at the Three Corners crossroads in Redridge Mountains. Couriers will be compensated for their time and travel.\"\n\nBeside the text is a crudely drawn map of the area near the aforementioned destination.>","Deliver the Shipping Label to someone at the Azeroth Commerce Authority trade hub in Redridge Mountains.",1},
[98248]={"<A torn shipping label can be found on the side of the now fully stocked crate. Though the intended recipient is torn off, details of its origin still remain.\n\n\"Return damaged shipments or empty crates to the Durotar Supply and Logistics trade outpost, now conveniently located due west of the Crossroads in the Barrens. Your time is valuable and we will compensate you for your efforts!\"\n\nBeside the text is a crudely drawn map of the area near the aforementioned destination.>","Deliver the Shipping Label to someone at the Durotar Supply and Logistics trade hub near the Crossroads in the Barrens.",1},
[98282]={"Certain alchemical recipes require ingredients sourced from, well, very dangerous places. And those are often just the base herbs! The other ingredients are even worse!\n\nI need to make more antivenom before I can leave again. I swear everything in this marsh is venomous. It's like it runs through the land itself!\n\nCan you help me? I'll need a venom gland from the spiders in Thelgen Rock to the far southeast. But it has to be unruptured, or too much venom will spill out before you can get here. Sorry!","Collect an Unruptured Stalker Gland from Thelgen Rock for Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor.",5},
[98283]={"The natural order of this land is breaking. Once it was that the Razormaw raptors kept the land from overgrowth. They now live in fear of their alpha, named only for the carnage it leaves behind.\n\nI fear the beast has been driven mad by the sickness that we have yet to fully excise.\n\nIt will respond to the malignant flesh of the diseased bears below Raptor Ridge, to the northeast. Leave their entrails in its cave lair.\n\nCarnage will come. Bring me its head.","Bring Carnage's Head to Rethiel the Greenwarden in The Green Belt.",6},
[98285]={"An engineer is ever-resourceful, and if you are in the wilds alone, it's always good to be able to put your trade to use. No good camp is complete without a few helpful constructs!\n\nYes, come back and see me when you've gained a little bit of experience as an engineer and I can show you how to make something special!","Speak with the Strange Hermit in Shadowgale Forest to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[98286]={"Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.","Speak with Nasalanna Windsinger in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[98287]={"Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.","Speak with Sprite Jumpsprocket in Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",3},
[98291]={"I plan tae get back into Grim Batol and reclaim it for the Wildhammers, $n. Or at least learn a thing or two.\n\nDon't look at me like that, now. I know the risks. I don't intend tae go in hammer swingin', ye know.\n\nRegardless, I'll need your help first. The Dragonmaw orcs march as we speak. They're all up an' down the Dragonmaw Retreat, where the red dragons routed them before.\n\nI need you tae thin their numbers before I have any chance of gettin' close. Ye can't miss 'em if you follow the road east.","Kill $1oa Dragonmaw Reclaimers, $2oa Dragonmaw Soulbinders, and $3oa Dragonmaw Infiltrators in Dragonmaw Retreat for Howin Kindfeather.",6},
[98293]={"The Dragonmaw are stockpiling all manner of weaponry. It would be wise to relieve them of these before more soldiers can be armed.\n\nCaptain Stoutfist in Menethil Keep would surely be interested in these.","Collect $1oa Dragonmaw Armaments in Dragonmaw Retreat, then bring them to Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Keep.",5},
[98297]={"I did a quick test flight while ye were out. The good news is the armor ye helped me craft for Bassbeak works like a charm!\n\nThe very bad news is I saw a group o' them Dragonmaw in the process of enslavin' a red dragonspawn.\n\nAbsolutely not. Not again.\n\nYou have tae take it out. You'll certainly need friends tae do so. Kill the warlocks holding it down first--that ought tae free it. Then put it out of its misery.\n\nNone of them will stand in the way of the Wildhammer.","Kill the Subdued Dragonspawn at the Dragonmaw Gates for Howin Kindfeather.",5},
[98298]={"Ah, it's all become so embarrassingly clear! Arugal hardly had any magic at all, let alone enough to create the worgen. 'Arugal's Curse.' Pah! Barely potent enough to last a few seconds.\n\nThese shackles prove he can bind the beasts, not create them. The worgen clearly spread their curse a different way. I would know how.\n\nGo to the Greymane Wall to the south. The worgen seem to be spreading to the humans nearby. Tear the beasts apart and bring me whatever you find. This requires a more direct approach.","Bring $1oa Worgen Bits to Dalar Dawnweaver in The Sepulcher.",5},
[98299]={"If there is one thing we do know, it is that Arugal is responsible for worgen within Silverpine--be it his own machinations or otherwise. What we don't know is how it spreads.\n\nWhile I research a way to stop the curse, our first priority is to contain it. It appears this affliction cannot infect forsaken, but a large group of humans have gathered by the Greymane Wall.\n\nGo to the wall and put down these refugees before they have a chance to become servants for Arugal. And try not to get bit, $r.","Slay $1oa Sickly Refugees and $2oa Haggard Refugees for Dalar Dawnweaver in The Sepulcher.",5},
[98300]={"My work here is far from over, $n. And I need tae send word to me wife Claira in Aerie Peak--and get Falstad an update as well.\n\nBut that's my business. Wildhammer business.\n\nThat said, you ought tae let King Magni Bronzebeard in Ironforge know about all this as well. Wetlands is but a stone's throw from his lands, and none of what's happenin' here is good news on one's doorstep. This letter oughta do the trick.\n\nYe can travel back through Dun Algaz or fly from Menethil Harbor to get to Ironforge.","Deliver Howin's Missive to King Magni Bronzebeard in Ironforge.",5},
[98310]={"There are other, larger golems all around the Wetlands. They each bear inscriptions marking them as Ados, Modr, Golm, and Neru--matching the missing pieces of the Goaz Stone you found!\n\nI'd be willing to bet if we can bring pieces of them as well, we'll reveal more of the Goaz Stone!\n\nYou'll find Ados at the Dragonmaw Gates to the east, near Grim Batol. Modr is right outside Dun Modr to the north. Golm lies beneath Grim Batol, east of Dun Algaz. Neru's behind Direforge Hill, to the northeast.","Use the Goaz Stone near Ados, Modr, Golm, and Neru and bring their hearts back to Prospector Whelgar.",6},
[98313]={"Whatever this is all about, $n, it's epic stuff alright.\n\nI'll bundle everything up nice for you. Take it to Historian Karnik in the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge. You'll usually find him in the back, nose-deep in some tome or another in the library.\n\nIt'll take a downright army to crack the case on this one, but if what we've seen so far is any indication it will well be worth it!","Bring the Whelgar Relic Package to Historian Karnik in Ironforge.",0},
[98319]={"It's bad enough havin' a troll problem, but the mountains are filled tae the brim with wendigos! They normally keep to their own caves, but they seem tae be spreadin' like bunnies. Now they've filled the Grizzled Den north of here.\n\nIf we want Whitebeard's report, we're gonna need to find my partner Cornelius. The blockhead got a little too excited and charged in head first. Brave, but stupid.\n\nHead into the cave and see where he is. And feel free to take out some of the beasts while yer at it.","Find Mountaineer Cornelius in the Grizzled Den for Mountaineer Gretchen.",3},
[98321]={"Hoha! Good to see a $r who's not afraid to get their hands dirty.\n\nIf yer lookin' fer work, I'm afraid I'm a little short on supplies at the moment. Our most reliable source of ore has been overrun by wendigo and now the cave has been abandoned. The miners had to drop everything when they fled!\n\nSay, why don't ye poke yer head around the Grizzled Den to the west and see if you can find some of our missing shipments. It would save us a great deal o' trouble.","Collect $1oa Flintfire Shipments from the Grizzled Den for Tongus Flintfire in Kharanos.",5},
[98322]={"Spelunking dark caves is adventurer business. My job's just to make reports and send them over to Ironforge.\n\nTrouble is, one of my reports hasn't... well, reported back. I asked a few mountaineers to learn more about the wendigo problem we have out here, but I haven't heard from them.\n\nIf you're already going to be out and about, what say you check in with Mountaineer Gretchen just west of town. I'm late enough as it is!","Check in on Mountaineer Gretchen west of Kharanos.",1},
[98325]={"I seek the best the Horde has to offer, $c. And ONLY the best.\n\nThere are certain tasks that require a degree of valor that few possess. And fewer still are willing to lay it on the line when it really counts.\n\nAre you $r enough to do what must be done? Let us speak if so.\n\nIf not, begone. I have no time to waste on cowardice.","Speak to Warlord Goretooth to serve the Kargath Expeditionary Force.",1},
[98326]={"Do ye know how hard it is to fish on a frozen lake? My poor husband, Paxton, has been out in the middle of it for days and we barely have a single sack to show fer it.\n\nWell, we DID have a sack to show fer it. Until the thrice-damned wendigo attacked me and made off with our haul. It'll take us weeks to fish all that back up! If that loudmouth Frosthowl didn't scare 'em all off, anyway.\n\nDo us a favor and get it back, aye? Drooling brute is hiding somewhere deep in the Grizzled Den to the southeast.","Slay Frosthowl and collect the Sack of Fish for Gretta Ganter in Brewnall Village.",5},
[98340]={"It would seem that you are ready for the next step in your journey, young druid. Dendrite Starblaze has sent for you, and wishes for you to seek him out in Moonglade once again.\n\nYou have already learned to call upon the magic to take you to Moonglade, so you should be able to embark immediately if you choose. I would suggest you leave soon, if you wish to continue your druidic training.","Speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.",2},
[98342]={"To draw upon my spirit, you will need more than a few words. To understand and respect my form you must prove that you can embody cunning, stealth, and if you should be cornered, ferocity.\n\nIn the Barrow Dens just east of here, are three relics of my favor you must acquire. They are guarded by powerful enraged spirits that will attack you on sight. A statue at the entrance will bless you with temporary stealth to get past them.\n\nReturn these relics to me. We will see if you are ready to take my shape.","Recover the Relic of the Fang, Relic of the Claw, and Relic of the Silent Shadow from the Stormrage Barrow Den, and return them to the Great Cat Spirit.",3},
[98362]={"The time has come for us to part ways once again, young one, as the application of your lessons takes you back to the one who sent you to me. It would seem your instructor, Turak Runetotem, has found a worthy pupil in you. I believe I see one as well. Heed his lessons and you shall soon be able to draw upon the Great Cat Spirit to take its shape.\n\nGo back to whence you came. When the time is right, we will meet again.","Return to Thunder Bluff and speak with Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise.",1},
[98372]={nil,nil,0},
[98387]={"You can't fight a war without weapons.\n\nThough the Blackrock orcs have encroached upon these lands, their brazen efforts are not without certain vulnerabilities.\n\nHead southeast below Stonewatch Keep, seek out their encampments, and target their weapons and supplies.\n\nWe'll see just how much of a threat they are without their tools of war.","Bring $1oa Stolen Weapons and $2oa Blackrock Supplies to Marshal Marris in Lakeshire.",5},
[98389]={"Greetings, $c. Yes, I am a paladin. Not even death can stop the Light.\n\nThis is something my kind have in common with all Forsaken--we have overcome what the living view as their end. However, some even among our own fear us; they suspect we will smite them as some monstrosity.\n\nIn truth, our relationship with undeath is complex, but I am not here to hurt our own. Help me show the others this. Venture to Night's Web Hollow to the northwest and free the freshly raised fools trapped by the spiders there.","Free $1oa Webbed Victims in Night's Web Hollow for Aramis Hammerhand in Deathknell.",5},
[98391]={"Blessings to you, $c. The Sisterhood of Elune has stood as a pillar of kaldorei society for thousands of years.\n\nBefore the Great Sundering, before the War of the Ancients, through the Long Vigil, we have guided and healed our people through the darkness. Such is our charge, and such is the demand of the peerless Mother Moon.\n\nWe now require your aid in a matter of great importance. Sister Aquinne awaits your arrival in Darnassus.","Speak to Sister Aquinne in Darnassus.",1},
[98392]={"These belts... look closely at the leather, $n. Do you see the taint running through the fibers?\n\nI have a suspicion as to its origin, but we will need further proof to be sure.\n\nVenture back out into the harpies' nests to the west and take out their leaders. If their necklaces carry the same darkness as these belts, we'll have our answer.","Collect Hatescreech's Amulet, Windmistress Gaedress' Amulet, and Witchmother Arysa's Amulet for Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak in the Oracle Glade.",5},
[98394]={"In the southern part of Moonglade, on a hill overlooking the bridge, resides a wise and cunning being we call the Great Cat Spirit.\n\nMuch like the Great Bear Spirit, this spirit has served as a tutor and mentor to druids that desire to take the feline shape. All druids eventually seek its wisdom, and if you desire to take the form of a cat, you will as well.\n\nGo meet with the Great Cat Spirit and learn what it will teach you.","Seek out the Great Cat Spirit in southern part Moonglade and learn what it has to share with you about the nature of the cat.",3},
[98398]={"I am impressed by what you have accomplished here in so short a time, $n. Would that I could ask you to remain here to assist me with my duties... but I know in my heart that greater tasks lie ahead for you.$b$bI have noticed the Oracle Tree has just shed a piece of its bark. No doubt it has a task that it wishes completed. You should speak with it.","Find the Oracle Tree Bark nearby to receive its message.",1},
[98403]={"Lord Melenas did not act alone; he was at the behest of another. The one you seek is Xethorr the Wicked. It seems he has twisted the spiders that call Teldrassil home, intending their venom for some foul plan.\n\nHe has taken residence deep in the forest, in the area to the northwest of here known as the Cleft. Take caution, and bring allies, for Xethorr is not an opponent to be trifled with.\n\nDispatch his brood, and bring me anything that may tell us more of the satyr's work here.","Kill $1oa Befouled Webwoods and bring Xethorr the Wicked's Mature Fel Moss to Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar.",5},
[98404]={"In order to draw upon my spirit, you will need to undergo a trial. To understand and respect my form you must prove that you can embody cunning, stealth, and if you should be cornered, ferocity.\n\nIn the Barrow Dens just east of here, are three relics you must acquire. They are guarded by powerful enraged spirits that will attack you on sight. A statue at the entrance will bless you with temporary stealth to get past them.\n\nReturn these relics to me to pass the druidic trial of these lands.","Recover the Relic of the Fang, Relic of the Claw, and Relic of the Silent Shadow from the Stormrage Barrow Den, and return them to the Avatar of Saeyleenan.",3},
[98405]={"In the southern part of Moonglade, on a hill overlooking the bridge, resides a wise and cunning being we call the Great Cat Spirit.\n\nMuch like the Great Bear Spirit, this spirit has served as a tutor and mentor to druids that desire to take the feline shape. All druids eventually seek its wisdom, and if you desire to take the form of a cat, you will as well.\n\nGo meet with the Great Cat Spirit and learn what it will teach you.","Seek out the Great Cat Spirit in southern part Moonglade and learn what it has to share with you about the nature of the cat.",3},
[98407]={"If the gnolls are growing so bold they are willing to camp this close to humans, there's no telling how much further they'll go. We need to deter them.\n\nThe beasts are hardly organized, but they seem to respect strength above all else. If we can slay the worst of them, maybe claim some of their trophies, we can remind these gnolls why they should stay in the hills where they belong.\n\nShould you see any of their thrashers, bring me their collars. That should put the fear of the Alliance back into them.","Collect $1oa Spiked Collars from Redridge Thrashers for Deputy Feldon near Lakeshire.",4},
[98418]={"Kurothel mentioned sightings of what they say are wolf-men. Those of the pack now lurking in greater numbers in our forest. Last we had spoken, druids were pursuing communication with those of the beast heart who displayed measured control of their animal instincts.\n\nHis written words show a darker struggle. If there is anything we can do to help see HIM again, surely quelling the demon threat that is driving him to this burning transformation will be of aid to his anguished soul.\n\nSlay the Xavian, $n.","Kill $1oa Xavian Rogues, $2oa Felsworn, $3oa Betrayers, and $4oa Hellcallers.\nReturn to Maseara Autumnmoon in Forest Song afterwards.",5},
[98423]={"Inside of the vault you find a tablet detailing the terms of a peace treaty between the Bronzebeard and Wildhammer dwarf clans. It appears to date back to the time period just after the War of the Three Hammers, and is very likely a notable piece of dwarven history. The king of Ironforge would no doubt be interested in this artifact.","Deliver the Treaty of Understanding to Magni Bronzebeard in Ironforge.",5},
[98426]={nil,nil,0},
[98427]={"The shredder one of the pages speaks of--I have seen them before in my travels. They can decimate a forest in a fraction of the time that hand and axe can.\n\nEntire glades--homes to the Earth Mother's children for millennia--erased in days.\n\nWe will not allow this to happen in our home, a stone's throw from where our young ones take their first steps.\n\n$n, I must ask you to gather others, go back into the mine to the northeast, and ensure it fells not a single tree more.","Bring the Clearcutter Key to Morin Cloudstalker outside Bloodhoof Village.",6},
[98430]={"Hail, $c. What brings you deep into such a dark and violent place?\n\nI was sent here by High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof as a part of our efforts to communicate with the gnolls that have taken residence. The rest of my mission must remain a secret, as do all things with the Longwalkers, the trusted scouts of our chieftain.\n\nAll you must know is our diplomacy was met with violence, and I fear I may be tonight's feast for the gnolls if you do not help me escape.\n\nAre you up to the task?","Help Perith Stormhoof escape Palemane Rock, and report his safety to Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff.",5},
[98459]={"Bart Tidewater's a no-good cheapskate, I tell ya!\n\n\"Captain of the Maiden's Virtue\" he calls himself. That ship's sailed as far as a rock in Tanaris! He's no captain, he's an actor who won enough hands of poker to buy the Virtue in the first place!\n\nIf you ever find yourself in Menethil Harbor over in the Wetlands, give this to him and let him know it's from ol' Half-fish.\n\nThere's a boat from here that can take you right to the harbor, by the way. It'll be the second stop!\n\nAnd he cheats at poker!","Deliver Tom's Gift to Bart Tidewater in Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",1},
[98461]={"If you're heading out of Auberdine, I could use your help!\n\nMy dear friend Tarrel and I were classmates in school. Oh, he was such a quickfire on all things excavation! We got split up after graduation--him to Wetlands, and me to here in Darkshore.\n\n<Hollee sighs, then her brow furrows slightly.>\n\nSorry, and his wife... Merrin.\n\nIt doesn't matter. If you go to the Wetlands, could you make sure he's alright? And maybe give him this? He's probably near Menethil Harbor. There's a boat straight there.","Deliver Hollee's Note to Tarrel Rockweaver near Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",1},
[98463]={"Look, I'm glad to have you at my bar, and that's exactly why I'm telling you this.\n\nThe real party? That's over at the Salty Sailor Tavern in Booty Bay. Yes, in Stranglethorn Vale--that Booty Bay.\n\nDon't give me that look. I know it's run by goblins. Bartenders talk, and bar patrons talk a LOT. All I'm saying is that if you want to see things get real wild, head over there.\n\nNixxrax Fillamug will keep you topped up, don't even worry.","Visit Nixxrax Fillamug in the Salty Sailor Tavern in Booty Bay in Stranglethorn.",1},
[98471]={"Greetings, $n. \n\nI have an assignment for you that is of the utmost priority. Please meet me in the mountains called Alterac, northwest of the village known as Strahnbrad. I will meet you at the cliff overlooking the Uplands valley.\n\nCome alone, and tell no one.","Meet Elaadrin Evengale at the cliffs overlooking The Uplands in Alterac Mountains.",3},
[98477]={"Any experienced shaman who attempts to scry the elemental plane can tell you that there is a blip of sorts, a distortion that you feel as you cross over to the other realms of existence.\n\nWe have need of adventurers like yourself to help us better understand this disturbance. Take this Elemental Attractor. You will be able to extract motes of unstable magic with it from the most skilled spellcasters and other powerful entities you may encounter. Bring me these motes so that we may study them.","Bring $1oa Motes of Unstable Magic to Nuara Tremorhoof.",6},
[98512]={"You there, stranger. Get low and keep quiet. We are not alone here.\n\nI was on patrol near the border and noticed that there are a number of Al'Aketh skulking around the house just up the hill there to the north. I don't know what they are doing here, but it can't be good.\n\nIf you want to make yourself useful, get in there and take them out. I'll wait here and watch your back.","Kill 10 Al'Aketh Assassins in the Shen'dar Highlands.",5},
[98517]={"Greetings, young Skyborne. The spirits have spoken of you, and tell me that you are ready to heed the call of fire. However, I shall not be the one to start you on that Path. Return to your home in the elemental plane, seek your mentors there. They will tell you what must be done.","Report to Sessaria Skystride or Aarnor Galestrike on Zephras Isle to continue your training as a Shaman. \n\nYou can return to Zephras via the skycutter transport that docks in Mulgore at Skywatcher Plateau, northwest of Thunder Bluff.",3},
[98545]={"Since you are here, I'd like you to deliver this letter to an old friend of mine in the Undercity. I'd deliver myself but I have a somewhat colorful history with the Dark Lady, and it would be better if a neutral third party made the delivery.\n\nYou are looking for a goblin named Glix Xizzix in the Trade Quarter area of the Undercity. I'm sure he'd be happy to compensate you for your time.\n\n<Leonid lets out a low chuckle as he hands you the letter.>","Deliver the Sealed Letter to Glix Xizzix in the Undercity.",1},
[98574]={"While you were helping me out, this memorandum was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the priest trainer Branstock. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance.","Read the Hallowed Memorandum and speak to Branstock Khalder in Anvilmar.",3},
[98576]={"Ah, while you were gone a parchment came for you, $n.$B$BRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the mage trainer Mai'ah. She would have words with you when you're ready.","Read the Glyphic Parchment and speak with Mai'ah near the entrance to the Den in the Valley of Trials.",3},
[98581]={"While you were helping me out, this rune was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. Based on the Wildhammer style to these inscriptions, I'm guessin' this came from the shaman trainer Teo Hammerstorm. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance.","Read the Archaic Rune and speak to Teo Hammerstorm in Anvilmar.",3},
[98601]={"While you were off dealing with the mindless Scourge, this scroll arrived for you. It reeks of the light, so I imagine it's of some importance to a paladin like yourself.\n\nRead it before heading out again. Just please--step away when you do. Paladins make me quite uneasy.","Read the Consecrated Scroll and speak to Aramis Hammerhand in the church in Deathknell.",3},
[98739]={"Now that you have received my blessing, return to Dendrite. He will instruct you further. I do hope we meet again someday.\n\nMay the shadows forever hide you and your foes easily fall prey to your claws, young one.","Speak to Dendrite.",3},
[98815]={"The Highlands are host to ruins of some sort, secrets now being explored by an expedition team. What I know is that they've got their own wildlife and beasts lurking in that mountain marshland. How about you take a foray in there with some well-equipped friends, and we work a trade?\n\nI don't care if they're hiding, I want their hides! Bring me the skins from four of the Thicket Raptors, I'll have a trade worked out for you to make it worth it.","Return $1oa Thicket Raptor Hides to James Halloran, the tanner, in Menethil Harbor.",3},
[98830]={"The air smells sharp and metallic as you reach down to inspect the corpse of Prince Tortheldrin. Extremely powerful magic was just dispelled here.\n\nYou notice that the corpse before you looks old and weathered, lacking the vitality that the prince exuded before he fell. There are other physical differences as well.\n\nOne of Tortheldrin's glaives lies near his body, broken in two. The Shen'dralar Ancients will want to know of what you observed here.","Deliver Tortheldrin's Broken Glaive to the Shen'dralar Ancient in Dire Maul.",5},
[98893]={"The Theramore Expeditionary Force are tenacious and continue to send reinforcements to bolster their position on the Darkspear Islands. $B$BGo, show them the might of the horde! Bring me the evidence of your victory in this key battleground and you will be well rewarded.","Bring 3 Darkspear Islands Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.",5},
[98895]={"The battle against the Darkspear Raiders is heating up. Without urgent aid, the Darkspear Islands will be lost to us. $B$BIt is your duty as a proud member of the Alliance to ensure this does not happen. Bring me proof of your contributions on the front lines and you will be revered as a hero of the Alliance!","Bring 3 Darkspear Islands Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.",3},
[98897]={"The battle against the Darkspear Raiders is heating up. Without urgent aid, the Darkspear Islands will be lost to us. $B$BIt is your duty as a proud member of the Alliance to ensure this does not happen. Bring me proof of your contributions on the front lines and you will be revered as a hero of the Alliance!","Bring 3 Darkspear Islands Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.",0},
[98899]={"The battle against the Darkspear Raiders is heating up. Without urgent aid, the Darkspear Islands will be lost to us. $B$BIt is your duty as a proud member of the Alliance to ensure this does not happen. Bring me proof of your contributions on the front lines and you will be revered as a hero of the Alliance!","Bring 3 Darkspear Islands Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.",5},
[98901]={"The battle against the Darkspear Raiders is heating up. Without urgent aid, the Darkspear Islands will be lost to us. $B$BIt is your duty as a proud member of the Alliance to ensure this does not happen. Bring me proof of your contributions on the front lines and you will be revered as a hero of the Alliance!","Bring 3 Darkspear Islands Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.",5},
[98903]={"Go forth and represent the Theramore Expeditionary Force in battle at Darkspear Islands, $n! Achieve victory and show these Horde dogs the might of the Alliance!","Win a Darkspear Islands battleground and return back to Brelinda McFarry at Northwatch Hold.",5},
[98904]={"Go forth and represent the Theramore Expeditionary Force in battle at Darkspear Islands, $n! Achieve victory and show these Horde dogs the might of the Alliance!","Win a Darkspear Islands battleground and return back to Brelinda McFarry at Northwatch Hold.",5},
[98905]={"Go forth and represent the Theramore Expeditionary Force in battle at Darkspear Islands, $n! Achieve victory and show these Horde dogs the might of the Alliance!","Win a Darkspear Islands battleground and return back to Brelinda McFarry at Northwatch Hold.",5},
[98906]={"The battle at the Darkspear Islands be locked in a stalemate, $c. Show those Alliance fools who the superior force is. \n\nCarry your head high in service of the Darkspear and claim victory in battle. The Loa will surely be givin' you their blessing, $c!","Win a Darkspear Islands battleground and return back to Nizook Boof at The Merchant Coast.",5},
[98908]={"The battle at the Darkspear Islands be locked in a stalemate, $c. Show those Alliance fools who the superior force is. \n\nCarry your head high in service of the Darkspear and claim victory in battle. The Loa will surely be givin' you their blessing, $c!","Win a Darkspear Islands battleground and return back to Nizook Boof at The Merchant Coast.",5},
[98977]={nil,nil,0},
[99046]={"The Council of the Forest sent a small group of sentinels to the Oracle Tree some time ago. The tree sends messages to our elders, and it falls to us to deliver them to Darnassus safely.\n\nI received word that our most recent runner has not yet arrived. The Oracle's messages vary in frequency, but it has been abnormally long.\n\nPlease head towards the Oracle Glade along the road to the west and check on her. It would have been Eralya Leafshadow's turn, and she is still in training. Elune guide you.","Search for Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow on the road leading to the Oracle Glade.",1},
[99052]={"One of my scouts has reported a sea giant followed those naga down here. Not sure if they brought him intentionally or what, but he's dangerous in any case.\n\nIt's a young one, but it could still rip an orc in half in a heartbeat if they were caught off guard. I need him gone. But I'd suggest you find some help to deal with it.","Kill the sea giant along Durotar's north coast and bring back proof of your accomplishment.",6},
[99073]={"The salve is ready. Take it to Eralya swiftly.\n\nI do not know if it will truly cure her. The rot festers quickly, and grows in strength as it spreads.\n\nIt will, if nothing else, ease her suffering. And that is still worth your haste.","Take the Lashwater Salve to Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow on the road to the Oracle Tree.",1},
[99079]={"The Longwalkers are our people's most trusted scouts. Though their loyalty lies with the High Chieftain alone, young Baine at times seeks their aid.\n\nThis is one such time. Longwalker Malah was dispatched near our borders to the east and did not return last night after three days. When this occurs, it is our duty to confirm their safety.\n\nI must ensure the village remains safe. Prove yourself, and seek Malah out. You will know her by her headband and feathered staff, emblematic of the Longwalkers.","Find Longwalker Malah Longwind east of Bloodhoof Village, near the edge of Mulgore.",1},
[99082]={"Your bravery defending your people demands recognition. Journey to Thunder Bluff to the northwest, our mighty city whose shadow grants us shade in the warmer months, and seek audience with my father.\n\nIt was he who led the charge with the young Warchief Thrall to reclaim these plains and drive the centaur away for good. As High Chieftain, he will reward you generously for your part in ensuring his own bravery is honored.\n\nYou must take a lift to reach the High Chieftain, who sits on the central rise.","Seek audience with High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff.",1},
[99101]={"Baine Bloodhoof leads our village. He must know of this incursion at once.\n\nBring him Longwalker Malah's report. You will find him at the center of town.\n\nQuickly, now. There is no time to waste!","Bring Longwalker Malah's Report to Baine Bloodhoof.",1},
[99128]={"This can only be the work of those murlocs on the other side of the lake. They're disgusting little things, with a vicious temper and teeth to match. \n\nIf we let this continue, there won't be any fish to speak of anywhere in this lake. If you could clear them out a bit, it would help me a ton.","Kill $1oa Murlocs and $2oa Murloc Streamrunner at Crystal Lake, then return to Jason Mathers.",5},
[99134]={"You are not a member of the Deathguard, and therefore have yet to disappoint me.\n\nAs a reward for your relative lack of incompetence, you shall punish those that have demonstrated such talents in excess.\n\nSwiftly now--$n, is it?--or I shall add your name to my ledger for someone else's reward.","Punish $1oa Deathguards for Executor Zygand.",4},
[99141]={"Make no mistake, $c--the Dark Lady demands the perfect execution of her will. As an Executor, it is my duty to see that this happens.\n\nReports from several of my Deathguards are overdue. Needless to say, my patience has run out. Obtain their reports and bring them to me in the Dark Lady's name.\n\nYou will find Deathguard Dillinger just west of here, by the graveyard. Deathguard Kristof is stationed at the waystation to the east. And check on the abomination Gordo; he wanders west near Stillwater Pond.","Obtain reports from Deathguard Dillinger, Deathguard Kristof, and Gordo for Executor Zygand.",4},
[99142]={"If you're heading east, towards the Balnir Farmstead, I have more you might do for me. Good help is ever so hard to find these days, as your run-in with Gordo illuminates ever so clearly.\n\nAs I acquire doom weed I perform some minor alchemical alterations and replant them on that farmstead to cultivate my ultimate creation. I call it tomb weed, and it shall be the herald of my glorious destiny.\n\nDo keep an eye on the Scourge in the area while you're there. They seem... drawn... to the weed. Curious.","Collect $1oa Tomb Weed and deliver them back to Junior Apothecary Holland.",5},
[99143]={"Those fish men must think like actual fish, right? Which means anything they like, fish will like!\n\nIf you rummage through some of their junk and return to me with anything that seems like it would make good bait, I'll reward you.","Collect $1oa pieces of shiny junk from the nearby Murloc camp.",4},
[99144]={"Light bless you for finding me. I was on my way from Bandarion Keep to deliver a message to Shari Stilwell in Brill when these monsters captured me. They wield the Light with a hatred in their hearts that makes what's left of my blood seethe. It goes against all I meditate for... all I strive to protect!\n\n<Bareth Dawnstone steadies himself.>\n\nI know some still take issue with my kind, but I assure you our intentions are pure. If you would aid me in escaping this place, I would be forever grateful.","Help Bareth Dawnstone escape Crusader's Outpost, and report his safety to Shari Stilwell in Brill.",5},
[99145]={nil,nil,0},
[99152]={"While the Tarnished in Shadowvale to the southwest are definitely a problem, we cannot allow the cellars below the town to fester into a full-blown Scourge uprising on Bandarion Keep.\n\nI need to get these trainees up to snuff in case that happens. You, however, are going to receive what I like to call a crash course.\n\nTravel beneath Shadowvale and retrieve some of their wretched bones so we can study them further. I need ones that still retain some of the initial reanimation magic--that's glowing ones.","Collect $1oa Faintly Glowing Bones for Hilda the Breaker.",5},
[99153]={"Oi, you! Word travels quickly among our ranks. I heard about the work you did with the cultists around the remnants of the battle with Naxxramas.\n\nProblem is, one of them cultists got away with a piece of the focusing crystal. Seems to still have some juice in it. Best guess we have is it's somewhere beneath Shadowvale. It's either raising 'em or making 'em stronger, and you don't want either one.\n\nFind that crystal before this gets out of hand.","Find the Hidden Crystal Fragment beneath Shadowvale for Ephram Barbaro.",5},
[99156]={"Damn it all! A new report came in while you were on patrol. There has been a sighting of a rogue abomination wandering Eastern Tirisfal Glades, near Venomweb Vale.\n\nSomething is wrong. Abominations don't just slip through the Bulwark unnoticed.\n\nKeep this matter on a strictly need-to-know basis. That said, such a creature will not fall easily; you will need allies if you wish to be more than its next meal.\n\nSee this through, and you will be duly rewarded. Bring me its heart as proof of the deed.","Bring Riptear's Heart to Deathguard Linnea.",5},
[99160]={"You may have noticed the elementals nearby. A shelf of rock and ice fell from the mountain peaks a few days ago and riled them up.\n\nThese frozen mountains are already treacherous for the average dwarf or human without the elements taking form. I am not one for fighting anymore--so any of the spirits you can kill would help make the road safer.","Destroy $1oa minor ice elementals.",4},
[99161]={"I noticed that the first elemental that appeared after the rockslide was larger than its peers. And from what I can tell, it has been the source of occasional weather changes and other minor slides.\n\nI've been calling it 'Avala', if you could kill it and retrieve the core as proof, I will reward you.","Kill Avala and retrieve its core.",5},
[99162]={"Even mountaineers from Ironforge have to keep their wits about them when traversing through the peaks of Dun Morogh. Falling snow and ice often spells the end of some more novice members' lives.\n\nAfter a slide, I usually try to find any sign of survivors or victims--while praying to the Light that there's nothing to be found. But with the elements acting up, I've held off wandering too far. If you could look for some lost mountaineers and bring me their rifles, I will return them to Ironforge.","Collect the rifles of fallen mountaineers.",5},
[99194]={nil,nil,5},
[99197]={nil,nil,2},
[99198]={nil,nil,3},
[99199]={nil,nil,5},
[99203]={"Ah, you've returned. Very good. Are you ready to learn to ride an armored galestrider?\n\nAs before, if you take the next step in your training with me, I will provide you with a free mount, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you would like. \n\nIt won't be cheap, but speak to me when you have enough coin. I will teach you about riding armored galestriders.","Learn the Journeyman Riding skill from Genn Fairweather.",0},
[99206]={"I'm glad you made your way back to me. I can tell by the scratches on your skin and the dirt on your armor that you've seen much of the world. It's time we got you a proper steed.\n\nKatie will provide you with a free mount once ye have completed the final leg of your training with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you would like just as before.\n\nSpeak to me when you have enough coin, and I will teach you all I know about riding armored horses.","Learn the Journeyman Riding skill from Randal Hunter.",0},
[99208]={"You are back. Good. It's time for you to learn to master the steed of a true Forsaken--the skeletal warhorse.\n\nZachariah will provide you with a free mount once you have completed the final round of your training with me, and after you will be able to purchase any additional mounts you desire.\n\nSpeak to me when you have enough coin, and I will teach you about skeletal warhorses.","Learn the Journeyman Riding skill from Velma Warnam.",0},
[99209]={"Yer back! Good, good. \n\nAre ye ready for a proper mountaineer's mount, $n?\n\nVeron will set ye up with a free armored ram once ye have finished the final leg of yer training with me, and afterwards you'll be able to purchase any additional mounts ye would like. \n\nSpeak ta me when you have enough coin, and I'll teach ye all I know about riding armored rams.","Learn the Journeyman Riding skill from Ultham Ironhorn.",0},
[99211]={"Greetings, $n. I didn't expect to see you back to my humble stables again so soon.\n\nYou certainly have had quite a journey. I think I can guess what has brought you here today.\n\nYou now have enough power, experience and skill to ride our deftest and most fearsome warhorses. These armored fiends will bear you through any trial, even past the gates of death itself. \n\nGo examine the armored undead warhorses and return to me when you have made your choice.","Inspect the armored undead riding warhorses to choose your epic mount.",0},
[99212]={"Salutations! I see today is a big day indeed; today you will synchronize your biometrics to the rider detection protocol of our fastest and fiercest mechanostriders! This protocol will help the strider distinguish you from other possible riders.\n\nIt clearly seems like you have enough strider experience to handle one of our very best.\n\nGo examine the upgraded mechanostriders and return to me when you have made your choice.","Inspect the upgraded riding mechanostriders to choose your epic mount.",3},
[99213]={"Greetings, $n! I am so glad to see you've returned to us.\n\nIt would seem you have enough experience to ride our fastest and fiercest steeds. You won't find a more steadfast companion for your journeys.\n\nChoosing one may be difficult as they are all excellent and trained to be steady even when in danger. Some may even recognize you from the last time you were here.\n\nGo and examine the armored horses and return to me when you have made your choice.","Inspect the armored riding horses to choose your epic mount.",0},
[99214]={"Greetings, friend! I am pleased to see you again. Today you have enough experience and aptitude to bond with our fastest and fiercest sabers.\n\nThese sabers are, of course, extremely intelligent and fiercely loyal to their bonded rider. You won't find a more noble and steadfast companion.\n\nAs such, you have an important choice to make. You and your saber will traverse the world together, so choose wisely!\n\nGo, examine the armored sabers and return to me when you have made your choice.","Inspect the armored riding sabers to choose your epic mount.",3},
[99216]={"Gales greetings, $n! I can't believe this day has come so soon. Today I am proud to say you have mastered galestrider riding, so I may now offer you our finest, fastest and boldest striders.\n\nLike before, you and your strider will traverse the world together, so you have an important choice to make. Many of these striders have grown in your time apart, but I would be willing to bet they still recognize you.\n\nGo examine the armored striders and return to me when you have made your choice.","Inspect the armored riding striders to choose your epic mount.",5},
[99217]={"Ah, I've been expecting you $n. It would seem the winds have brought you to me once again, so you may ride our fastest and strongest kodos.\n\nToday, I am proud to present to you your next kodo. Much like yourself, each has grown stronger and faster since you last met.\n\nYou and your kodo will travel the world together just like before, so find which one speaks to you.\n\nGo examine the armored kodos and return to me when you have made your choice.","Inspect the armored riding kodos to choose your epic mount.",0},
[99233]={"There must be more to the Maul than this!$B$BPerhaps the loud Spectator who oversees the event at Dire Maul will know!","Speak with Griniblix the Spectator above the Maul in Dire Maul.",1},
[99326]={"Greetings! Are you here to examine our horses?\n\nThese steeds are descendants from both the historical Lordaeron stock and our own local horses. You won't find a more steadfast companion for your journeys.\n\nChoosing one may be difficult as they are all excellent and trained to be steady even when in danger. Don't forget, you and your horse will traverse the world together. I'm sure whatever choice you make will suit you best.\n\nGo examine the horses and return to me when you have made your choice.","Inspect the riding horses to choose your first mount.",0},
[99411]={"Help, $n! My prized puppy, Kyle, has run away! I just know he's running around Bloodhoof Village, lost and hungry.$B$BWill you find him and feed him? Once he eats he will settle down and come home.$B$BTo feed him you will need to find food. His favorite meal is tender strider meat. Just venture east and you should find plenty of striders. Hunt one down and take its succulent meat to Kyle. When you see Kyle in town, put the meat down and he is sure to come to you.","Ahab Wheathoof at Bloodhoof Village in Mulgore wants you to feed his prized puppy, Kyle the Frenzied.$B$BFeed Kyle Tender Strider Meat and return to Ahab Wheathoof.",5},
}
FQB.QuestTextBuild = "wowf 1.60.1.70959"
